{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/pump.jolt'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.stream.ws.pump\n     2\t  \"Jolt-only owner-thread pump under the native WebSocket host adapter (J6d;\n     3\t   J6 plan rulings A1-A5). One instance per `create` call: its registry of\n     4\t   descriptors, write queues, close records and deadlines live in that\n     5\t   instance and nowhere else, so two instances never share state.\n     6\t\n     7\t   Ownership (A1). Every entry runs on the thread that drives the instance;\n     8\t   nothing here waits, parks or polls a socket. A driver polls the `interest`\n     9\t   descriptors until the earlier of its cadence and `next-deadline`\n    10\t   (`jolt.io-poller/clock-ms`, nil when nothing is due), then hands the\n    11\t   `[[fd revents] ...]` it observed to `pump!`, `[]` on a timeout: every\n    12\t   call runs the due expiries. A composition that never pumps an instance\n    13\t   makes no progress, by design.\n    14\t\n    15\t   Bounded turn (A1). One `pump!` visits each ready descriptor at most once,\n    16\t   starting after the one visited last in the previous turn (round robin in\n    17\t   registration order). A connection visit attempts at most one write of\n    18\t   the head of its queue and reads at most one chunk (one reused 64 KiB\n    19\t   native buffer); a listener visit accepts at most `accept-batch`.\n    20\t\n    21\t   One ordered write path (A3). Each connection owns one FIFO of whole wire\n    22\t   segments; the head carries an offset and is never rewritten. `send!`\n    23\t   writes at once only into an empty FIFO and queues the unsent tail;\n    24\t   otherwise it appends. Protocol output (pongs, close frames) joins the\n    25\t   same FIFO at generation time; nothing has priority. `send!` answers nil\n    26\t   or `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}`, never false.\n    27\t   `queued-bytes` counts every byte handed over and not yet accepted by the\n    28\t   kernel, control frames included; 0 after the terminal.\n    29\t\n    30\t   Two connection modes. A :raw connection (an HTTP upgrade in progress, or\n    31\t   a plain byte stream) delivers `:on-data` chunks, `:on-eof` once and\n    32\t   `:on-error` once. `upgraded!` turns it into a :ws connection, which parses\n    33\t   its input one frame at a time through the injected `:protocol`\n    34\t   (`{:parser :parse-frame :encode-frame :close-payload :mask-key}`; the\n    35\t   parse contract is `(parse-frame state chunk offset)` =>\n    36\t   `[event-or-nil state' offset']` with `:message`, `:ping`, `:pong`,\n    37\t   `:close` and `:fail` events, a close-frame failure carrying `:close?\n    38\t   true`), answers each ping with one pong, delivers `:on-message`, and\n    39\t   reports exactly one `:on-closed` terminal.\n    40\t\n    41\t   Control budget (A4). At most `max-pongs` pending pongs per connection plus\n    42\t   one reserved close slot. When the pongs fill the budget the connection\n    43\t   stops parsing after that frame, leaves read interest and keeps the\n    44\t   unparsed rest of its chunk; when a drain frees a pong slot the rest is\n    45\t   parsed before any new read, and read interest returns once it is\n    46\t   consumed. The close slot never counts against the budget and is never\n    47\t   refused.\n    48\t\n    49\t   Close record (A5). `{:local nil|:queued|:sent, :peer nil|:received,\n    50\t   :peer-status nil|:absent|:invalid|code, :code, :reason, :initiator,\n    51\t   :deadline}`. The first of a local `close!` and the peer's close frame\n    52\t   starts the 5 s `close-deadline`; the first local request wins. The\n    53\t   terminal code: a completed handshake reports the local code when this\n    54\t   side initiated, else the peer's status (an empty close reports 1005, an\n    55\t   invalid one 1002); a peer close followed by end of stream before the\n    56\t   response left reports the peer's status; end of stream, reset or a\n    57\t   transfer failure without a peer close reports 1006; deadline expiry in\n    58\t   any state reports 1006. A parser `:fail` without `:close?` fails the\n    59\t   connection (RFC 6455 section 7.1.7) and opens no handshake: the record\n    60\t   gets `:failed? true`, the close frame takes the reserved slot, input is\n    61\t   read only to see end of stream and discarded, and once the frame is\n    62\t   written the terminal is the local code with cause `:fail`; the peer's\n    63\t   reply is never parsed. A `:fail` after a local `close!` keeps that\n    64\t   request's frame and code and ends the same way. 1005 and 1006 are never\n    65\t   put on the wire. A ping that arrives once a local close is queued gets no\n    66\t   pong: the pong would queue behind our close frame, RFC 6455 section 5.5.1\n    67\t   forbids only data frames after a close, and no Autobahn case exercises\n    68\t   it.\n    69\t\n    70\t   Listeners. Accepted sockets register with `:listener` and `:upgrading?`;\n    71\t   at `max-pending-upgrades` upgrading sockets (or `:max-connections` owned\n    72\t   ones) the listener leaves the interest set until a slot frees. An\n    73\t   upgrade not completed within its timeout is released and reported to\n    74\t   `:on-upgrade-expired`. `close-listener!` closes the listener descriptor;\n    75\t   `drained?` answers true once no connection it owns is left, and its\n    76\t   `:on-drained` is called once then. `lower-deadlines!` brings the close\n    77\t   deadline of every connection a listener owns to at most a given time.\n    78\t\n    79\t   Callbacks. Data callbacks (`:on-data`, `:on-message`) run inside the\n    80\t   visit. Terminals and other lifecycle reports run at the start or end of\n    81\t   a turn, never inside an entry the composition called; `next-deadline`\n    82\t   answers now while one is owed.\n    83\t\n    84\t   Native memory: the read and write buffers exist while the registry is\n    85\t   non-empty and are freed when its last descriptor leaves.\"\n    86\t  (:require\n    87\t    [dao.stream.ws.tcp :as tcp]\n    88\t    [jolt.ffi :as ffi]\n    89\t    [jolt.io-poller :as poller]\n    90\t    [jolt.socket.native :as native]))\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\t(def chunk-bytes\n    94\t  \"The read chunk and the largest single write attempt.\"\n    95\t  (* 64 1024))\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\t(def accept-batch\n    99\t  \"The most connections one listener visit accepts.\"\n   100\t  16)\n   101\t\n   102\t\n   103\t(def max-pongs\n   104\t  \"Pending pongs per connection before its input pauses (A4).\"\n   105\t  16)\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\t(def close-deadline-ms\n   109\t  \"From the first close event to forced teardown (A5).\"\n   110\t  5000)\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\t(def max-pending-upgrades\n   114\t  \"Default per-listener cap on accepted, not yet upgraded sockets (A4).\"\n   115\t  64)\n   116\t\n   117\t\n   118\t(def upgrade-timeout-ms\n   119\t  \"Default deadline for an upgrade, from accept or connect (A4).\"\n   120\t  10000)\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\t(def closed-outcome {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed})\n   124\t\n   125\t\n   126\t(def ^:private no-close\n   127\t  {:local nil, :peer nil, :peer-status nil, :code nil, :reason nil, :initiator nil,\n   128\t   :deadline nil})\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\t;; =============================================================================\n   132\t;; Instance\n   133\t;; =============================================================================\n   134\t\n   135\t(defn create\n   136\t  \"A fresh pump instance with an empty registry.\"\n   137\t  []\n   138\t  {::state (atom {:handles {}           ; fd -> handle, registered only\n   139\t                  :last-id -1           ; id of the handle visited last\n   140\t                  :next-id 0\n   141\t                  :notify []            ; thunks owed (terminals, lifecycle reports)\n   142\t                  :closed-listeners {}  ; id -> handle, closed and not yet reported drained\n   143\t                  :rbuf nil\n   144\t                  :wbuf nil})})\n   145\t\n   146\t\n   147\t(defn- st\n   148\t  [p]\n   149\t  (::state p))\n   150\t\n   151\t\n   152\t(defn- cell\n   153\t  [h]\n   154\t  @(::cell h))\n   155\t\n   156\t\n   157\t(defn- cell!\n   158\t  [h f & args]\n   159\t  (apply swap! (::cell h) f args))\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t(defn- alloc-buffer\n   163\t  []\n   164\t  (let [b (ffi/alloc chunk-bytes)]\n   165\t    (when (ffi/null? b)\n   166\t      (throw (ex-info \"dao.stream.ws.pump native allocation failed\" {:bytes chunk-bytes})))\n   167\t    b))\n   168\t\n   169\t\n   170\t(defn- maybe-release!\n   171\t  \"Free the native buffers once the registry is empty.\"\n   172\t  [p]\n   173\t  (let [s (st p)\n   174\t        {:keys [handles rbuf wbuf]} @s]\n   175\t    (when (and rbuf (empty? handles))\n   176\t      (swap! s assoc :rbuf nil :wbuf nil)\n   177\t      (ffi/free rbuf)\n   178\t      (ffi/free wbuf))))\n   179\t\n   180\t\n   181\t(defn- owe!\n   182\t  \"Queue thunk `f` for the start or end of a turn.\"\n   183\t  [p f]\n   184\t  (swap! (st p) update :notify conj f)\n   185\t  nil)\n   186\t\n   187\t\n   188\t(defn- register!\n   189\t  [p fd fields]\n   190\t  (let [s (st p)]\n   191\t    (when-not (:rbuf @s)\n   192\t      (swap! s assoc :rbuf (alloc-buffer) :wbuf (alloc-buffer)))\n   193\t    (let [h {:id (:next-id @s), :fd fd, ::cell (atom fields)}]\n   194\t      (swap! s #(-> % (assoc-in [:handles fd] h) (update :next-id inc)))\n   195\t      h)))\n   196\t\n   197\t\n   198\t(defn- registered?\n   199\t  [p h]\n   200\t  (identical? h (get-in @(st p) [:handles (:fd h)])))\n   201\t\n   202\t\n   203\t(defn open?\n   204\t  [h]\n   205\t  (= :open (:status (cell h))))\n   206\t\n   207\t\n   208\t(defn- owned\n   209\t  \"The registered connections listener `lh` owns.\"\n   210\t  [p lh]\n   211\t  (filter #(= (:id lh) (:owner (cell %))) (vals (:handles @(st p)))))\n   212\t\n   213\t\n   214\t;; =============================================================================\n   215\t;; Registration\n   216\t;; =============================================================================\n   217\t\n   218\t(defn listener!\n   219\t  \"Register listener `fd` (nonblocking, listening). Options: `:on-accept`\n   220\t   (each `{:fd :peer}`, inside the visit; the callee registers it with\n   221\t   `connection!` passing `:listener` and `:upgrading? true`, or closes it;\n   222\t   without one, accepted descriptors are closed), `:on-accept-error`,\n   223\t   `:on-drained`, `:max-pending-upgrades` (default 64), `:max-connections`\n   224\t   (default nil, unbounded), `:upgrade-timeout-ms` (default 10 s). Answers\n   225\t   the handle.\"\n   226\t  [p fd opts]\n   227\t  (register! p fd (merge {:max-pending-upgrades max-pending-upgrades\n   228\t                          :upgrade-timeout-ms upgrade-timeout-ms}\n   229\t                         (select-keys opts [:on-accept :on-accept-error :on-drained\n   230\t                                            :max-pending-upgrades :max-connections\n   231\t                                            :upgrade-timeout-ms])\n   232\t                         {:kind :listener, :status :open, :accepting? true})))\n   233\t\n   234\t\n   235\t(defn connection!\n   236\t  \"Register connection `fd` (nonblocking) in :raw mode. `:connecting? true`\n   237\t   marks a dial in progress: its first ready turn reads SO_ERROR and calls\n   238\t   `:on-connected` or reports `:on-error`. `:listener` names the owning\n   239\t   listener; `:upgrading? true` starts the upgrade deadline (the listener's\n   240\t   or `:upgrade-timeout-ms`) and counts against the listener's pending\n   241\t   cap. `:close-deadline-ms` overrides the 5 s close deadline. Callbacks: `:on-data`, `:on-eof`, `:on-error`, `:on-drained`,\n   242\t   `:on-upgrade-expired`, and for :ws mode `:on-message`, `:on-closed`.\n   243\t   Answers the handle.\"\n   244\t  [p fd {:keys [connecting? listener upgrading?] :as opts}]\n   245\t  (let [timeout (or (:upgrade-timeout-ms opts)\n   246\t                    (when listener (:upgrade-timeout-ms (cell listener)))\n   247\t                    upgrade-timeout-ms)]\n   248\t    (register! p fd (merge (select-keys opts [:on-connected :on-data :on-eof :on-error\n   249\t                                              :on-drained :on-upgrade-expired\n   250\t                                              :on-message :on-closed])\n   251\t                           {:kind (if connecting? :connecting :connection)\n   252\t                            :mode :raw\n   253\t                            :status :open, :pending [], :queued 0, :reading? true\n   254\t                            :owner (:id listener)\n   255\t                            :upgrading? (boolean upgrading?)\n   256\t                            :upgrade-deadline (when upgrading? (+ (poller/clock-ms) timeout))\n   257\t                            :pongs 0, :remainder nil\n   258\t                            :close-deadline-ms (or (:close-deadline-ms opts) close-deadline-ms)\n   259\t                            :close no-close}))))\n   260\t\n   261\t\n   262\t(defn upgraded!\n   263\t  \"Turn :raw connection `h` into a :ws connection parsing through\n   264\t   `protocol` (`{:parser :parse-frame :encode-frame :close-payload\n   265\t   :mask-key}`); `leftover` (bytes after the upgrade head, or nil) is parsed\n   266\t   before any new read. Frees its pending-upgrade slot.\"\n   267\t  [_p h protocol leftover]\n   268\t  (cell! h assoc\n   269\t         :mode :ws, :protocol protocol, :parser (:parser protocol)\n   270\t         :upgrading? false, :upgrade-deadline nil\n   271\t         :remainder (when (and leftover (pos? (alength leftover)))\n   272\t                      {:chunk leftover, :offset 0}))\n   273\t  nil)\n   274\t\n   275\t\n   276\t(defn set-accepting!\n   277\t  \"Pause (false) or resume (true) accepting on listener `h`.\"\n   278\t  [_p h accepting?]\n   279\t  (cell! h assoc :accepting? (boolean accepting?))\n   280\t  nil)\n   281\t\n   282\t\n   283\t(defn set-reading!\n   284\t  \"Stop (false) or resume (true) reading connection `h`.\"\n   285\t  [_p h reading?]\n   286\t  (cell! h assoc :reading? (boolean reading?))\n   287\t  nil)\n   288\t\n   289\t\n   290\t(defn set-deadline!\n   291\t  \"Call `(f)` once on the first turn at or after monotonic `at-ms`\n   292\t   (`jolt.io-poller/clock-ms`). Replaces any earlier such deadline of `h`.\"\n   293\t  [_p h at-ms f]\n   294\t  (cell! h assoc :deadline at-ms :on-deadline f)\n   295\t  nil)\n   296\t\n   297\t\n   298\t(defn clear-deadline!\n   299\t  [_p h]\n   300\t  (cell! h dissoc :deadline :on-deadline)\n   301\t  nil)\n   302\t\n   303\t\n   304\t(defn queued-bytes\n   305\t  \"Bytes handed to `h` and not yet accepted by the kernel: exact, 0 after\n   306\t   the terminal.\"\n   307\t  [h]\n   308\t  (:queued (cell h) 0))\n   309\t\n   310\t\n   311\t(defn pending-tags\n   312\t  \"The tags of `h`'s pending segments in FIFO order (:pong, :close, or nil\n   313\t   for data), with the head's offset: `[[tag offset len] ...]`.\"\n   314\t  [h]\n   315\t  (mapv (fn [{:keys [tag off bytes]}] [tag off (alength bytes)]) (:pending (cell h))))\n   316\t\n   317\t\n   318\t(defn close-record\n   319\t  [h]\n   320\t  (:close (cell h)))\n   321\t\n   322\t\n   323\t(defn read-interest?\n   324\t  \"Whether `h` is asking to be read.\"\n   325\t  [h]\n   326\t  (let [{:keys [reading? pongs remainder]} (cell h)]\n   327\t    (boolean (and reading? (< pongs max-pongs) (nil? remainder)))))\n   328\t\n   329\t\n   330\t;; =============================================================================\n   331\t;; Release and terminals\n   332\t;; =============================================================================\n   333\t\n   334\t(defn- release!\n   335\t  \"Close `h`'s descriptor and drop it from the registry with `status`; true\n   336\t   when it was open.\"\n   337\t  [p h status]\n   338\t  (when (open? h)\n   339\t    (cell! h assoc :status status :pending [] :queued 0 :remainder nil)\n   340\t    (when (registered? p h)\n   341\t      (swap! (st p) update :handles dissoc (:fd h)))\n   342\t    (tcp/shutdown! (:fd h) :both)\n   343\t    (tcp/close! (:fd h))\n   344\t    true))\n   345\t\n   346\t\n   347\t(defn discard!\n   348\t  \"Release `h` now: descriptor closed, queue dropped, `queued-bytes` 0, no\n   349\t   callback. Idempotent.\"\n   350\t  [p h]\n   351\t  (release! p h :closed)\n   352\t  (maybe-release! p)\n   353\t  nil)\n   354\t\n   355\t\n   356\t(defn- status-code\n   357\t  [peer-status]\n   358\t  (case peer-status :absent 1005 :invalid 1002 peer-status))\n   359\t\n   360\t\n   361\t(defn- terminal\n   362\t  \"The terminal `{:code :reason}` for close record `c` and `cause`.\"\n   363\t  [c cause]\n   364\t  (let [{:keys [initiator peer peer-status code reason peer-reason]} c]\n   365\t    (case cause\n   366\t      :handshake (if (= :local initiator)\n   367\t                   {:code code, :reason (or reason \"\")}\n   368\t                   {:code (status-code peer-status), :reason (or peer-reason \"\")})\n   369\t      :fail {:code code, :reason (or reason \"\")}\n   370\t      (:eof :reset :transfer) (if (= :received peer)\n   371\t                                {:code (status-code peer-status), :reason (or peer-reason \"\")}\n   372\t                                {:code 1006, :reason \"\"})\n   373\t      {:code 1006, :reason \"\"})))\n   374\t\n   375\t\n   376\t(defn- terminate!\n   377\t  \"End :ws connection `h` once with `cause` (:handshake, :eof, :reset,\n   378\t   :transfer, :deadline): descriptor shut, queue released, one owed\n   379\t   `:on-closed`.\"\n   380\t  [p h cause detail]\n   381\t  (let [c (:close (cell h))]\n   382\t    (when (release! p h :closed)\n   383\t      (let [t (assoc (terminal c cause) :cause cause)\n   384\t            t (if detail (assoc t :detail detail) t)]\n   385\t        (when-let [f (:on-closed (cell h))]\n   386\t          (owe! p #(f t)))))))\n   387\t\n   388\t\n   389\t(defn- fail!\n   390\t  \"A transfer failure: a :ws connection terminates per A5, a :raw one owes\n   391\t   `:on-error` once with `failure`.\"\n   392\t  [p h failure]\n   393\t  (if (= :ws (:mode (cell h)))\n   394\t    (terminate! p h (if (= :reset (:class failure)) :reset :transfer) failure)\n   395\t    (when (release! p h :failed)\n   396\t      (when-let [f (:on-error (cell h))]\n   397\t        (owe! p #(f failure))))))\n   398\t\n   399\t\n   400\t;; =============================================================================\n   401\t;; Writes (A3)\n   402\t;; =============================================================================\n   403\t\n   404\t(defn- write-once!\n   405\t  \"One send of at most `chunk-bytes` of `bs` from `off`: the bytes the\n   406\t   kernel accepted (0 on EAGAIN), or a failure map.\"\n   407\t  [p fd bs off]\n   408\t  (let [wbuf (:wbuf @(st p))\n   409\t        n (min chunk-bytes (- (alength bs) off))]\n   410\t    (ffi/write-array wbuf bs off n)\n   411\t    (let [r (tcp/send-chunk! fd wbuf n)]\n   412\t      (cond\n   413\t        (= :would-block r) 0\n   414\t        (:error r) r\n   415\t        :else (:n r)))))\n   416\t\n   417\t\n   418\t(declare segment-done!)\n   419\t\n   420\t\n   421\t(defn- enqueue!\n   422\t  \"Hand whole segment `bs` tagged `tag` to `h`'s FIFO: one write attempt\n   423\t   when the FIFO is empty and the connection is established, else append.\n   424\t   Answers nil, or `closed-outcome` when the immediate write failed (nothing\n   425\t   sent).\"\n   426\t  [p h bs tag]\n   427\t  (let [{:keys [kind pending]} (cell h)\n   428\t        len (alength bs)\n   429\t        seg {:bytes bs, :off 0, :tag tag}]\n   430\t    (if (or (seq pending) (not= :connection kind))\n   431\t      (do (cell! h #(-> % (update :pending conj seg) (update :queued + len)))\n   432\t          nil)\n   433\t      (let [r (write-once! p (:fd h) bs 0)]\n   434\t        (cond\n   435\t          (map? r) (do (fail! p h r) closed-outcome)\n   436\t          (= r len) (do (segment-done! p h tag) nil)\n   437\t          :else (do (cell! h #(-> % (update :pending conj (assoc seg :off r))\n   438\t                                  (update :queued + (- len r))))\n   439\t                    nil))))))\n   440\t\n   441\t\n   442\t(defn send!\n   443\t  \"Hand whole segment `bs` (a byte array the caller no longer mutates) to\n   444\t   connection `h`. Answers nil (accepted: on the wire or queued) or\n   445\t   `closed-outcome` (failed, closed or closing: nothing sent). A :ws\n   446\t   connection refuses data once either side's close exists, so no data\n   447\t   frame follows our close frame (RFC 6455 section 5.5.1).\"\n   448\t  [p h bs]\n   449\t  (let [{:keys [status mode close]} (cell h)]\n   450\t    (cond\n   451\t      (not= :open status) closed-outcome\n   452\t      (and (= :ws mode) (or (:local close) (:peer close))) closed-outcome\n   453\t      (zero? (alength bs)) nil\n   454\t      :else (let [r (enqueue! p h bs nil)]\n   455\t              (maybe-release! p)\n   456\t              r))))\n   457\t\n   458\t\n   459\t(defn- drain-once!\n   460\t  \"One write of the head segment; answers whether bytes moved.\"\n   461\t  [p h]\n   462\t  (let [{:keys [bytes off tag]} (first (:pending (cell h)))\n   463\t        r (write-once! p (:fd h) bytes off)]\n   464\t    (cond\n   465\t      (map? r) (do (fail! p h r) true)\n   466\t      (zero? r) false\n   467\t      :else (let [off' (+ off r)\n   468\t                  done? (= off' (alength bytes))]\n   469\t              (cell! h #(-> %\n   470\t                            (update :queued - r)\n   471\t                            (update :pending (fn [q]\n   472\t                                               (if done?\n   473\t                                                 (subvec q 1)\n   474\t                                                 (assoc-in q [0 :off] off'))))))\n   475\t              (when done? (segment-done! p h tag))\n   476\t              true))))\n   477\t\n   478\t\n   479\t;; =============================================================================\n   480\t;; Close (A5) and control output (A4)\n   481\t;; =============================================================================\n   482\t\n   483\t(defn- frame\n   484\t  \"The wire bytes of a control frame through `h`'s protocol.\"\n   485\t  [h opcode payload]\n   486\t  (let [{:keys [encode-frame mask-key]} (:protocol (cell h))]\n   487\t    (encode-frame (cond-> {:opcode opcode, :payload payload}\n   488\t                    mask-key (assoc :mask-key (mask-key))))))\n   489\t\n   490\t\n   491\t(defn close-frame\n   492\t  \"The wire bytes of a close frame with `code` and `reason` through `h`'s\n   493\t   protocol; a nil `code` is the empty close. 1005 and 1006 are refused:\n   494\t   they are reports, never wire codes (RFC 6455 section 7.4.1).\"\n   495\t  [h code reason]\n   496\t  (when (#{1005 1006} code)\n   497\t    (throw (ex-info \"close code 1005/1006 is never serialized\" {:code code})))\n   498\t  (frame h :close ((:close-payload (:protocol (cell h))) code reason)))\n   499\t\n   500\t\n   501\t(defn- start-close\n   502\t  \"Close record `c` after its first close event: initiator and deadline\n   503\t   (`ms` from now, kept if an earlier one was lowered in).\"\n   504\t  [c initiator ms]\n   505\t  (if (or (:local c) (:peer c))\n   506\t    c\n   507\t    (let [d (+ (poller/clock-ms) ms)]\n   508\t      (assoc c :initiator initiator :deadline (if (:deadline c) (min d (:deadline c)) d)))))\n   509\t\n   510\t\n   511\t(defn close!\n   512\t  \"Request the close handshake on :ws connection `h` with `code` and\n   513\t   `reason`. The first request wins: a later one, or one after the peer's\n   514\t   close was answered, changes nothing. The close frame takes the reserved\n   515\t   control slot behind everything already queued.\"\n   516\t  [p h code reason]\n   517\t  (let [{:keys [status mode close]} (cell h)]\n   518\t    (when (and (= :open status) (= :ws mode) (nil? (:local close)))\n   519\t      (let [bs (close-frame h code reason)]\n   520\t        (cell! h update :close #(-> (start-close % :local (:close-deadline-ms (cell h)))\n   521\t                                    (assoc :local :queued :code code :reason reason)))\n   522\t        (enqueue! p h bs :close)\n   523\t        (maybe-release! p))))\n   524\t  nil)\n   525\t\n   526\t\n   527\t(defn- segment-done!\n   528\t  [p h tag]\n   529\t  (case tag\n   530\t    :pong (cell! h update :pongs dec)\n   531\t    :close (do (cell! h assoc-in [:close :local] :sent)\n   532\t               (cond\n   533\t                 (:failed? (:close (cell h))) (terminate! p h :fail nil)\n   534\t                 (= :received (:peer (:close (cell h)))) (terminate! p h :handshake nil)))\n   535\t    nil)\n   536\t  (when (and (open? h) (empty? (:pending (cell h))))\n   537\t    (when-let [f (:on-drained (cell h))] (owe! p f))))\n   538\t\n   539\t\n   540\t(defn- fail-connection!\n   541\t  \"A parser :fail without :close? fails the connection (RFC 6455 section\n   542\t   7.1.7): the close frame takes the reserved slot, later input is\n   543\t   discarded unparsed (read only to see EOF or reset) and the unparsed rest\n   544\t   is dropped. The peer's reply is never parsed: the terminal is `:fail`\n   545\t   with the local code once the frame is written. After a local `close!`\n   546\t   the requested frame keeps the slot (no second frame) and its code: still\n   547\t   queued, the connection fails once it is written; already sent, it fails\n   548\t   now.\"\n   549\t  [p h code reason]\n   550\t  (let [{:keys [status mode close]} (cell h)]\n   551\t    (when (and (= :open status) (= :ws mode) (nil? (:peer close)))\n   552\t      (case (:local close)\n   553\t        nil (let [bs (close-frame h code reason)]\n   554\t              (cell! h #(-> %\n   555\t                            (assoc :remainder nil)\n   556\t                            (update :close (fn [c]\n   557\t                                             (-> (start-close c :local (:close-deadline-ms %))\n   558\t                                                 (assoc :local :queued :code code :reason reason\n   559\t                                                        :failed? true))))))\n   560\t              (enqueue! p h bs :close)\n   561\t              (maybe-release! p))\n   562\t        :queued (cell! h #(-> %\n   563\t                              (assoc :remainder nil)\n   564\t                              (assoc-in [:close :failed?] true)))\n   565\t        :sent (do (cell! h assoc-in [:close :failed?] true)\n   566\t                  (terminate! p h :fail nil)\n   567\t                  (maybe-release! p)))))\n   568\t  nil)\n   569\t\n   570\t\n   571\t(defn- peer-close!\n   572\t  \"The peer's close frame: record it, start the deadline if first, and\n   573\t   answer it unless this side's close is already queued or sent.\"\n   574\t  [p h status code reason]\n   575\t  (cell! h update :close #(-> (start-close % :peer (:close-deadline-ms (cell h)))\n   576\t                              (assoc :peer :received :peer-status status :peer-reason reason)))\n   577\t  (let [{:keys [local]} (:close (cell h))]\n   578\t    (cond\n   579\t      (= :sent local) (terminate! p h :handshake nil)\n   580\t      (= :queued local) nil\n   581\t      :else (let [[rcode rreason] (case status\n   582\t                                    :absent [nil nil]\n   583\t                                    :invalid [1002 \"dao.stream/protocol-error\"]\n   584\t                                    [code nil])]\n   585\t              (cell! h update :close assoc :local :queued :code rcode :reason rreason)\n   586\t              (enqueue! p h (close-frame h rcode rreason) :close)))))\n   587\t\n   588\t\n   589\t(defn- pong!\n   590\t  [p h payload]\n   591\t  (cell! h update :pongs inc)\n   592\t  (enqueue! p h (frame h :pong payload) :pong))\n   593\t\n   594\t\n   595\t(defn- handle-event!\n   596\t  [p h ev]\n   597\t  (let [{:keys [local peer]} (:close (cell h))]\n   598\t    (case (:type ev)\n   599\t      :ping (when (nil? local) (pong! p h (:payload ev)))\n   600\t      :pong nil\n   601\t      :message (when (and (nil? local) (nil? peer))\n   602\t                 (when-let [f (:on-message (cell h))] (f ev)))\n   603\t      :close (when (nil? peer)\n   604\t               (peer-close! p h (if (nil? (:code ev)) :absent (:code ev)) (:code ev) (:reason ev)))\n   605\t      :fail (if (:close? ev)\n   606\t              (when (nil? peer) (peer-close! p h :invalid nil nil))\n   607\t              (fail-connection! p h (:code ev) (:reason ev)))\n   608\t      nil)))\n   609\t\n   610\t\n   611\t(defn- parse-input!\n   612\t  \"Parse `chunk` from `offset` one frame at a time until it is consumed,\n   613\t   the connection ends, or the pong budget fills; keep the unparsed rest.\"\n   614\t  [p h chunk offset]\n   615\t  (let [parse (:parse-frame (:protocol (cell h)))\n   616\t        n (alength chunk)]\n   617\t    (loop [off offset]\n   618\t      (cond\n   619\t        (not (open? h)) nil\n   620\t        (>= off n) (cell! h assoc :remainder nil)\n   621\t        (>= (:pongs (cell h)) max-pongs) (cell! h assoc :remainder {:chunk chunk, :offset off})\n   622\t        :else (let [[ev parser' off'] (parse (:parser (cell h)) chunk off)]\n   623\t                (cell! h assoc :parser parser')\n   624\t                (if (nil? ev)\n   625\t                  (cell! h assoc :remainder nil)\n   626\t                  (do (handle-event! p h ev)\n   627\t                      (recur off'))))))))\n   628\t\n   629\t\n   630\t(defn- resume!\n   631\t  \"Parse a held remainder once the pong budget has room; answers whether\n   632\t   anything was parsed.\"\n   633\t  [p h]\n   634\t  (when (and (open? h) (< (:pongs (cell h)) max-pongs))\n   635\t    (when-let [{:keys [chunk offset]} (:remainder (cell h))]\n   636\t      (parse-input! p h chunk offset)\n   637\t      true)))\n   638\t\n   639\t\n   640\t;; =============================================================================\n   641\t;; Reads and visits (A1)\n   642\t;; =============================================================================\n   643\t\n   644\t(defn- read-once!\n   645\t  \"One recv chunk into the reused buffer; answers whether anything\n   646\t   happened.\"\n   647\t  [p h]\n   648\t  (let [rbuf (:rbuf @(st p))\n   649\t        r (tcp/recv-chunk! (:fd h) rbuf chunk-bytes)\n   650\t        ws? (= :ws (:mode (cell h)))]\n   651\t    (cond\n   652\t      (= :would-block r) false\n   653\t      (= :eof r) (do (if ws?\n   654\t                       (terminate! p h :eof nil)\n   655\t                       (do (cell! h assoc :reading? false :eof? true)\n   656\t                           (when-let [f (:on-eof (cell h))] (owe! p f))))\n   657\t                     true)\n   658\t      (:error r) (do (fail! p h r) true)\n   659\t      :else (let [chunk (ffi/read-array rbuf (:n r))]\n   660\t              (if ws?\n   661\t                ;; a failed connection reads only to see EOF or reset: the\n   662\t                ;; input is discarded, never parsed\n   663\t                (when-not (:failed? (:close (cell h))) (parse-input! p h chunk 0))\n   664\t                (when-let [f (:on-data (cell h))] (f chunk)))\n   665\t              true))))\n   666\t\n   667\t\n   668\t(def ^:private write-ready (bit-or native/pollout native/pollerr native/pollhup native/pollnval))\n   669\t\n   670\t\n   671\t(defn- visit-connection!\n   672\t  [p h rev]\n   673\t  (let [wrote? (when (and (pos? (bit-and rev write-ready)) (seq (:pending (cell h))))\n   674\t                 (drain-once! p h))\n   675\t        ;; resume before read: a held remainder is parsed first, and read\n   676\t        ;; interest returns only once it is consumed\n   677\t        resumed? (resume! p h)\n   678\t        read? (when (and (not resumed?) (open? h) (read-interest? h)\n   679\t                         (pos? (bit-and rev native/poll-readable)))\n   680\t                (read-once! p h))]\n   681\t    (boolean (or wrote? resumed? read?))))\n   682\t\n   683\t\n   684\t(defn- visit-connecting!\n   685\t  [p h rev]\n   686\t  (when (pos? rev)\n   687\t    (let [r (tcp/connect-result (:fd h))]\n   688\t      (if (map? r)\n   689\t        (fail! p h r)\n   690\t        (do (cell! h assoc :kind :connection)\n   691\t            (when-let [f (:on-connected (cell h))] (owe! p f)))))\n   692\t    true))\n   693\t\n   694\t\n   695\t(defn- can-accept?\n   696\t  [p lh]\n   697\t  (let [{:keys [status accepting? max-pending-upgrades max-connections]} (cell lh)\n   698\t        mine (owned p lh)]\n   699\t    (and (= :open status) accepting?\n   700\t         (< (count (filter #(:upgrading? (cell %)) mine)) max-pending-upgrades)\n   701\t         (or (nil? max-connections) (< (count mine) max-connections)))))\n   702\t\n   703\t\n   704\t(defn- visit-listener!\n   705\t  [p h]\n   706\t  (loop [i 0, moved? false]\n   707\t    (if (or (= i accept-batch) (not (can-accept? p h)))\n   708\t      moved?\n   709\t      (let [r (tcp/accept! (:fd h))]\n   710\t        (cond\n   711\t          (= :would-block r) moved?\n   712\t          (:error r) (do (when-let [f (:on-accept-error (cell h))] (owe! p #(f r))) true)\n   713\t          ;; :on-accept runs inside the visit: the callee's registration is\n   714\t          ;; what the pending-upgrade cap counts. Without one, nobody owns\n   715\t          ;; the descriptor, so it is closed rather than leaked.\n   716\t          :else (do (if-let [f (:on-accept (cell h))]\n   717\t                      (f r)\n   718\t                      (tcp/close! (:fd r)))\n   719\t                    (recur (inc i) true)))))))\n   720\t\n   721\t\n   722\t(defn interest\n   723\t  \"`[[fd events] ...]` for this instance's next poll, registration order.\"\n   724\t  [p]\n   725\t  (vec (keep (fn [h]\n   726\t               (let [{:keys [kind pending]} (cell h)\n   727\t                     ev (case kind\n   728\t                          :listener (if (can-accept? p h) native/pollin 0)\n   729\t                          :connecting native/pollout\n   730\t                          :connection (bit-or (if (read-interest? h) native/pollin 0)\n   731\t                                              (if (seq pending) native/pollout 0)))]\n   732\t                 (when (pos? ev) [(:fd h) ev])))\n   733\t             (sort-by :id (vals (:handles @(st p)))))))\n   734\t\n   735\t\n   736\t(defn- runnable-remainder?\n   737\t  [h]\n   738\t  (let [{:keys [remainder pongs]} (cell h)]\n   739\t    (and remainder (< pongs max-pongs))))\n   740\t\n   741\t\n   742\t(defn next-deadline\n   743\t  \"The nearest due time on `jolt.io-poller/clock-ms`: now while a report is\n   744\t   owed or a held remainder can be parsed; else the nearest upgrade, close\n   745\t   or registered deadline; nil when nothing is due (an empty registry).\"\n   746\t  [p]\n   747\t  (let [{:keys [handles notify closed-listeners]} @(st p)\n   748\t        hs (vals handles)\n   749\t        ;; a closed listener is due only once its drain report is owed: while\n   750\t        ;; it still owns connections, their own deadlines bound the wait\n   751\t        drained (some (fn [[_ lh]] (empty? (owned p lh))) closed-listeners)]\n   752\t    (if (or (seq notify) drained (some runnable-remainder? hs))\n   753\t      (poller/clock-ms)\n   754\t      (let [ds (mapcat (fn [h]\n   755\t                         (let [c (cell h)]\n   756\t                           (keep identity [(:deadline c) (:upgrade-deadline c)\n   757\t                                           (:deadline (:close c))])))\n   758\t                       hs)]\n   759\t        (when (seq ds) (reduce min ds))))))\n   760\t\n   761\t\n   762\t(defn- deliver-notify!\n   763\t  [p]\n   764\t  (let [owed (:notify @(st p))]\n   765\t    (swap! (st p) assoc :notify [])\n   766\t    (doseq [f owed] (f))\n   767\t    (boolean (seq owed))))\n   768\t\n   769\t\n   770\t(defn- expire!\n   771\t  \"Run every due deadline; answers whether any fired.\"\n   772\t  [p]\n   773\t  (let [now (poller/clock-ms)\n   774\t        due? #(and % (<= % now))\n   775\t        fired (atom false)]\n   776\t    (doseq [h (sort-by :id (vals (:handles @(st p))))]\n   777\t      (let [c (cell h)]\n   778\t        (cond\n   779\t          (not (registered? p h)) nil\n   780\t          (due? (:upgrade-deadline c))\n   781\t          (do (reset! fired true)\n   782\t              (release! p h :closed)\n   783\t              (when-let [f (:on-upgrade-expired c)] (owe! p f)))\n   784\t          (due? (:deadline (:close c)))\n   785\t          (do (reset! fired true)\n   786\t              (cond\n   787\t                (= :ws (:mode c)) (terminate! p h :deadline nil)\n   788\t                (:upgrading? c) (do (release! p h :closed)\n   789\t                                    (when-let [f (:on-upgrade-expired c)] (owe! p f)))\n   790\t                ;; a plain :raw stream has no upgrade to expire: its lowered\n   791\t                ;; deadline ends it as a failure\n   792\t                :else (fail! p h {:error :close-deadline, :class :other})))\n   793\t          (due? (:deadline c))\n   794\t          (let [f (:on-deadline c)]\n   795\t            (reset! fired true)\n   796\t            (cell! h dissoc :deadline :on-deadline)\n   797\t            (when f (f))))))\n   798\t    @fired))\n   799\t\n   800\t\n   801\t(defn- report-drained!\n   802\t  [p]\n   803\t  (doseq [[id lh] (:closed-listeners @(st p))]\n   804\t    (when (empty? (owned p lh))\n   805\t      (swap! (st p) update :closed-listeners dissoc id)\n   806\t      (when-let [f (:on-drained (cell lh))] (owe! p f)))))\n   807\t\n   808\t\n   809\t(defn- rotation\n   810\t  \"The handles named in `ready`, in registration order starting after the\n   811\t   id visited last.\"\n   812\t  [p ready]\n   813\t  (let [{:keys [handles last-id]} @(st p)\n   814\t        revents (reduce (fn [m [fd rev]] (update m fd (fnil bit-or 0) rev)) {} ready)\n   815\t        hs (sort-by (comp :id first)\n   816\t                    (keep (fn [[fd rev]]\n   817\t                            (when-let [h (get handles fd)]\n   818\t                              (when (pos? rev) [h rev])))\n   819\t                          revents))\n   820\t        after? #(> (:id (first %)) last-id)]\n   821\t    (concat (filter after? hs) (remove after? hs))))\n   822\t\n   823\t\n   824\t(defn pump!\n   825\t  \"One bounded turn over `ready` (`[[fd revents] ...]` from the driver's\n   826\t   poll; `[]` after a timeout): owed reports, one visit per ready\n   827\t   descriptor, held remainders that can resume, due expiries, owed reports.\n   828\t   Answers `{:progressed? boolean}`.\"\n   829\t  [p ready]\n   830\t  (let [s (st p)]\n   831\t    (try\n   832\t      (let [notified? (deliver-notify! p)\n   833\t            turn (vec (rotation p ready))\n   834\t            visited (doall\n   835\t                      (for [[h rev] turn\n   836\t                            ;; a descriptor released earlier in this turn,\n   837\t                            ;; or its number reused, is not visited\n   838\t                            :when (registered? p h)]\n   839\t                        (let [moved? (case (:kind (cell h))\n   840\t                                       :listener (visit-listener! p h)\n   841\t                                       :connecting (visit-connecting! p h rev)\n   842\t                                       :connection (visit-connection! p h rev))]\n   843\t                          (swap! s assoc :last-id (:id h))\n   844\t                          moved?)))\n   845\t            seen (set (map (comp :id first) turn))\n   846\t            resumed (doall\n   847\t                      (for [h (sort-by :id (vals (:handles @s)))\n   848\t                            :when (and (not (seen (:id h))) (runnable-remainder? h))]\n   849\t                        (resume! p h)))\n   850\t            fired? (expire! p)\n   851\t            _ (report-drained! p)\n   852\t            late? (deliver-notify! p)]\n   853\t        {:progressed? (boolean (or notified? (some true? visited) (some true? resumed)\n   854\t                                   fired? late?))})\n   855\t      (finally\n   856\t        (maybe-release! p)))))\n   857\t\n   858\t\n   859\t;; =============================================================================\n   860\t;; Listener lifecycle (A6 seam)\n   861\t;; =============================================================================\n   862\t\n   863\t(defn close-listener!\n   864\t  \"Close listener `lh`'s descriptor (no more accepts). Connections it owns\n   865\t   stay; `drained?` turns true once none is left, and `:on-drained` is owed\n   866\t   once then.\"\n   867\t  [p lh]\n   868\t  (when (release! p lh :closed)\n   869\t    (swap! (st p) assoc-in [:closed-listeners (:id lh)] lh))\n   870\t  (maybe-release! p)\n   871\t  nil)\n   872\t\n   873\t\n   874\t(defn drained?\n   875\t  \"True when listener `lh`'s descriptor is closed and no connection it owns\n   876\t   is left.\"\n   877\t  [p lh]\n   878\t  (and (not (open? lh)) (empty? (owned p lh))))\n   879\t\n   880\t\n   881\t(defn lower-deadlines!\n   882\t  \"Bring the close deadline of every connection listener `lh` owns to at\n   883\t   most monotonic `at-ms`, setting one where none exists. Expiry is the\n   884\t   A5 deadline: shut, 1006.\"\n   885\t  [p lh at-ms]\n   886\t  (doseq [h (owned p lh)]\n   887\t    (cell! h update-in [:close :deadline] #(if % (min % at-ms) at-ms)))\n   888\t  nil)\n   889\t\n   890\t\n   891\t(defn host-pump\n   892\t  \"The instance as the driver's `:pump` value (A2): `:interest`,\n   893\t   `:deadline` (clock-ms or nil) and `:pump!`.\"\n   894\t  [p]\n   895\t  {:interest #(interest p)\n   896\t   :deadline #(next-deadline p)\n   897\t   :pump! #(pump! p %)})\n   898\t\n   899\t\n   900\t(defn debug-state\n   901\t  \"This instance's registry for diagnostics: its descriptors, whether its\n   902\t   native buffers are held, and owed reports.\"\n   903\t  [p]\n   904\t  (let [{:keys [handles rbuf notify]} @(st p)]\n   905\t    {:fds (vec (sort (keys handles)))\n   906\t     :buffers? (some? rbuf)\n   907\t     :notify (count notify)}))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/dev/jolt_workload_w.clj && nl -ba src/dev/jolt_workload_w_run.clj'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/dev/jolt_workload_w.clj && nl -ba src/dev/jolt_workload_w_run.clj'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns jolt-workload-w\n     2\t  \"J6g Workload W harness and peer cross-host integration (BRIEF-j6g.md).\n     3\t   Pre-registered criterion (v3 Section 2 A1, amended by v3.1 D4):\n     4\t   One jolt process serving two peers on the same machine while the REPL evaluates\n     5\t   a submitted loop each round; peer A sends one binary message at the\n     6\t   composition's :ws/max-frame-bytes (4,194,304 bytes); peer B exchanges 1 KiB\n     7\t   request/reply messages concurrently, up to 8 outstanding, at 10 Hz, for the\n     8\t   whole of A's transfer and >= 60 s (>= 600 overlapping round trips; fewer than\n     9\t   500 samples is an invalid run).\n    10\t   Criterion: during A's transfer, B's round-trip p99 <= 250 ms, no reply lost;\n    11\t   A's message delivered once; the REPL step count advances every owner round.\n    12\t\n    13\t   Deliverable 1: The workload W harness and sampler.\n    14\t   Deliverable 2: Peer cross-host rows (hosts that dial/listen, reachability\n    15\t   refusals on the REPL path).\n    16\t   Deliverable 3: REPL served-stream rejoin peer probe.\"\n    17\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n    18\t            [dao.host.bytes :as bytes]\n    19\t            [dao.host.text :as text]\n    20\t            [jolt.io-poller :as poller]\n    21\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    22\t            [dao.stream.cbor :as cbor]\n    23\t            [dao.stream.remote-channel :as remote-channel]\n    24\t            [dao.stream.rpc :as rpc]\n    25\t            [dao.stream.waitset.driver :as wake]\n    26\t            [dao.stream.ws :as ws]\n    27\t            [dao.stream.ws.jolt :as wsj]\n    28\t            [dao.stream.ws.rfc6455 :as rfc6455]\n    29\t            [dao.stream.ws.tcp :as tcp]\n    30\t            [dao.stream.ws.upgrade :as upgrade]\n    31\t            [jolt.ffi :as ffi]\n    32\t            [jolt.socket.native :as native]\n    33\t            [yin.repl.connect :as connect]\n    34\t            [yin.repl.driver :as driver]\n    35\t            [yin.repl.host :as host]\n    36\t            [yin.repl.main :as repl.main]\n    37\t            [yin.repl.serve :as serve]))\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\t;; =============================================================================\n    41\t;; Raw TCP helpers (probe sockets outside the adapter)\n    42\t;; =============================================================================\n    43\t\n    44\t(defn- bvec\n    45\t  [bs]\n    46\t  (mapv #(bit-and (int %) 0xFF) (vec bs)))\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(defn- octets\n    50\t  [v]\n    51\t  (byte-array (map unchecked-byte v)))\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\t(defn- ascii\n    55\t  [v]\n    56\t  (apply str (map char v)))\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\t(defn- with-native\n    60\t  [n f]\n    61\t  (let [p (ffi/alloc n)]\n    62\t    (try (f p)\n    63\t         (finally (ffi/free p)))))\n    64\t\n    65\t\n    66\t(defn- raw-peer!\n    67\t  [port]\n    68\t  (let [{:keys [fd state]} (tcp/connect! (tcp/parse-address \"127.0.0.1\" port))]\n    69\t    (when (= :connecting state)\n    70\t      (native/poll-one fd native/pollout 2000)\n    71\t      (tcp/connect-result fd))\n    72\t    {:fd fd, :in (atom []), :end (atom nil)}))\n    73\t\n    74\t\n    75\t(defn- raw-poll!\n    76\t  [{:keys [fd in end]}]\n    77\t  (when-not @end\n    78\t    (with-native 65536\n    79\t      (fn [p]\n    80\t        (loop []\n    81\t          (let [r (tcp/recv-chunk! fd p 65536)]\n    82\t            (cond\n    83\t              (= :would-block r) nil\n    84\t              (= :eof r) (reset! end :eof)\n    85\t              (:error r) (reset! end (:class r))\n    86\t              :else (do (swap! in into (bvec (ffi/read-array p (:n r))))\n    87\t                        (recur)))))))))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(defn- write-all!\n    91\t  ([fd bs]\n    92\t   (write-all! fd bs (+ (poller/clock-ms) 300000)))\n    93\t  ([fd bs deadline]\n    94\t   (let [bs (if (bytes/bytes? bs) bs (octets bs))\n    95\t         n (alength bs)\n    96\t         max-stalls 100]\n    97\t     (with-native (max 1 n)\n    98\t       (fn [p]\n    99\t         (loop [off 0\n   100\t                stalls 0]\n   101\t           (when (>= (poller/clock-ms) deadline)\n   102\t             (throw (ex-info \"raw write deadline exceeded\"\n   103\t                             {:workload/failure :timeout, :off off, :total n})))\n   104\t           (if (>= off n)\n   105\t             off\n   106\t             (do\n   107\t               ;; A short send must resume at the unsent byte, not byte zero.\n   108\t               (ffi/write-array p bs off (- n off))\n   109\t               (let [r (tcp/send-chunk! fd p (- n off))]\n   110\t                 (cond\n   111\t                   (:error r)\n   112\t                   (throw (ex-info \"raw write failed\" {:error r}))\n   113\t\n   114\t                   (and (map? r) (number? (:n r)) (pos? (:n r)) (<= (:n r) (- n off)))\n   115\t                   (recur (+ off (:n r)) 0)\n   116\t\n   117\t                   (or (= :would-block r) (= 0 (:n r)))\n   118\t                   (let [remaining (max 0 (long (- deadline (poller/clock-ms))))\n   119\t                         _ (native/poll-one fd native/pollout (min 2000 remaining))\n   120\t                         stalls (inc stalls)]\n   121\t                     (if (>= stalls max-stalls)\n   122\t                       (throw (ex-info \"TRANSFER STALLED: raw write made no progress\"\n   123\t                                       {:workload/failure :transfer-stalled,\n   124\t                                        :off off, :total n, :stalls stalls, :result r}))\n   125\t                       (recur off stalls)))\n   126\t\n   127\t                   :else\n   128\t                   (throw (ex-info \"unexpected raw write result\" {:result r}))))))))))))\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\t(defn- write-some!\n   132\t  [fd bs off limit]\n   133\t  (let [bs (if (bytes/bytes? bs) bs (octets bs))\n   134\t        n (min (- (alength bs) off) limit)]\n   135\t    (with-native n\n   136\t      (fn [p]\n   137\t        (ffi/write-array p bs off n)\n   138\t        (let [r (tcp/send-chunk! fd p n)]\n   139\t          (cond\n   140\t            (= :would-block r) :would-block\n   141\t            (:error r) (throw (ex-info \"raw write-some failed\" {:error r}))\n   142\t            (map? r) (:n r)\n   143\t             :else (throw (ex-info \"unexpected raw write-some result\" {:result r}))))))))\n   144\t\n   145\t\n   146\t(defn- head-end\n   147\t  [v]\n   148\t  (let [n (count v)]\n   149\t    (loop [i 3]\n   150\t      (cond\n   151\t        (>= i n) nil\n   152\t        (and (= 13 (nth v (- i 3)))\n   153\t             (= 10 (nth v (- i 2)))\n   154\t             (= 13 (nth v (- i 1)))\n   155\t             (= 10 (nth v i)))\n   156\t        (inc i)\n   157\t        :else (recur (inc i))))))\n   158\t\n   159\t\n   160\t(defn- raw-close!\n   161\t  [peer]\n   162\t  (tcp/shutdown! (:fd peer) :both)\n   163\t  (tcp/close! (:fd peer)))\n   164\t\n   165\t\n   166\t;; =============================================================================\n   167\t;; Int32 Big-Endian packing for request IDs\n   168\t;; =============================================================================\n   169\t\n   170\t(defn- int32->bytes!\n   171\t  [bs off val]\n   172\t  (bytes/set! bs off (bit-and (bit-shift-right val 24) 0xFF))\n   173\t  (bytes/set! bs (+ off 1) (bit-and (bit-shift-right val 16) 0xFF))\n   174\t  (bytes/set! bs (+ off 2) (bit-and (bit-shift-right val 8) 0xFF))\n   175\t  (bytes/set! bs (+ off 3) (bit-and val 0xFF))\n   176\t  bs)\n   177\t\n   178\t\n   179\t(defn- bytes->int32\n   180\t  [bs off]\n   181\t  (bit-or (bit-shift-left (bit-and (bytes/get bs off) 0xFF) 24)\n   182\t          (bit-shift-left (bit-and (bytes/get bs (+ off 1)) 0xFF) 16)\n   183\t          (bit-shift-left (bit-and (bytes/get bs (+ off 2)) 0xFF) 8)\n   184\t          (bit-and (bytes/get bs (+ off 3)) 0xFF)))\n   185\t\n   186\t\n   187\t;; =============================================================================\n   188\t;; Deliverable 1: Workload W Harness\n   189\t;; =============================================================================\n   190\t\n   191\t(defn- make-1kib-request\n   192\t  [id]\n   193\t  (let [bs (bytes/alloc 1024)]\n   194\t    (int32->bytes! bs 0 id)\n   195\t    bs))\n   196\t\n   197\t\n   198\t(defn- check-deadline!\n   199\t  [deadline phase]\n   200\t  (when (>= (poller/clock-ms) deadline)\n   201\t    (throw (ex-info \"Workload W exceeded its five-minute deadline\"\n   202\t                    {:workload/failure :timeout, :phase phase}))))\n   203\t\n   204\t\n   205\t(defn run-workload-w\n   206\t  \"Run the pre-registered Workload W benchmark:\n   207\t   - Peer A: one 4,194,304 byte binary message (:ws/max-frame-bytes) paced over >= 60 s.\n   208\t   - Peer B: 1 KiB request/reply concurrent (up to 8 outstanding) at 10 Hz.\n   209\t   - REPL loop: evaluates a submitted loop each round, step count advances every round.\n   210\t   - Criterion: p99 <= 250 ms, no reply lost, A delivered once, REPL step advances every round.\n   211\t   Run through bb workload-w:jolt for the independent five-minute watchdog.\n   212\t   Returns {:pass? ... :p99 ... :samples ... :elapsed-ms ... :delivered-once? ... :repl-advances? ...}.\"\n   213\t  [& {:keys [target-duration-ms target-samples]\n   214\t      :or {target-duration-ms 60000 target-samples 600}}]\n   215\t  (println \"================================================================================\")\n   216\t  (println \"J6g Workload W: Starting benchmark (target duration:\" target-duration-ms\n   217\t           \"ms, target samples:\" target-samples \")\")\n   218\t  (println \"================================================================================\")\n   219\t  (let [run-start (poller/clock-ms)\n   220\t        deadline (+ run-start 300000)\n   221\t        w (wake/make-wake)\n   222\t        server-inst (wsj/create)\n   223\t        client-b-inst (wsj/create)\n   224\t\n   225\t        ;; Peer A accounting\n   226\t        a-deliveries (atom [])\n   227\t        a-delivered-once? (atom false)\n   228\t\n   229\t        ;; Server bind\n   230\t        server-bound? (atom false)\n   231\t        server-port (atom 0)\n   232\t        _ (wsj/bind! server-inst\n   233\t                     {:bind-host \"127.0.0.1\"\n   234\t                      :bind-port 0\n   235\t                      :ws/max-frame-bytes 4194304\n   236\t                      :codecs [cbor/profile]\n   237\t                      :deposit! (fn [event detail]\n   238\t                                  (when (= :bind-succeeded event)\n   239\t                                    (reset! server-port (:port detail))\n   240\t                                    (reset! server-bound? true)))\n   241\t                      :accept! (fn [path seam _now]\n   242\t                                 (cond\n   243\t                                   (= path \"/peer-a\")\n   244\t                                   {:ws/adapter\n   245\t                                    {:opened! (fn [])\n   246\t                                     :binary! (fn [payload]\n   247\t                                                (swap! a-deliveries conj (alength payload)))\n   248\t                                     :message! (fn [_])\n   249\t                                     :closed! (fn [_ _])\n   250\t                                     :error! (fn [_])\n   251\t                                     :too-large! (fn [])}}\n   252\t\n   253\t                                   (= path \"/peer-b\")\n   254\t                                   (let [seam-ref (atom seam)]\n   255\t                                     {:ws/adapter\n   256\t                                      {:opened! (fn [])\n   257\t                                       :binary! (fn [payload]\n   258\t                                                  ((:send! @seam-ref) payload))\n   259\t                                       :message! (fn [msg]\n   260\t                                                   ((:send! @seam-ref) msg))\n   261\t                                       :closed! (fn [_ _])\n   262\t                                       :error! (fn [_])\n   263\t                                       :too-large! (fn [])}})))})\n   264\t\n   265\t        ;; Drive until server listener is bound\n   266\t        _ (loop []\n   267\t            (check-deadline! deadline :server-bind)\n   268\t            (when-not @server-bound?\n   269\t              (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 (wsj/host-pump server-inst) nil)\n   270\t              (recur)))\n   271\t        port @server-port]\n   272\t\n   273\t    (println \"Server listening on port\" port)\n   274\t\n   275\t    ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   276\t    ;; Peer B setup: connects via client adapter\n   277\t    ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   278\t    (let [b-opened? (atom false)\n   279\t          b-samples (atom [])\n   280\t          b-outstanding (atom {})\n   281\t          b-lost (atom 0)\n   282\t          b-req-seq (atom 0)\n   283\t          b-seam (atom nil)\n   284\t          b-cb {:ws/codec cbor/profile\n   285\t                :ws/max-frame-bytes 4194304\n   286\t                :opened! #(reset! b-opened? true)\n   287\t                :binary! (fn [payload]\n   288\t                           (let [now (poller/clock-ms)\n   289\t                                 req-id (bytes->int32 payload 0)\n   290\t                                 sent-at (get @b-outstanding req-id)]\n   291\t                             (if sent-at\n   292\t                               (do (swap! b-outstanding dissoc req-id)\n   293\t                                    (swap! b-samples conj (- now sent-at))\n   294\t                                    ;; The independent sampler observes every completed reply.\n   295\t                                    (println \"W-SAMPLE\" (- now sent-at))\n   296\t                                    (flush))\n   297\t                               (swap! b-lost inc))))\n   298\t                :message! (fn [_])\n   299\t                :closed! (fn [_ _])\n   300\t                :error! (fn [_])\n   301\t                :too-large! (fn [])}]\n   302\t\n   303\t      (reset! b-seam (wsj/connect! client-b-inst\n   304\t                                   {:ws/host \"127.0.0.1\"\n   305\t                                    :ws/port port\n   306\t                                    :ws/path \"/peer-b\"}\n   307\t                                   b-cb))\n   308\t\n   309\t      ;; Drive until Peer B connection is open\n   310\t      (loop []\n   311\t        (check-deadline! deadline :peer-b-upgrade)\n   312\t        (when-not @b-opened?\n   313\t          (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 (wsj/host-pump server-inst) nil)\n   314\t          (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 (wsj/host-pump client-b-inst) nil)\n   315\t          (recur)))\n   316\t\n   317\t      (println \"Peer B connected and upgraded\")\n   318\t\n   319\t      ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   320\t      ;; Peer A setup: connects via raw socket, upgrades to /peer-a\n   321\t      ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   322\t      (let [raw-a (raw-peer! port)\n   323\t            upgrade-req (str \"GET /peer-a HTTP/1.1\\r\\n\"\n   324\t                             \"Host: 127.0.0.1:\" port \"\\r\\n\"\n   325\t                             \"Upgrade: websocket\\r\\n\"\n   326\t                             \"Connection: Upgrade\\r\\n\"\n   327\t                             \"Sec-WebSocket-Key: dGhlIHNhbXBsZSBub25jZQ==\\r\\n\"\n   328\t                             \"Sec-WebSocket-Version: 13\\r\\n\"\n   329\t                             \"Sec-WebSocket-Protocol: dao.stream.cbor\\r\\n\\r\\n\")]\n   330\t        (write-all! (:fd raw-a) (text/utf8-encode upgrade-req) deadline)\n   331\t\n   332\t        ;; Drive until Peer A upgrade response arrives\n   333\t        (loop []\n   334\t          (check-deadline! deadline :peer-a-upgrade)\n   335\t          (raw-poll! raw-a)\n   336\t          (when-not (head-end @(:in raw-a))\n   337\t            (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 (wsj/host-pump server-inst) nil)\n   338\t            (recur)))\n   339\t\n   340\t        (println \"Peer A connected and upgraded\")\n   341\t\n   342\t        ;; Prepare Peer A's 4,194,304-byte binary frame\n   343\t        (let [a-payload (bytes/alloc 4194304)\n   344\t              mask-key (byte-array [(unchecked-byte 0x37) (unchecked-byte 0xFA)\n   345\t                                    (unchecked-byte 0x21) (unchecked-byte 0x3D)])\n   346\t              a-frame (rfc6455/encode-frame {:opcode :binary\n   347\t                                             :payload a-payload\n   348\t                                             :mask-key mask-key\n   349\t                                             :fin? true})\n   350\t              total-a-frame-len (alength a-frame)\n   351\t              a-sent (atom 0)\n   352\t\n   353\t              ;; REPL loop setup\n   354\t              repl-state (atom (repl.main/boot {:adapter (host/websocket)}))\n   355\t              repl-step-count (atom 0)\n   356\t              owner-round-count (atom 0)\n   357\t\n   358\t              ;; Timing and dispatch state\n   359\t              start-time (poller/clock-ms)\n   360\t              last-10hz-tick (atom start-time)\n   361\t              last-telemetry-tick (atom start-time)\n   362\t              a-stalls (atom 0)\n   363\t              a-stalled? (atom false)\n   364\t              timed-out? (atom false)\n   365\t              max-consecutive-stalls 500\n   366\t              server-pump (wsj/host-pump server-inst)\n   367\t              client-b-pump (wsj/host-pump client-b-inst)]\n   368\t\n   369\t          (println \"Frame length for Peer A:\" total-a-frame-len \"bytes\")\n   370\t          (println \"Entering owner round loop...\")\n   371\t          (flush)\n   372\t\n   373\t          ;; Main owner loop\n   374\t          (loop []\n   375\t            (let [now (poller/clock-ms)\n   376\t                  elapsed (- now start-time)]\n   377\t\n   378\t              ;; Hard timeout guard: cap whole run at 5 minutes\n   379\t              (if (>= now deadline)\n   380\t                (do (reset! timed-out? true)\n   381\t                    (println \"HARD CAP EXCEEDED: workload-w exceeded 5 minutes (\"\n   382\t                             (- now run-start) \"ms), terminating loop.\"))\n   383\t\n   384\t                (do\n   385\t                  ;; 1. Advance owner round and step REPL loop\n   386\t                  (swap! owner-round-count inc)\n   387\t                  (when (= 1 @owner-round-count)\n   388\t                    (println \"W-PHASE repl-step\")\n   389\t                    (flush))\n   390\t                  (driver/submit-line! (:input @repl-state)\n   391\t                                       \"(loop [i 0] (if (< i 5) (recur (inc i)) i))\")\n   392\t                  (let [stepped (driver/repl-step @repl-state now)\n   393\t                        [_entries next-st] (driver/take-outbox stepped)]\n   394\t                    (reset! repl-state next-st)\n   395\t                    (swap! repl-step-count inc))\n   396\t\n   397\t                  ;; 2. Paced Peer A transfer across target-duration-ms (with no-progress guard)\n   398\t                  (when (= 1 @owner-round-count)\n   399\t                    (println \"W-PHASE peer-a-send\")\n   400\t                    (flush))\n   401\t                  (when-not @a-stalled?\n   402\t                    (let [target-bytes (if (>= elapsed target-duration-ms)\n   403\t                                         total-a-frame-len\n   404\t                                         (min total-a-frame-len\n   405\t                                              (long (* total-a-frame-len\n   406\t                                                       (/ (double elapsed) (double target-duration-ms))))))]\n   407\t                      (when (< @a-sent target-bytes)\n   408\t                        (let [to-write (min (- target-bytes @a-sent) 65536)\n   409\t                              r (write-some! (:fd raw-a) a-frame @a-sent to-write)]\n   410\t                          (cond\n   411\t                            (or (= :would-block r) (= 0 r))\n   412\t                            (let [stalls (swap! a-stalls inc)]\n   413\t                              (native/poll-one (:fd raw-a) native/pollout 0)\n   414\t                              (when (>= stalls max-consecutive-stalls)\n   415\t                                (reset! a-stalled? true)\n   416\t                                (println \"TRANSFER STALLED: Peer A hit\" stalls\n   417\t                                         \"consecutive no-progress polls at\" @a-sent \"/\" total-a-frame-len \"bytes. Aborting transfer leg.\")\n   418\t                                (flush)))\n   419\t\n   420\t                            (and (number? r) (pos? r) (<= r to-write))\n   421\t                            (do (reset! a-stalls 0)\n   422\t                                (swap! a-sent + r))\n   423\t\n   424\t                            :else\n   425\t                            (do (reset! a-stalled? true)\n   426\t                                (println \"TRANSFER STALLED: unexpected Peer A send result\" r)\n   427\t                                (flush)))))))\n   428\t\n   429\t                  ;; 3. Peer B 10 Hz dispatch: concurrent requests up to 8 outstanding\n   430\t                  (when (>= (- now @last-10hz-tick) 100)\n   431\t                    (reset! last-10hz-tick now)\n   432\t                    (when (< (count @b-outstanding) 8)\n   433\t                      (let [id (swap! b-req-seq inc)\n   434\t                            req-bs (make-1kib-request id)]\n   435\t                        (swap! b-outstanding assoc id now)\n   436\t                        ((:send! @b-seam) req-bs))))\n   437\t\n   438\t                  ;; 4. Periodic sampler flush every 10 seconds to ensure telemetry\n   439\t                  (when (>= (- now @last-telemetry-tick) 10000)\n   440\t                    (reset! last-telemetry-tick now)\n   441\t                    (let [sc (count @b-samples)\n   442\t                          cur-p99 (when (pos? sc)\n   443\t                                    (nth (sort @b-samples) (min (dec sc) (int (* 0.99 sc)))))]\n   444\t                      (println (str \"TELEMETRY: elapsed=\" (long (/ elapsed 1000)) \"s, samples=\" sc\n   445\t                                    \", running p99=\" (if cur-p99 (str cur-p99 \"ms\") \"ABSENT\") \", A-sent=\" @a-sent \"/\" total-a-frame-len\n   446\t                                    \" (\" (long (* 100 (/ (double @a-sent) (double total-a-frame-len)))) \"%), A-deliveries=\" (count @a-deliveries)\n   447\t                                    (when @a-stalled? \" [A-STALLED]\")))\n   448\t                      (flush)))\n   449\t\n   450\t                  ;; 5. Pump I/O for server and client B\n   451\t                  (when (= 1 @owner-round-count)\n   452\t                    (println \"W-PHASE server-pump\")\n   453\t                    (flush))\n   454\t                  (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 server-pump nil)\n   455\t                  (when (= 1 @owner-round-count)\n   456\t                    (println \"W-PHASE client-b-pump\")\n   457\t                    (flush))\n   458\t                  (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 client-b-pump nil)\n   459\t                  (when (= 1 @owner-round-count)\n   460\t                    (println \"W-PHASE owner-round-complete\")\n   461\t                    (flush))\n   462\t\n   463\t                  ;; Check exit conditions\n   464\t                  (let [a-done? (or @a-stalled?\n   465\t                                    (and (>= @a-sent total-a-frame-len)\n   466\t                                         (seq @a-deliveries)))\n   467\t                        time-done? (>= elapsed target-duration-ms)\n   468\t                        samples-done? (>= (count @b-samples) target-samples)]\n   469\t\n   470\t                    (if (and a-done? time-done? samples-done?)\n   471\t                      ;; Drain trailing in-flight requests briefly\n   472\t                      (let [drain-deadline (+ (poller/clock-ms) 500)]\n   473\t                        (loop []\n   474\t                          (when (and (seq @b-outstanding)\n   475\t                                     (< (poller/clock-ms) (min deadline drain-deadline)))\n   476\t                            (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 server-pump nil)\n   477\t                            (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 client-b-pump nil)\n   478\t                            (recur))))\n   479\t                      (recur)))))))\n   480\t\n   481\t          ;; Cleanup sockets\n   482\t          (raw-close! raw-a)\n   483\t          (wsj/close-host! client-b-inst)\n   484\t          (wsj/close-host! server-inst)\n   485\t          (wake/close! w)\n   486\t\n   487\t          ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------\n   488\t          ;; Evaluation of pre-registered criterion\n   489\t          ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------\n   490\t          (let [sample-count (count @b-samples)\n   491\t                elapsed-ms (- (poller/clock-ms) run-start)\n   492\t                valid-run? (>= sample-count 500)\n   493\t                target-samples-met? (>= sample-count target-samples)\n   494\t                sorted (sort @b-samples)\n   495\t                p99-idx (int (* 0.99 sample-count))\n   496\t                p99 (when (and (not @timed-out?) (pos? sample-count))\n   497\t                      (nth sorted (min (dec sample-count) p99-idx)))\n   498\t                p99-ok? (and (some? p99) (<= p99 250))\n   499\t                repl-advances? (= @owner-round-count @repl-step-count)\n   500\t                a-deliv-count (count @a-deliveries)\n   501\t                a-deliv-len (or (first @a-deliveries) 0)\n   502\t                delivered-once? (and (= 1 a-deliv-count)\n   503\t                                     (= 4194304 a-deliv-len))\n   504\t                replies-lost (count @b-outstanding)\n   505\t                no-reply-lost? (and (zero? @b-lost) (zero? replies-lost))\n   506\t                all-pass? (and (not @timed-out?)\n   507\t                               (not @a-stalled?)\n   508\t                               valid-run?\n   509\t                               target-samples-met?\n   510\t                               p99-ok?\n   511\t                               repl-advances?\n   512\t                               delivered-once?\n   513\t                               no-reply-lost?)]\n   514\t\n   515\t            (println)\n   516\t            (println \"================================================================================\")\n   517\t            (println \"Workload W Results:\" (if all-pass? \"SUCCESS\" \"FAILURE\"))\n   518\t            (println \"================================================================================\")\n   519\t            (println \"  Hard cap timed out:           \" @timed-out?)\n   520\t            (println \"  Elapsed:                      \" elapsed-ms \"ms\")\n   521\t            (println \"  Peer A transfer stalled:      \" @a-stalled?)\n   522\t            (println \"  Sample count:                 \" sample-count\n   523\t                     (str \"(valid >= 500: \" valid-run? \", target >= \" target-samples \": \" target-samples-met? \")\"))\n   524\t            (println \"  p99 round-trip latency:       \" (if (some? p99) (str p99 \"ms\") \"ABSENT\")\n   525\t                     (str \"(criterion <= 250 ms: \" p99-ok? \")\"))\n   526\t            (println \"  Peer B replies lost:          \" replies-lost \"(unanswered) +\" @b-lost \"(corrupt)\")\n   527\t            (println \"  Peer A delivered once:        \" delivered-once?\n   528\t                     (str \"(deliveries: \" a-deliv-count \", bytes: \" a-deliv-len \", sent: \" @a-sent \")\"))\n   529\t            (println \"  REPL per-round step advance:  \" repl-advances?\n   530\t                     (str \"(rounds: \" @owner-round-count \", REPL steps: \" @repl-step-count \")\"))\n   531\t            (println)\n   532\t\n   533\t            ;; Required report records per BRIEF-j6g.md\n   534\t            (if (some? p99)\n   535\t              (println \"RECORD p99\" p99 \"ms\")\n   536\t              (println \"RECORD p99 ABSENT\"))\n   537\t            (println \"RECORD sample count\" sample-count)\n   538\t            (println \"RECORD elapsed ms\" elapsed-ms)\n   539\t            (println \"RECORD delivered once\" delivered-once?)\n   540\t            (println \"RECORD per-round step advance\" repl-advances?)\n   541\t\n   542\t            (if all-pass?\n   543\t              (do (println \"PASS workload-w\")\n   544\t                  {:pass? true\n   545\t                   :p99 p99\n   546\t                    :samples sample-count\n   547\t                    :elapsed-ms elapsed-ms\n   548\t                    :timed-out? @timed-out?\n   549\t                    :transfer-stalled? @a-stalled?\n   550\t                   :delivered-once? delivered-once?\n   551\t                   :repl-advances? repl-advances?\n   552\t                   :replies-lost replies-lost})\n   553\t              (do (println \"FAIL workload-w\")\n   554\t                  {:pass? false\n   555\t                   :p99 p99\n   556\t                    :samples sample-count\n   557\t                    :elapsed-ms elapsed-ms\n   558\t                    :timed-out? @timed-out?\n   559\t                    :transfer-stalled? @a-stalled?\n   560\t                   :delivered-once? delivered-once?\n   561\t                   :repl-advances? repl-advances?\n   562\t                   :replies-lost replies-lost}))))))))\n   563\t\n   564\t\n   565\t;; =============================================================================\n   566\t;; Deliverable 2: Peer Cross-Host Rows\n   567\t;; =============================================================================\n   568\t\n   569\t(defn run-cross-host-rows\n   570\t  \"Verify cross-host listener, dialer, and REPL path reachability rows:\n   571\t   - Hosts that listen: 127.0.0.1, 0.0.0.0, localhost, ::1; port 0 ephemeral; port collision.\n   572\t   - Hosts that dial: 127.0.0.1, localhost, [::1]; hostname refused; wss refused.\n   573\t   - REPL reachability refusals: local reachability failure, reachability failure, disclaimed path.\"\n   574\t  []\n   575\t  (println \"================================================================================\")\n   576\t  (println \"J6g Cross-Host Rows: Running checks...\")\n   577\t  (println \"================================================================================\")\n   578\t  (let [w (wake/make-wake)\n   579\t        passed (atom 0)\n   580\t        failed (atom 0)\n   581\t        check! (fn [label ok? detail]\n   582\t                 (if ok?\n   583\t                   (do (swap! passed inc)\n   584\t                       (println \"  ok  \" label))\n   585\t                   (do (swap! failed inc)\n   586\t                       (println \"  FAIL\" label detail))))]\n   587\t\n   588\t    ;; 1. Hosts that listen: 127.0.0.1, 0.0.0.0, localhost, ::1\n   589\t    (doseq [bind-host [\"127.0.0.1\" \"0.0.0.0\" \"localhost\" \"::1\"]]\n   590\t      (let [inst (wsj/create)\n   591\t            bound-port (atom nil)\n   592\t            res (wsj/bind! inst {:bind-host bind-host\n   593\t                                 :bind-port 0\n   594\t                                 :deposit! (fn [ev detail]\n   595\t                                             (when (= :bind-succeeded ev)\n   596\t                                               (reset! bound-port (:port detail))))})]\n   597\t        (check! (str \"listen on \" bind-host \" binds ephemeral port\")\n   598\t                (and (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome res))\n   599\t                     (pos? (or @bound-port 0)))\n   600\t                {:res res :port @bound-port})\n   601\t        (wsj/close-host! inst)))\n   602\t\n   603\t    ;; Port collision check\n   604\t    (let [inst1 (wsj/create)\n   605\t          inst2 (wsj/create)\n   606\t          bound-port (atom nil)\n   607\t          _ (wsj/bind! inst1 {:bind-host \"127.0.0.1\"\n   608\t                              :bind-port 0\n   609\t                              :deposit! (fn [ev detail]\n   610\t                                          (when (= :bind-succeeded ev)\n   611\t                                            (reset! bound-port (:port detail))))})\n   612\t          collision-res (wsj/bind! inst2 {:bind-host \"127.0.0.1\"\n   613\t                                          :bind-port @bound-port\n   614\t                                          :deposit! (fn [_ _])})]\n   615\t      (check! \"listen on colliding port returns transport-error\"\n   616\t              (= :dao.stream/transport-error (:dao.stream/outcome collision-res))\n   617\t              {:collision collision-res})\n   618\t      (wsj/close-host! inst2)\n   619\t      (wsj/close-host! inst1))\n   620\t\n   621\t    ;; 2. Hosts that dial: 127.0.0.1, localhost, [::1]\n   622\t    (doseq [[bind-h dial-h label] [[\"127.0.0.1\" \"127.0.0.1\" \"127.0.0.1\"]\n   623\t                                   [\"127.0.0.1\" \"localhost\" \"localhost\"]\n   624\t                                   [\"::1\" \"[::1]\" \"[::1]\"]]]\n   625\t      (let [si (wsj/create)\n   626\t            ci (wsj/create)\n   627\t            port (atom nil)\n   628\t            _ (wsj/bind! si {:bind-host bind-h\n   629\t                             :bind-port 0\n   630\t                             :deposit! (fn [ev detail]\n   631\t                                         (when (= :bind-succeeded ev)\n   632\t                                           (reset! port (:port detail))))})\n   633\t            opened? (atom false)\n   634\t            seam (wsj/connect! ci\n   635\t                               {:ws/host dial-h :ws/port @port :ws/path \"/repl\"}\n   636\t                               {:ws/codec cbor/profile\n   637\t                                :opened! #(reset! opened? true)\n   638\t                                :binary! (fn [_])\n   639\t                                :message! (fn [_])\n   640\t                                :closed! (fn [_ _])\n   641\t                                :error! (fn [_])\n   642\t                                :too-large! (fn [])})\n   643\t            deadline (+ (poller/clock-ms) 5000)]\n   644\t        (loop []\n   645\t          (when-not (or @opened? (> (poller/clock-ms) deadline))\n   646\t            (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 (wsj/host-pump si) nil)\n   647\t            (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 (wsj/host-pump ci) nil)\n   648\t            (recur)))\n   649\t        (check! (str \"dial on \" label \" connects and opens\")\n   650\t                (and (some? seam) @opened?)\n   651\t                {:seam seam :opened? @opened?})\n   652\t        (wsj/close-host! ci)\n   653\t        (wsj/close-host! si)))\n   654\t\n   655\t    ;; Refusal of host name (resolver trap not sprung)\n   656\t    (let [ci (wsj/create)\n   657\t          trap (fn [& _] (throw (ex-info \"resolver called\" {})))]\n   658\t      (with-redefs-fn {#'native/resolve-addrs trap\n   659\t                       #'native/c-getaddrinfo trap}\n   660\t        (fn []\n   661\t          (let [seam (wsj/connect! ci\n   662\t                                   {:ws/host \"example.invalid\"\n   663\t                                    :ws/port 80\n   664\t                                    :ws/path \"/repl\"}\n   665\t                                   {:opened! (fn [])\n   666\t                                    :closed! (fn [_ _])\n   667\t                                    :message! (fn [_])\n   668\t                                    :binary! (fn [_])})]\n   669\t            (check! \"dial to hostname returns nil, resolver trap not sprung\"\n   670\t                    (nil? seam)\n   671\t                    {:seam seam}))))\n   672\t      (wsj/close-host! ci))\n   673\t\n   674\t    ;; Refusal of wss scheme\n   675\t    (let [ci (wsj/create)\n   676\t          seam (wsj/connect! ci\n   677\t                               {:ws/scheme \"wss\"\n   678\t                                :ws/host \"127.0.0.1\"\n   679\t                                :ws/port 443\n   680\t                                :ws/path \"/repl\"}\n   681\t                               {:opened! (fn [])\n   682\t                                :closed! (fn [_ _])\n   683\t                                :message! (fn [_])\n   684\t                                :binary! (fn [_])})]\n   685\t      (check! \"dial with wss scheme is refused explicitly (nil returned)\"\n   686\t              (nil? seam)\n   687\t              {:seam seam})\n   688\t      (wsj/close-host! ci))\n   689\t\n   690\t    ;; 3. Reachability refusals on the REPL path (yin.repl.connect/open)\n   691\t    ;; 3a. Host name yields local reachability failure text\n   692\t    (let [ci (wsj/create)\n   693\t          opened (connect/open {:url \"daostream:ws://example.invalid:80/repl\"\n   694\t                                :host {:connect! (fn [d a] (wsj/connect! ci d a))}\n   695\t                                :now 0})\n   696\t          text (pr-str opened)]\n   697\t      (check! \"connect/open to hostname gives local reachability failure text\"\n   698\t              (str/includes? text \"local reachability failure\")\n   699\t              {:opened text})\n   700\t      (wsj/close-host! ci))\n   701\t\n   702\t    ;; 3b. Unbound / unreachable port yields reachability failure text\n   703\t    (let [ci (wsj/create)\n   704\t          ;; Unbound port on loopback: dial fails immediately on connect\n   705\t          unused-port 59999\n   706\t          opened (connect/open {:url (str \"daostream:ws://127.0.0.1:\" unused-port \"/repl\")\n   707\t                                :host (host/websocket)\n   708\t                                :now 0})\n   709\t          conn (connect/connection-key opened)\n   710\t          client (connect/client-key opened)\n   711\t          deadline (+ (poller/clock-ms) 3000)\n   712\t          observed (loop [c conn cl client]\n   713\t                     (let [c' (connect/step! c (poller/clock-ms))\n   714\t                           cl' (:dao.stream.rpc/state (rpc/poll! cl))\n   715\t                           [c'' ev] (connect/observe-terminal c' (:terminal cl'))]\n   716\t                       (cond\n   717\t                         ev [c'' ev]\n   718\t                         (> (poller/clock-ms) deadline) [c'' nil]\n   719\t                         :else (do (wake/sleep-fds! w 10 nil nil)\n   720\t                                   (recur c'' cl')))))\n   721\t          event (second observed)\n   722\t          ev-text (connect/text-key event)]\n   723\t      (check! \"connect/open to unbound port observes transport-error reachability failure\"\n   724\t              (and (some? event)\n   725\t                   (str/includes? (str ev-text) \"reachability failure\"))\n   726\t              {:event event :text ev-text})\n   727\t      (wsj/close-host! ci))\n   728\t\n   729\t    (wake/close! w)\n   730\t    (println)\n   731\t    (println \"Cross-host rows:\" @passed \"passed,\" @failed \"failed\")\n   732\t    (if (zero? @failed)\n   733\t      (do (println \"PASS cross-host\") true)\n   734\t      (do (println \"FAIL cross-host\") false))))\n   735\t\n   736\t\n   737\t;; =============================================================================\n   738\t;; Deliverable 3: REPL Served-Stream Rejoin Checks\n   739\t;; =============================================================================\n   740\t\n   741\t(defn- step-peer!\n   742\t  [peer now]\n   743\t  (swap! (:connection peer) connect/step! now)\n   744\t  (swap! (:client peer) #(:dao.stream.rpc/state (rpc/poll! %))))\n   745\t\n   746\t\n   747\t(defn- drive-repl-peers!\n   748\t  [w insts peers pred ms]\n   749\t  (let [deadline (+ (poller/clock-ms) ms)\n   750\t        hps (mapv wsj/host-pump insts)]\n   751\t    (loop []\n   752\t      (let [now (poller/clock-ms)]\n   753\t        (doseq [p peers] (step-peer! p now))\n   754\t        (doseq [hp hps] (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 hp nil))\n   755\t        (cond\n   756\t          (pred) true\n   757\t          (> (poller/clock-ms) deadline) false\n   758\t          :else (recur))))))\n   759\t\n   760\t\n   761\t(defn run-served-stream-rejoin\n   762\t  \"Run the 4 served-stream facts over two jolt host instances:\n   763\t   Fact 1: evaluation round trips and two clients get their own answers.\n   764\t   Fact 2: killing connection is observable and requests are lost.\n   765\t   Fact 3: reattaching resumes served stream and deposit medium.\n   766\t   Fact 4: stopping endpoint ends served stream (not closes it).\"\n   767\t  []\n   768\t  (println \"================================================================================\")\n   769\t  (println \"J6g Served-Stream Rejoin: Running 4 served-stream peer facts...\")\n   770\t  (println \"================================================================================\")\n   771\t  (let [w (wake/make-wake)\n   772\t        passed (atom 0)\n   773\t        failed (atom 0)\n   774\t        check! (fn [label ok? detail]\n   775\t                 (if ok?\n   776\t                   (do (swap! passed inc)\n   777\t                       (println \"  ok  \" label))\n   778\t                   (do (swap! failed inc)\n   779\t                       (println \"  FAIL\" label detail))))]\n   780\t\n   781\t    ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   782\t    ;; Fact 1: Two clients connect and get their own answers without crosstalk\n   783\t    ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   784\t    (let [si (wsj/create)\n   785\t          ci1 (wsj/create)\n   786\t          ci2 (wsj/create)\n   787\t          port (atom 0)\n   788\t          server-st (atom (serve/serve! {:bind-host \"127.0.0.1\"\n   789\t                                         :bind-port 0\n   790\t                                         :host {:bind! (fn [opts]\n   791\t                                                         (wsj/bind! si (assoc opts :ws.jolt/adapter-of\n   792\t                                                                              #(some-> (:ws/handle %) ws/adapter))))\n   793\t                                                :unbind! (fn [lh dep] (wsj/unbind! si lh dep))\n   794\t                                                :connect! (fn [d a] (wsj/connect! si d a))}}))\n   795\t          ;; Advance server until port bound\n   796\t          _ (loop []\n   797\t              (let [stepped (serve/step @server-st (poller/clock-ms))\n   798\t                    [_ next-st] (serve/take-outbox stepped)]\n   799\t                (reset! server-st next-st)\n   800\t                (when-let [p (get-in next-st [:spec :port])]\n   801\t                  (when (pos? p) (reset! port p)))\n   802\t                (when (zero? @port)\n   803\t                  (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 (wsj/host-pump si) nil)\n   804\t                  (recur))))\n   805\t          url (str \"daostream:ws://127.0.0.1:\" @port \"/repl\")\n   806\t          now (poller/clock-ms)\n   807\t          p1-open (connect/open {:url url :host {:connect! (fn [d a] (wsj/connect! ci1 d a))} :now now})\n   808\t          p2-open (connect/open {:url url :host {:connect! (fn [d a] (wsj/connect! ci2 d a))} :now now})\n   809\t          peer1 {:connection (atom (connect/connection-key p1-open))\n   810\t                 :client (atom (connect/client-key p1-open))}\n   811\t          peer2 {:connection (atom (connect/connection-key p2-open))\n   812\t                 :client (atom (connect/client-key p2-open))}]\n   813\t\n   814\t      ;; Send eval requests\n   815\t      (let [c1 (rpc/request! @(:client peer1) 1 :op/eval \"(+ 40 2)\")\n   816\t            c2 (rpc/request! @(:client peer2) 2 :op/eval \"(+ 20 3)\")]\n   817\t        (reset! (:client peer1) c1)\n   818\t        (reset! (:client peer2) c2)\n   819\t\n   820\t        ;; Drive until both answers arrive\n   821\t        (drive-repl-peers! w [si ci1 ci2] [peer1 peer2]\n   822\t                           (fn []\n   823\t                             (let [stepped (serve/step @server-st (poller/clock-ms))\n   824\t                                   [_ next-st] (serve/take-outbox stepped)]\n   825\t                               (reset! server-st next-st)\n   826\t                               (and (some? (rpc/response @(:client peer1) 1))\n   827\t                                    (some? (rpc/response @(:client peer2) 2)))))\n   828\t                           5000)\n   829\t\n   830\t        (let [ans1 (rpc/response @(:client peer1) 1)\n   831\t              ans2 (rpc/response @(:client peer2) 2)]\n   832\t          (check! \"Fact 1: peer 1 gets 42 and peer 2 gets 23 without crosstalk\"\n   833\t                  (and (= \"42\" (rpc/answer-ok ans1))\n   834\t                       (= \"23\" (rpc/answer-ok ans2))\n   835\t                       (nil? (rpc/response @(:client peer1) 2))\n   836\t                       (nil? (rpc/response @(:client peer2) 1)))\n   837\t                  {:ans1 ans1 :ans2 ans2})))\n   838\t\n   839\t      (wsj/close-host! ci1)\n   840\t      (wsj/close-host! ci2)\n   841\t      (wsj/close-host! si))\n   842\t\n   843\t    ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   844\t    ;; Fact 2: Killing connection while request in-flight observes request lost\n   845\t    ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   846\t    (let [si (wsj/create)\n   847\t          ci (wsj/create)\n   848\t          port (atom 0)\n   849\t          server-st (atom (serve/serve! {:bind-host \"127.0.0.1\"\n   850\t                                         :bind-port 0\n   851\t                                         :host {:bind! (fn [opts]\n   852\t                                                         (wsj/bind! si (assoc opts :ws.jolt/adapter-of\n   853\t                                                                              #(some-> (:ws/handle %) ws/adapter))))\n   854\t                                                :unbind! (fn [lh dep] (wsj/unbind! si lh dep))\n   855\t                                                :connect! (fn [d a] (wsj/connect! si d a))}}))\n   856\t          _ (loop []\n   857\t              (let [stepped (serve/step @server-st (poller/clock-ms))\n   858\t                    [_ next-st] (serve/take-outbox stepped)]\n   859\t                (reset! server-st next-st)\n   860\t                (when-let [p (get-in next-st [:spec :port])]\n   861\t                  (when (pos? p) (reset! port p)))\n   862\t                (when (zero? @port)\n   863\t                  (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 (wsj/host-pump si) nil)\n   864\t                  (recur))))\n   865\t          url (str \"daostream:ws://127.0.0.1:\" @port \"/repl\")\n   866\t          now (poller/clock-ms)\n   867\t          p-open (connect/open {:url url :host {:connect! (fn [d a] (wsj/connect! ci d a))} :now now})\n   868\t          peer {:connection (atom (connect/connection-key p-open))\n   869\t                :client (atom (connect/client-key p-open))}]\n   870\t\n   871\t      ;; Connect first\n   872\t      (drive-repl-peers! w [si ci] [peer]\n   873\t                         (fn []\n   874\t                           (let [stepped (serve/step @server-st (poller/clock-ms))\n   875\t                                 [_ next-st] (serve/take-outbox stepped)]\n   876\t                             (reset! server-st next-st)\n   877\t                             (remote-channel/opened? (:dial @(:connection peer)))))\n   878\t                         3000)\n   879\t\n   880\t      ;; Stall server driver, send request, and close client connection\n   881\t      (let [c (rpc/request! @(:client peer) 99 :op/eval \"(+ 1 2)\")]\n   882\t        (reset! (:client peer) c)\n   883\t        (swap! (:connection peer) connect/close!)\n   884\t\n   885\t        ;; Drive client until terminal observed\n   886\t        (drive-repl-peers! w [ci] [peer]\n   887\t                           (fn []\n   888\t                             (some? (:terminal @(:client peer))))\n   889\t                           3000)\n   890\t\n   891\t        (let [[conn' ev] (connect/observe-terminal @(:connection peer) (:terminal @(:client peer)))]\n   892\t          (check! \"Fact 2: client observes detached and lost request\"\n   893\t                  (and (= :detached (:status conn'))\n   894\t                       (= :dao.stream.rpc/detached (:terminal @(:client peer))))\n   895\t                  {:conn conn' :ev ev :terminal (:terminal @(:client peer))})))\n   896\t\n   897\t      (wsj/close-host! ci)\n   898\t      (wsj/close-host! si))\n   899\t\n   900\t    ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   901\t    ;; Fact 3: Reattaching resumes served stream and shared shell state survives\n   902\t    ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   903\t    (let [si (wsj/create)\n   904\t          ci (wsj/create)\n   905\t          port (atom 0)\n   906\t          server-st (atom (serve/serve! {:bind-host \"127.0.0.1\"\n   907\t                                         :bind-port 0\n   908\t                                         :host {:bind! (fn [opts]\n   909\t                                                         (wsj/bind! si (assoc opts :ws.jolt/adapter-of\n   910\t                                                                              #(some-> (:ws/handle %) ws/adapter))))\n   911\t                                                :unbind! (fn [lh dep] (wsj/unbind! si lh dep))\n   912\t                                                :connect! (fn [d a] (wsj/connect! si d a))}}))\n   913\t          _ (loop []\n   914\t              (let [stepped (serve/step @server-st (poller/clock-ms))\n   915\t                    [_ next-st] (serve/take-outbox stepped)]\n   916\t                (reset! server-st next-st)\n   917\t                (when-let [p (get-in next-st [:spec :port])]\n   918\t                  (when (pos? p) (reset! port p)))\n   919\t                (when (zero? @port)\n   920\t                  (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 (wsj/host-pump si) nil)\n   921\t                  (recur))))\n   922\t          url (str \"daostream:ws://127.0.0.1:\" @port \"/repl\")\n   923\t          now (poller/clock-ms)\n   924\t          client-host {:connect! (fn [d a] (wsj/connect! ci d a))}\n   925\t          p-open (connect/open {:url url :host client-host :now now})\n   926\t          peer {:connection (atom (connect/connection-key p-open))\n   927\t                :client (atom (connect/client-key p-open))}]\n   928\t\n   929\t      ;; 1. Define x = 10\n   930\t      (let [c (rpc/request! @(:client peer) 10 :op/eval \"(def x 10)\")]\n   931\t        (reset! (:client peer) c)\n   932\t        (drive-repl-peers! w [si ci] [peer]\n   933\t                           (fn []\n   934\t                             (let [stepped (serve/step @server-st (poller/clock-ms))\n   935\t                                   [_ next-st] (serve/take-outbox stepped)]\n   936\t                               (reset! server-st next-st)\n   937\t                               (some? (rpc/response @(:client peer) 10))))\n   938\t                           5000)\n   939\t        (check! \"Fact 3: (def x 10) evaluated\"\n   940\t                (= \"10\" (rpc/answer-ok (rpc/response @(:client peer) 10)))\n   941\t                {:ans (rpc/response @(:client peer) 10)}))\n   942\t\n   943\t      ;; 2. Disconnect and reattach\n   944\t      (swap! (:connection peer) connect/close!)\n   945\t      (drive-repl-peers! w [ci] [peer]\n   946\t                         (fn [] (some? (:terminal @(:client peer))))\n   947\t                         2000)\n   948\t      (let [now' (poller/clock-ms)\n   949\t            reattached (connect/reattach @(:connection peer) @(:client peer) now')]\n   950\t        (reset! (:connection peer) (connect/connection-key reattached))\n   951\t        (reset! (:client peer) (connect/client-key reattached))\n   952\t\n   953\t        ;; 3. Query x on reattached connection\n   954\t        (let [c2 (rpc/request! @(:client peer) 11 :op/eval \"x\")]\n   955\t          (reset! (:client peer) c2)\n   956\t          (drive-repl-peers! w [si ci] [peer]\n   957\t                             (fn []\n   958\t                               (let [stepped (serve/step @server-st (poller/clock-ms))\n   959\t                                     [_ next-st] (serve/take-outbox stepped)]\n   960\t                                 (reset! server-st next-st)\n   961\t                                 (some? (rpc/response @(:client peer) 11))))\n   962\t                             5000)\n   963\t          (check! \"Fact 3: reattached connection reads x = 10\"\n   964\t                  (= \"10\" (rpc/answer-ok (rpc/response @(:client peer) 11)))\n   965\t                  {:ans (rpc/response @(:client peer) 11)})))\n   966\t\n   967\t      (wsj/close-host! ci)\n   968\t      (wsj/close-host! si))\n   969\t\n   970\t    ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   971\t    ;; Fact 4: Stopping endpoint ends served stream (terminal :ended, not :detached)\n   972\t    ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   973\t    (let [si (wsj/create)\n   974\t          ci (wsj/create)\n   975\t          port (atom 0)\n   976\t          server-st (atom (serve/serve! {:bind-host \"127.0.0.1\"\n   977\t                                         :bind-port 0\n   978\t                                         :host {:bind! (fn [opts]\n   979\t                                                         (wsj/bind! si (assoc opts :ws.jolt/adapter-of\n   980\t                                                                              #(some-> (:ws/handle %) ws/adapter))))\n   981\t                                                :unbind! (fn [lh dep] (wsj/unbind! si lh dep))\n   982\t                                                :connect! (fn [d a] (wsj/connect! si d a))}}))\n   983\t          _ (loop []\n   984\t              (let [stepped (serve/step @server-st (poller/clock-ms))\n   985\t                    [_ next-st] (serve/take-outbox stepped)]\n   986\t                (reset! server-st next-st)\n   987\t                (when-let [p (get-in next-st [:spec :port])]\n   988\t                  (when (pos? p) (reset! port p)))\n   989\t                (when (zero? @port)\n   990\t                  (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 (wsj/host-pump si) nil)\n   991\t                  (recur))))\n   992\t          url (str \"daostream:ws://127.0.0.1:\" @port \"/repl\")\n   993\t          now (poller/clock-ms)\n   994\t          client-host {:connect! (fn [d a] (wsj/connect! ci d a))}\n   995\t          p-open (connect/open {:url url :host client-host :now now})\n   996\t          peer {:connection (atom (connect/connection-key p-open))\n   997\t                :client (atom (connect/client-key p-open))}]\n   998\t\n   999\t      ;; Open connection and eval (+ 3 4)\n  1000\t      (let [c (rpc/request! @(:client peer) 7 :op/eval \"(+ 3 4)\")]\n  1001\t        (reset! (:client peer) c)\n  1002\t        (drive-repl-peers! w [si ci] [peer]\n  1003\t                           (fn []\n  1004\t                             (let [stepped (serve/step @server-st (poller/clock-ms))\n  1005\t                                   [_ next-st] (serve/take-outbox stepped)]\n  1006\t                               (reset! server-st next-st)\n  1007\t                               (some? (rpc/response @(:client peer) 7))))\n  1008\t                           5000)\n  1009\t        (check! \"Fact 4: (+ 3 4) evaluates to 7\"\n  1010\t                (= \"7\" (rpc/answer-ok (rpc/response @(:client peer) 7)))\n  1011\t                {:ans (rpc/response @(:client peer) 7)}))\n  1012\t\n  1013\t      ;; Stop endpoint\n  1014\t      (swap! server-st serve/stop!)\n  1015\t      (drive-repl-peers! w [si ci] [peer]\n  1016\t                         (fn []\n  1017\t                           (let [stepped (serve/step @server-st (poller/clock-ms))\n  1018\t                                 [_ next-st] (serve/take-outbox stepped)]\n  1019\t                             (reset! server-st next-st)\n  1020\t                             (and (serve/stopped? next-st)\n  1021\t                                  (some? (:terminal @(:client peer))))))\n  1022\t                         5000)\n  1023\t\n  1024\t      (let [[conn' ev] (connect/observe-terminal @(:connection peer) (:terminal @(:client peer)))]\n  1025\t        (check! \"Fact 4: client observes :ended, not bare detached\"\n  1026\t                (and (= :ended (:status conn'))\n  1027\t                     (= :dao.stream.rpc/ended (:terminal @(:client peer))))\n  1028\t                {:conn conn' :ev ev :terminal (:terminal @(:client peer))}))\n  1029\t\n  1030\t      (wsj/close-host! ci)\n  1031\t      (wsj/close-host! si))\n  1032\t\n  1033\t    (wake/close! w)\n  1034\t    (println)\n  1035\t    (println \"Served-stream rejoin:\" @passed \"passed,\" @failed \"failed\")\n  1036\t    (if (zero? @failed)\n  1037\t      (do (println \"PASS served-stream\") true)\n  1038\t      (do (println \"FAIL served-stream\") false))))\n  1039\t\n  1040\t\n  1041\t;; =============================================================================\n  1042\t;; CLI Dispatcher\n  1043\t;; =============================================================================\n  1044\t\n  1045\t(defn -main\n  1046\t  [& args]\n  1047\t  (when-not (= \"1\" (System/getenv \"JOLT_WORKLOAD_W_SUPERVISED\"))\n  1048\t    (println \"Workload W Results: FAILURE\")\n  1049\t    (println \"Use bb workload-w:jolt so the independent watchdog owns the runtime cap.\")\n  1050\t    (println \"RECORD p99 ABSENT\")\n  1051\t    (println \"RECORD sample count 0\")\n  1052\t    (println \"RECORD elapsed ms 0\")\n  1053\t    (println \"FAIL workload-w\")\n  1054\t    (flush)\n  1055\t    (System/exit 1))\n  1056\t  (let [cmd (or (first args) \"workload-w\")\n  1057\t        ok? (case cmd\n  1058\t              \"workload-w\" (:pass? (run-workload-w))\n  1059\t              \"quick-w\" (:pass? (run-workload-w :target-duration-ms 2000 :target-samples 20))\n  1060\t              \"cross-host\" (run-cross-host-rows)\n  1061\t              \"served-stream\" (run-served-stream-rejoin)\n  1062\t              \"all\" (and (run-cross-host-rows)\n  1063\t                         (run-served-stream-rejoin)\n  1064\t                         (:pass? (run-workload-w)))\n  1065\t              (do (println \"Unknown command:\" cmd\n  1066\t                           \"- valid commands: workload-w, quick-w, cross-host, served-stream, all\")\n  1067\t                  false))]\n  1068\t    (flush)\n  1069\t    (System/exit (if ok? 0 1))))\n  1070\t\n  1071\t(apply -main *command-line-args*)\n     1\t(ns jolt-workload-w-run\n     2\t  \"Independent watchdog and sampler for the single-threaded Workload W worker.\n     3\t   Run with bb workload-w:jolt [workload-w|quick-w|cross-host|served-stream|all].\"\n     4\t  (:require [clojure.edn :as edn]\n     5\t            [clojure.string :as str]))\n     6\t\n     7\t\n     8\t(def hard-cap-ms 300000)\n     9\t(def telemetry-ms 10000)\n    10\t\n    11\t\n    12\t(defn- now-ms\n    13\t  []\n    14\t  (quot (System/nanoTime) 1000000))\n    15\t\n    16\t\n    17\t(defn- p99\n    18\t  [samples]\n    19\t  (when (seq samples)\n    20\t    (nth (sort samples) (min (dec (count samples)) (int (* 0.99 (count samples)))))))\n    21\t\n    22\t\n    23\t(defn- observe-line\n    24\t  [state line]\n    25\t  (if (str/starts-with? line \"W-SAMPLE \")\n    26\t    (let [sample (try (edn/read-string (subs line 9)) (catch Exception _ nil))]\n    27\t      (if (and (number? sample) (<= 0 sample))\n    28\t        (-> state\n    29\t            (update :samples conj sample)\n    30\t            (assoc :last-output-at (now-ms)))\n    31\t        (assoc state :sample-error line)))\n    32\t    (do\n    33\t      (println line)\n    34\t      (flush)\n    35\t      (cond-> (assoc state :last-output-at (now-ms))\n    36\t        (str/starts-with? line \"W-PHASE \") (assoc :phase (subs line 8))\n    37\t        (= line \"FAIL workload-w\") (assoc :reported-failure? true)))))\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\t(defn- read-output\n    41\t  \"Only ready characters, at most 8192 per turn: a partial line or a noisy\n    42\t   worker must not block the watchdog's clock or its ten-second sampler.\"\n    43\t  [reader state]\n    44\t  (let [chunk (StringBuilder.)\n    45\t        eof? (loop [remaining 8192]\n    46\t               (if (and (pos? remaining) (.ready reader))\n    47\t                 (let [c (.read reader)]\n    48\t                   (if (= -1 c)\n    49\t                     true\n    50\t                     (do (.append chunk (char c))\n    51\t                         (recur (dec remaining)))))\n    52\t                 false))\n    53\t        lines (str/split (str (:partial state) chunk) #\"\\n\" -1)]\n    54\t    (assoc (reduce observe-line state (butlast lines))\n    55\t           :partial (last lines) :eof? eof?)))\n    56\t\n    57\t\n    58\t(defn- telemetry!\n    59\t  [state elapsed]\n    60\t  (println \"WATCHDOG TELEMETRY\"\n    61\t           (pr-str {:elapsed-ms elapsed,\n    62\t                    :samples (count (:samples state)),\n    63\t                    :running-p99-ms (or (p99 (:samples state)) \"ABSENT\"),\n    64\t                    :first-round-phase (:phase state),\n    65\t                    :output-age-ms (- (now-ms) (:last-output-at state))}))\n    66\t  (flush))\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\t(defn- failure!\n    70\t  [state elapsed reason]\n    71\t  (println \"Workload W Results: FAILURE\")\n    72\t  (println \"RECORD failure reason\" reason)\n    73\t  (println \"RECORD p99 ABSENT\")\n    74\t  (println \"RECORD sample count\" (count (:samples state)))\n    75\t  (println \"RECORD elapsed ms\" elapsed)\n    76\t  (println \"FAIL workload-w\")\n    77\t  (flush))\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t(defn- kill-tree!\n    81\t  [process]\n    82\t  (let [root (.toHandle process)\n    83\t        tree (conj (vec (iterator-seq (.iterator (.descendants root)))) root)]\n    84\t    ;; Capture descendants before signaling: launcher children may be reparented.\n    85\t    (doseq [handle tree]\n    86\t      (.destroyForcibly handle))))\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t(defn- run-watched\n    90\t  [args]\n    91\t  (let [started (now-ms)\n    92\t        command (into [\"sh\" \"-c\"\n    93\t                       \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_workload_w.clj \\\"$@\\\"\"\n    94\t                       \"jolt\"] args)\n    95\t        builder (ProcessBuilder. ^java.util.List command)\n    96\t        _ (.put (.environment builder) \"JOLT_WORKLOAD_W_SUPERVISED\" \"1\")\n    97\t        _ (.redirectError builder java.lang.ProcessBuilder$Redirect/INHERIT)\n    98\t        process (.start builder)]\n    99\t    (try\n   100\t      (with-open [reader (java.io.BufferedReader.\n   101\t                          (java.io.InputStreamReader. (.getInputStream process) \"UTF-8\"))]\n   102\t        (loop [state {:samples [], :partial \"\", :phase \"loading\", :last-output-at started}\n   103\t               next-telemetry (+ started telemetry-ms)]\n   104\t          (let [state (read-output reader state)\n   105\t                now (now-ms)\n   106\t                elapsed (- now started)]\n   107\t            (when (>= now next-telemetry)\n   108\t              (telemetry! state elapsed))\n   109\t            (cond\n   110\t              (:sample-error state)\n   111\t              (do\n   112\t                (kill-tree! process)\n   113\t                (failure! state elapsed :invalid-sample)\n   114\t                1)\n   115\t\n   116\t              (>= elapsed hard-cap-ms)\n   117\t              (do\n   118\t                (kill-tree! process)\n   119\t                (failure! state elapsed :hard-cap)\n   120\t                1)\n   121\t\n   122\t              (not (.isAlive process))\n   123\t              ;; Drain already-buffered output without waiting for another line.\n   124\t              (if (and (not (:eof? state)) (.ready reader))\n   125\t                (recur state next-telemetry)\n   126\t                (let [state (if (str/blank? (:partial state))\n   127\t                              state\n   128\t                              (observe-line state (:partial state)))\n   129\t                      status (.exitValue process)]\n   130\t                  (when (and (not (zero? status)) (not (:reported-failure? state)))\n   131\t                    (failure! state elapsed :worker-failure))\n   132\t                  status))\n   133\t\n   134\t              :else\n   135\t              (do\n   136\t                (Thread/sleep 10)\n   137\t                (recur state (if (>= now next-telemetry)\n   138\t                               (+ now telemetry-ms)\n   139\t                               next-telemetry)))))))\n   140\t      (finally\n   141\t        (when (.isAlive process) (kill-tree! process))))))\n   142\t\n   143\t\n   144\t(System/exit (run-watched *command-line-args*))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/jolt.jolt && rg -n 'owner|round|sleep-fds|deadline|pump' src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/jolt.jolt && rg -n 'owner|round|sleep-fds|deadline|pump' src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.stream.ws.jolt\n     2\t  \"The jolt host edge for the DaoStream v2 WebSocket transport (J6e; J6\n     3\t   plan rulings A1-A6 and the J6e design rulings R1-R7): a dialer and a\n     4\t   listener over the owner-thread pump (`dao.stream.ws.pump`) and the\n     5\t   nonblocking TCP substrate (`dao.stream.ws.tcp`), the HTTP upgrade from\n     6\t   the pure `dao.stream.ws.upgrade` core, and frames from the pure\n     7\t   `dao.stream.ws.rfc6455` core with jolt's SHA-1 and masking entropy\n     8\t   (`dao.stream.ws.crypto`).\n     9\t\n    10\t   One instance per `create` call. Its pump registry, connection records\n    11\t   and listener records live in that instance and nowhere else; two\n    12\t   instances never share state. Nothing here waits, parks or polls: the\n    13\t   instance makes progress only while a driver polls `(host-pump instance)`\n    14\t   and hands it readiness (A1, A2).\n    15\t\n    16\t   Seams. `connect!` and a listener's `accept!` get the raw-socket seam\n    17\t   `{:send! :close! :queued-bytes}` (the server's also `:ws/subprotocol`).\n    18\t   `send!` frames a string as text and host bytes as binary and answers nil\n    19\t   or `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}`, never false: the\n    20\t   transport decides `full` from `:queued-bytes`, which counts every wire\n    21\t   byte not yet accepted by the kernel. `close!` answers nil. Callbacks into\n    22\t   the composition use the `dao.stream.ws/adapter` key shape (`:opened!`\n    23\t   `:message!` `:binary!` `:closed!` `:too-large!`, plus `:ws/codec` and\n    24\t   `:ws/max-frame-bytes` on the dialer's map).\n    25\t\n    26\t   Terminals (R6). Each upgraded connection reports exactly one\n    27\t   `(:closed! code reason)`, from the pump's owed terminal, never inside\n    28\t   `send!` or `close!`; a parser failure over the message bound (1009)\n    29\t   calls `:too-large!` first. Before its upgrade completes a dialed\n    30\t   connection has no frames: every failure there (refused connect, a\n    31\t   refused or invalid 101, an unsolicited extension, an oversized head, the\n    32\t   upgrade deadline, end of stream) is one `:closed! 1006\n    33\t   \\\"dao.stream/connect-failed\\\"`, and a transport `close!` then discards\n    34\t   the socket and reports its own code. A pre-upgrade server socket has no\n    35\t   composition handle: a refused upgrade answers its HTTP status and\n    36\t   deposits one `:upgrade-failed`.\n    37\t\n    38\t   Policies (A4). Head 8 KiB (incremental), 64 pending upgrades per\n    39\t   listener with accept paused at the cap, a 10 s upgrade deadline and a\n    40\t   5 s close deadline (both overridable per instance and per listener),\n    41\t   the pump's 64 KiB read chunk and 16-pong control budget. The pong budget\n    42\t   can stall a peer that pings faster than its socket drains, by design and\n    43\t   bounded. A ping that arrives once a local close is queued gets no pong:\n    44\t   the pong would queue behind our close frame, RFC 6455 section 5.5.1\n    45\t   forbids only data frames after a close, and no Autobahn case exercises\n    46\t   it. This side sends no unsolicited pings and ignores pongs.\n    47\t\n    48\t   Addresses are IPv4 or IPv6 literals or `localhost` (A8): any other host\n    49\t   name, and a descriptor naming the `wss` scheme, makes `connect!` answer\n    50\t   nil, which the attacher reports as a transport error. Nothing resolves.\n    51\t\n    52\t   Shutdown (A6). `unbind!` closes the listener at once, discards the\n    53\t   sockets it owns that are still upgrading, closes 1001 any upgraded one\n    54\t   nobody has closed yet, and lowers every owned connection's close\n    55\t   deadline to within `unbind-grace-ms`; the listener's `:stopped` is\n    56\t   deposited once its last owned connection has ended. `close-host!` is\n    57\t   forced cleanup after the owner loop has ended: every descriptor closed,\n    58\t   every buffer released, no deposit and no callback.\n    59\t\n    60\t   Clocks (R7). Pump deadlines are monotonic (`jolt.io-poller/clock-ms`);\n    61\t   the `now` handed to `accept!` is wall-clock milliseconds, the domain the\n    62\t   endpoint's acceptance expiry compares against.\"\n    63\t  (:require\n    64\t    [dao.host.text :as text]\n    65\t    [dao.stream.codec :as codec]\n    66\t    [dao.stream.ws.crypto :as crypto]\n    67\t    [dao.stream.ws.pump :as pump]\n    68\t    [dao.stream.ws.rfc6455 :as rfc6455]\n    69\t    [dao.stream.ws.tcp :as tcp]\n    70\t    [dao.stream.ws.upgrade :as upgrade]\n    71\t    [jolt.io-poller :as poller]))\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t(def unbind-grace-ms\n    75\t  \"How long connections a stopped listener owns may drain (A6): strictly\n    76\t   below the remote channel's 2000 ms stop grace, so `:stopped` precedes\n    77\t   its unconfirmed verdict.\"\n    78\t  1500)\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\t(def ^:private ok {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})\n    82\t(def ^:private transport-error {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error})\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\t(def ^:private connect-failed \"dao.stream/connect-failed\")\n    86\t\n    87\t\n    88\t;; =============================================================================\n    89\t;; Instance\n    90\t;; =============================================================================\n    91\t\n    92\t(defn create\n    93\t  \"A fresh instance with an empty registry. `opts`: `:upgrade-timeout-ms`\n    94\t   and `:close-deadline-ms` override the pump defaults for every connection\n    95\t   this instance makes (a listener's own options take precedence).\"\n    96\t  ([] (create nil))\n    97\t  ([opts]\n    98\t   {::pump (pump/create)\n    99\t    ::opts (select-keys opts [:upgrade-timeout-ms :close-deadline-ms])\n   100\t    ::state (atom {:closed? false\n   101\t                   :owed []           ; thunks for the start or end of a turn\n   102\t                   :conns #{}         ; connection records (atoms), live\n   103\t                   :listeners {}      ; listener id -> listener record (atom)\n   104\t                   :unbind-closed 0})}))\n   105\t\n   106\t\n   107\t(defn- st\n   108\t  [inst]\n   109\t  (::state inst))\n   110\t\n   111\t\n   112\t(defn- live?\n   113\t  [inst]\n   114\t  (not (:closed? @(st inst))))\n   115\t\n   116\t\n   117\t(defn- gated\n   118\t  \"`f` as a pump callback that does nothing once the instance is closed:\n   119\t   `close-host!` flushes owed pump reports through it without reaching the\n   120\t   composition.\"\n   121\t  [inst f]\n   122\t  (fn [& args]\n   123\t    (when (live? inst) (apply f args))))\n   124\t\n   125\t\n   126\t(defn- owe!\n   127\t  \"Queue thunk `f` for the start or end of the next turn, outside any entry\n   128\t   the composition is in.\"\n   129\t  [inst f]\n   130\t  (swap! (st inst) update :owed conj f)\n   131\t  nil)\n   132\t\n   133\t\n   134\t(defn- deliver-owed!\n   135\t  [inst]\n   136\t  (let [owed (:owed @(st inst))]\n   137\t    (swap! (st inst) assoc :owed [])\n   138\t    (doseq [f owed] (when (live? inst) (f)))\n   139\t    (boolean (seq owed))))\n   140\t\n   141\t\n   142\t(defn- forget!\n   143\t  [inst c]\n   144\t  (swap! (st inst) update :conns disj c)\n   145\t  nil)\n   146\t\n   147\t\n   148\t(defn host-pump\n   149\t  \"The instance as the driver's `:pump` value (A2): the pump's interest and\n   150\t   deadline (now while this edge owes a report), and `pump!`.\"\n   151\t  [inst]\n   152\t  (let [p (::pump inst)]\n   153\t    {:interest #(pump/interest p)\n   154\t     :deadline #(if (seq (:owed @(st inst))) (poller/clock-ms) (pump/next-deadline p))\n   155\t     :pump! (fn [ready]\n   156\t              (let [before? (deliver-owed! inst)\n   157\t                    r (pump/pump! p ready)\n   158\t                    after? (deliver-owed! inst)]\n   159\t                {:progressed? (boolean (or before? (:progressed? r) after?))}))}))\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t;; =============================================================================\n   163\t;; Frames\n   164\t;; =============================================================================\n   165\t\n   166\t(defn- protocol\n   167\t  \"The pump's protocol map for `role` (:server or :client), whose parser\n   168\t   bounds a message at `max` bytes (nil is unbounded). Client frames are\n   169\t   masked with a fresh key each.\"\n   170\t  [role max]\n   171\t  (cond-> {:parser (rfc6455/parser {:role role, :max-message-bytes max})\n   172\t           :parse-frame rfc6455/parse-frame\n   173\t           :encode-frame rfc6455/encode-frame\n   174\t           :close-payload rfc6455/close-payload}\n   175\t    (= :client role) (assoc :mask-key crypto/mask-key)))\n   176\t\n   177\t\n   178\t(defn- data-frame\n   179\t  \"The wire bytes of one message: a string as a text frame, host bytes as a\n   180\t   binary frame; masked for the client role.\"\n   181\t  [role payload]\n   182\t  (rfc6455/encode-frame\n   183\t    (cond-> (if (string? payload)\n   184\t              {:opcode :text, :payload (text/utf8-encode payload)}\n   185\t              {:opcode :binary, :payload payload})\n   186\t      (= :client role) (assoc :mask-key (crypto/mask-key)))))\n   187\t\n   188\t\n   189\t(defn- deliver-message!\n   190\t  [cb ev]\n   191\t  (when cb\n   192\t    (let [payload (:payload ev)]\n   193\t      (if (= :text (:opcode ev))\n   194\t        ((:message! cb) (text/utf8-decode payload 0 (alength payload)))\n   195\t        ((:binary! cb) payload)))))\n   196\t\n   197\t\n   198\t(defn- report-closed!\n   199\t  \"The one terminal of an upgraded connection, from the pump's owed\n   200\t   `:on-closed`.\"\n   201\t  [cb {:keys [code reason cause]}]\n   202\t  (when cb\n   203\t    (when (and (= :fail cause) (= 1009 code))\n   204\t      ((:too-large! cb)))\n   205\t    ((:closed! cb) code reason)))\n   206\t\n   207\t\n   208\t(defn- seam\n   209\t  \"The raw-socket seam over connection record `c`, whose role frames\n   210\t   outbound messages.\"\n   211\t  [p c role]\n   212\t  {:send! (fn [payload]\n   213\t            (let [{:keys [phase h]} @c]\n   214\t              (if (= :open phase)\n   215\t                (pump/send! p h (data-frame role payload))\n   216\t                pump/closed-outcome)))\n   217\t   :close! (fn [code reason]\n   218\t             (let [{:keys [phase h]} @c]\n   219\t               (when (= :open phase) (pump/close! p h code reason)))\n   220\t             nil)\n   221\t   :queued-bytes #(if-let [h (:h @c)] (pump/queued-bytes h) 0)})\n   222\t\n   223\t\n   224\t;; =============================================================================\n   225\t;; Dialer\n   226\t;; =============================================================================\n   227\t\n   228\t(defn- random-key\n   229\t  \"A Sec-WebSocket-Key: sixteen CSPRNG bytes, four masking-key draws.\"\n   230\t  []\n   231\t  (let [out (byte-array 16)]\n   232\t    (dotimes [i 4]\n   233\t      (let [k (crypto/mask-key)]\n   234\t        (dotimes [j 4] (aset out (+ (* 4 i) j) (aget k j)))))\n   235\t    (upgrade/client-key out)))\n   236\t\n   237\t\n   238\t(defn- client-failed!\n   239\t  \"End dialed connection `c` before its upgrade: socket released, one\n   240\t   `:closed!` (`code`, `reason`).\"\n   241\t  [inst c code reason]\n   242\t  (let [{:keys [phase h cb]} @c]\n   243\t    (when-not (= :closed phase)\n   244\t      (swap! c assoc :phase :closed)\n   245\t      (when h (pump/discard! (::pump inst) h))\n   246\t      (forget! inst c)\n   247\t      ((:closed! cb) code reason))))\n   248\t\n   249\t\n   250\t(defn- client-request!\n   251\t  \"Send the upgrade request on dialed connection `c` once it is connected.\n   252\t   A failed write is reported by the pump through `:on-error`.\"\n   253\t  [inst c]\n   254\t  (let [{:keys [h request]} @c]\n   255\t    (swap! c assoc :phase :upgrading)\n   256\t    (pump/send! (::pump inst) h (text/utf8-encode request))\n   257\t    nil))\n   258\t\n   259\t\n   260\t(defn- client-head!\n   261\t  \"Response head bytes on dialed connection `c`.\"\n   262\t  [inst c chunk]\n   263\t  (when (= :upgrading (:phase @c))\n   264\t    (let [{:keys [head-parser key offered h cb]} @c\n   265\t          [hp result] (upgrade/head-feed head-parser chunk)]\n   266\t      (swap! c assoc :head-parser hp)\n   267\t      (cond\n   268\t        (nil? result) nil\n   269\t        (:refused result) (client-failed! inst c 1006 connect-failed)\n   270\t        :else\n   271\t        (let [verdict (upgrade/check-response (upgrade/parse-response (:head result))\n   272\t                                              {:key key, :offered offered, :sha1 crypto/sha1})]\n   273\t          (if (not= :ok (:outcome verdict))\n   274\t            (client-failed! inst c 1006 connect-failed)\n   275\t            (do (pump/upgraded! (::pump inst) h (protocol :client (:ws/max-frame-bytes cb))\n   276\t                                (:rest result))\n   277\t                (swap! c assoc :phase :open)\n   278\t                ((:opened! cb)))))))))\n   279\t\n   280\t\n   281\t(defn- secure?\n   282\t  [descriptor]\n   283\t  (= \"wss\" (:ws/scheme descriptor)))\n   284\t\n   285\t\n   286\t(defn connect!\n   287\t  \"Start dialing `descriptor` (`:ws/host` a literal or localhost, `:ws/port`,\n   288\t   `:ws/path`) with composition callbacks `cb` (the `dao.stream.ws/adapter`\n   289\t   shape; `:ws/codec` names the one subprotocol offered, none without it).\n   290\t   Never waits. Answers the seam, or nil for an address this host does not\n   291\t   dial (a host name, the wss scheme) or a closed instance. The upgrade\n   292\t   request is built, and an invalid field refused (thrown), before any\n   293\t   socket exists. A connect that fails reports its one `:closed!` on a later\n   294\t   turn.\"\n   295\t  [inst descriptor cb]\n   296\t  (let [p (::pump inst)\n   297\t        addr (tcp/parse-address (:ws/host descriptor) (:ws/port descriptor))]\n   298\t    (when (and (live? inst) (not (secure? descriptor)) (not (:error addr)))\n   299\t      (let [offered (if-let [c (:ws/codec cb)] [(codec/codec-name c)] [])\n   300\t            key (random-key)\n   301\t            {:keys [head]} (upgrade/client-request {:host (:ws/host descriptor)\n   302\t                                                    :port (:ws/port descriptor)\n   303\t                                                    :path (:ws/path descriptor)\n   304\t                                                    :key key\n   305\t                                                    :subprotocols offered})\n   306\t            c (atom {:phase :connecting, :role :client, :cb cb, :offered offered\n   307\t                     :key key, :request head, :head-parser (upgrade/head-parser)})\n   308\t            r (tcp/connect! addr)]\n   309\t        (if (:error r)\n   310\t          (do (swap! c assoc :phase :closed)\n   311\t              (owe! inst #((:closed! cb) 1006 connect-failed)))\n   312\t          (let [opts (::opts inst)\n   313\t                fail #(client-failed! inst c 1006 connect-failed)\n   314\t                h (pump/connection!\n   315\t                    p (:fd r)\n   316\t                    (cond-> {:connecting? (= :connecting (:state r))\n   317\t                             :upgrading? true\n   318\t                             :on-connected (gated inst #(client-request! inst c))\n   319\t                             :on-data (gated inst #(client-head! inst c %))\n   320\t                             :on-eof (gated inst fail)\n   321\t                             :on-error (gated inst (fn [_] (fail)))\n   322\t                             :on-upgrade-expired (gated inst fail)\n   323\t                             :on-message (gated inst #(deliver-message! cb %))\n   324\t                             :on-closed (gated inst (fn [t]\n   325\t                                                      (swap! c assoc :phase :closed)\n   326\t                                                      (forget! inst c)\n   327\t                                                      (report-closed! cb t)))}\n   328\t                      (:upgrade-timeout-ms opts) (assoc :upgrade-timeout-ms (:upgrade-timeout-ms opts))\n   329\t                      (:close-deadline-ms opts) (assoc :close-deadline-ms (:close-deadline-ms opts))))]\n   330\t            (swap! c assoc :h h)\n   331\t            (swap! (st inst) update :conns conj c)\n   332\t            (when (= :connected (:state r))\n   333\t              (client-request! inst c))))\n   334\t        (assoc (seam p c :client)\n   335\t               :close! (fn [code reason]\n   336\t                         (let [{:keys [phase h]} @c]\n   337\t                           (case phase\n   338\t                             :open (pump/close! p h code reason)\n   339\t                             :closed nil\n   340\t                             ;; before the upgrade: no frame exists to close with\n   341\t                             (do (swap! c assoc :phase :closed)\n   342\t                                 (when h (pump/discard! p h))\n   343\t                                 (forget! inst c)\n   344\t                                 (owe! inst #((:closed! cb) code reason)))))\n   345\t                         nil))))))\n   346\t\n   347\t\n   348\t;; =============================================================================\n   349\t;; Listener\n   350\t;; =============================================================================\n   351\t\n   352\t(def ^:private failure-text\n   353\t  {:yin.repl.endpoint/subprotocol-required \"the WebSocket upgrade offered no supported subprotocol\"\n   354\t   :yin.repl.endpoint/websocket-required \"the request was not a WebSocket upgrade\"\n   355\t   :yin.repl.endpoint/bad-request \"the WebSocket upgrade request was invalid\"\n   356\t   :yin.repl.endpoint/head-too-large \"the WebSocket upgrade head exceeded 8 KiB\"\n   357\t   :yin.repl.endpoint/upgrade-expired \"the WebSocket upgrade did not complete in time\"\n   358\t   :yin.repl.endpoint/upgrade-threw \"the host failed while accepting an upgrade\"\n   359\t   :yin.repl.endpoint/socket-error \"the socket failed before the upgrade completed\"})\n   360\t\n   361\t\n   362\t(defn- upgrade-failed!\n   363\t  [lrec code]\n   364\t  ((:deposit! (:opts @lrec)) :upgrade-failed {:code code, :message (failure-text code)}))\n   365\t\n   366\t\n   367\t(defn- refusal-code\n   368\t  \"The `:upgrade-failed` code of an upgrade refusal (`server-response`\n   369\t   reason or a `head-feed` refusal).\"\n   370\t  [reason]\n   371\t  (case reason\n   372\t    :subprotocol :yin.repl.endpoint/subprotocol-required\n   373\t    (:connection :upgrade) :yin.repl.endpoint/websocket-required\n   374\t    :head-too-large :yin.repl.endpoint/head-too-large\n   375\t    :yin.repl.endpoint/bad-request))\n   376\t\n   377\t\n   378\t(defn- refusal-head\n   379\t  \"The refusal response for `status`, with the dao.stream reason as a plain\n   380\t   text body where the JVM edge sends one.\"\n   381\t  [status code]\n   382\t  (let [body (case code\n   383\t               :yin.repl.endpoint/subprotocol-required \"dao.stream/subprotocol-required\"\n   384\t               :yin.repl.endpoint/websocket-required \"dao.stream/websocket-required\"\n   385\t               nil)]\n   386\t    (if body\n   387\t      (str \"HTTP/1.1 \" status \" Bad Request\\r\\n\"\n   388\t           \"Connection: close\\r\\nContent-Type: text/plain\\r\\n\"\n   389\t           \"Content-Length: \" (alength (text/utf8-encode body)) \"\\r\\n\\r\\n\" body)\n   390\t      (upgrade/refusal-response status))))\n   391\t\n   392\t\n   393\t(defn- refuse!\n   394\t  \"Answer a refused upgrade on raw connection `c` with `status`, deposit one\n   395\t   `:upgrade-failed`, and release the socket once the response is written.\"\n   396\t  [inst lrec c status code]\n   397\t  (let [p (::pump inst)\n   398\t        h (:h @c)]\n   399\t    (swap! c assoc :phase :refusing)\n   400\t    (pump/set-reading! p h false)\n   401\t    (upgrade-failed! lrec code)\n   402\t    (pump/send! p h (text/utf8-encode (refusal-head status code)))\n   403\t    (when (and (pump/open? h) (zero? (pump/queued-bytes h)))\n   404\t      (swap! c assoc :phase :closed)\n   405\t      (pump/discard! p h)\n   406\t      (forget! inst c))))\n   407\t\n   408\t\n   409\t(defn- accept-upgrade!\n   410\t  \"A complete, accepted upgrade on raw connection `c`: the 101 is queued, the\n   411\t   connection turns :ws, and the composition's `accept!` gets its seam.\"\n   412\t  [inst lrec c request response rest]\n   413\t  (let [p (::pump inst)\n   414\t        h (:h @c)\n   415\t        {:keys [accept! adapter-of max-frame]} @lrec\n   416\t        subprotocol (some-> (:subprotocol response) codec/codec-name)]\n   417\t    (if (pump/send! p h (text/utf8-encode (:response response)))\n   418\t      ;; the 101 could not be written: the pump reports :on-error\n   419\t      nil\n   420\t      (do (pump/upgraded! p h (protocol :server max-frame) rest)\n   421\t          (swap! c assoc :phase :open)\n   422\t          (let [target (or (upgrade/canonical-path (:target request)) (:target request))\n   423\t                result (try (accept! target (assoc (seam p c :server) :ws/subprotocol subprotocol)\n   424\t                                     (System/currentTimeMillis))\n   425\t                            (catch Throwable _ ::threw))]\n   426\t            (if (= ::threw result)\n   427\t              (do (upgrade-failed! lrec :yin.repl.endpoint/upgrade-threw)\n   428\t                  (pump/close! p h 1011 \"dao.stream/upgrade-failed\"))\n   429\t              (swap! c assoc :cb (adapter-of result))))))))\n   430\t\n   431\t\n   432\t(defn- server-head!\n   433\t  \"Request head bytes on raw connection `c`.\"\n   434\t  [inst lrec c chunk]\n   435\t  (when (= :upgrading (:phase @c))\n   436\t    (let [[hp result] (upgrade/head-feed (:head-parser @c) chunk)]\n   437\t      (swap! c assoc :head-parser hp :seen? true)\n   438\t      (cond\n   439\t        (nil? result) nil\n   440\t        (= :head-too-large (:refused result)) (refuse! inst lrec c 431 :yin.repl.endpoint/head-too-large)\n   441\t        (:refused result) (refuse! inst lrec c 400 :yin.repl.endpoint/bad-request)\n   442\t        :else\n   443\t        (let [request (upgrade/parse-request (:head result))\n   444\t              response (upgrade/server-response request {:sha1 crypto/sha1\n   445\t                                                         :codecs (:codecs (:opts @lrec))})]\n   446\t          (if (= :refuse (:outcome response))\n   447\t            (let [code (refusal-code (:reason response))]\n   448\t              (refuse! inst lrec c (:status response) code))\n   449\t            (accept-upgrade! inst lrec c request response (:rest result))))))))\n   450\t\n   451\t\n   452\t(defn- server-pre-failed!\n   453\t  \"A raw server socket ended before its upgrade completed: released, and\n   454\t   one `:upgrade-failed` with `code` unless nothing was ever received.\"\n   455\t  [inst lrec c code]\n   456\t  (let [{:keys [phase h seen?]} @c]\n   457\t    (when (#{:upgrading :refusing} phase)\n   458\t      (swap! c assoc :phase :closed)\n   459\t      (pump/discard! (::pump inst) h)\n   460\t      (forget! inst c)\n   461\t      (when (and (= :upgrading phase) (or seen? (= code :yin.repl.endpoint/upgrade-expired)))\n   462\t        (upgrade-failed! lrec code)))))\n   463\t\n   464\t\n   465\t(defn- accepted!\n   466\t  \"Listener `lrec` accepted `{:fd :peer}`: register it upgrading.\"\n   467\t  [inst lrec {:keys [fd]}]\n   468\t  (let [p (::pump inst)\n   469\t        c (atom {:phase :upgrading, :role :server, :head-parser (upgrade/head-parser)\n   470\t                 :listener (:id (:lh @lrec))})\n   471\t        close-ms (or (:close-deadline-ms @lrec) (:close-deadline-ms (::opts inst)))\n   472\t        h (pump/connection!\n   473\t            p fd\n   474\t            (cond-> {:listener (:lh @lrec)\n   475\t                     :upgrading? true\n   476\t                     :on-data (gated inst #(server-head! inst lrec c %))\n   477\t                     :on-eof (gated inst #(server-pre-failed! inst lrec c :yin.repl.endpoint/socket-error))\n   478\t                     :on-error (gated inst (fn [_]\n   479\t                                             (server-pre-failed! inst lrec c\n   480\t                                                                 :yin.repl.endpoint/socket-error)))\n   481\t                     :on-upgrade-expired (gated inst #(server-pre-failed! inst lrec c\n   482\t                                                                          :yin.repl.endpoint/upgrade-expired))\n   483\t                     ;; a refusal's response written: release the socket\n   484\t                     :on-drained (gated inst #(when (= :refusing (:phase @c))\n   485\t                                                (swap! c assoc :phase :closed)\n   486\t                                                (pump/discard! p (:h @c))\n   487\t                                                (forget! inst c)))\n   488\t                     :on-message (gated inst #(deliver-message! (:cb @c) %))\n   489\t                     :on-closed (gated inst (fn [t]\n   490\t                                              (swap! c assoc :phase :closed)\n   491\t                                              (forget! inst c)\n   492\t                                              (rep