e/jolt-parser/jolt_parser.cpp, src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt, src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/parser.cljc, the pinned runtime headers the ruling cites (build/native/src/antlr4-cpp-runtime-4.13.2: Parser.h:273-296, ParserATNSimulator.h:776-793, tree/ParseTree.h, support/CPPUtils.h:23). The ruling is binding: do not re-derive the mechanism; if a runtime fact it relies on proves false when you build it, STOP that part and report with evidence (the orchestrator mobs the Architect). Own: native/jolt-parser/**, src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt, src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/parser.cljc (+ its consumers cst_export_test.cljc and dev probes the ruling names), src/dev/jolt_j5_*.clj, bb.edn jolt-j5 tasks, spec §7.6/§10.1, known-gaps row 59 (reopen/close IN PLACE under the union rule; never rewrite the file) and the survivors row, test files for C1-C11. Constraints: ws/pump/crypto files belong to the J6 worktrees, do not touch. No fallback parser, no grammar change, pins untouched. Do NOT stage or commit. Do NOT cite collab/ paths in any design doc or ledger text (owner rule: collab is ephemeral; cite only repository paths or archive/ paths). Run focused tests and the crash-capable legs in child processes in the FOREGROUND only (max timeouts); on this laptop run the budget/crash legs C1-C6 (macOS arm64 is required again for the new mechanism); the long lanes, sanitizer (C5) and Linux legs are the orchestrator's on shiva/jupiter: list exactly the commands. Keep local runs light (owner asked to reduce laptop load: one lane at a time). Begin the final response with Completed-GMT / Completed-Local / Coding-Agent: claude / Session-ID: a5c84655-a61f-4a23-9732-4d1bf8e23f3d, then changed files, exact outcomes with counts per C item (met / unmet / not run and why), concerns.\ncollab/jolt/1793140000000-architect-j4d-cosign.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:10:- **P2 | [src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:186](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:186) | Evidence:** Invalid UTF-8 in a key file throws before `load-key` constructs its path-bearing refusal. `fs.cljc:89` delegates directly to `text/utf8-decode`, whose error at `text.jolt:284` contains no path. This remains fail-closed and exposes no seed, but misses the documented path diagnostic. The new test at `main_test.cljc:459` covers malformed EDN, not malformed bytes. **Concrete fix:** wrap read/decode failures with a sanitized key-file refusal containing `:path`, and add an invalid-UTF-8 fixture.\ncollab/jolt/1793140000000-architect-j4d-cosign.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:12:- **P2 | [native/jolt-file/probes/run.clj:587](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/native/jolt-file/probes/run.clj:587) | Evidence:** The `--no-state` probe runs after `--reset` saved an empty configuration and supplies its store explicitly. It therefore cannot distinguish “never read state” from “read state, then override it.” The unit test at `state_test.cljc:187` similarly overrides the saved VM. Production code correctly bypasses loading at `main.cljc:844–849`; this is a coverage gap. **Concrete fix:** place malformed state on disk, start with `--no-state`, and assert successful startup plus byte-identical state afterward.\ncollab/jolt/1793144000000-engineer-j6a-fixes.prompt.md:1:Resume J6a. The independent reviewer (codex/luna, raw log collab/luna-review.jsonl; final message is the last agent_message) found two P2s; the orchestrator agrees with both:\ncollab/jolt/1793145000000-reviewer-j6a-confirm.gpt-6-luna.prompt.md:10:Resume session 01a17f2a-09b7-7d90-bba9-ae94d6d17eac for the J6a diff in /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-jolt-j6a (git -C /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-jolt-j6a diff). The orchestrator independently checked your two P2s: (1) rxFrameStats truthiness — agree; the engineer now validates dict/str keys/non-negative non-bool int counts and added null/false/-1/\"1\" fixtures; (2) stale \"reject extension offers\" — agree; reworded in all 216 N/A reasons in cases.json and triage.md, pin.json recomputed, README command fixed. Orchestrator reran: unittest 9 OK; harness.py check 517/6/301. Re-read only the relevant lines, challenge these conclusions, recompute the sha256 pins. Do not edit.\ncollab/jolt/1792427226000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r7.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:138:| `dao.stream.datagram.jvm` / UDP / P2P-DHT (J7) | Do not load the JVM socket namespace on jolt. J0 first probes the small raw-transport addition on the existing `jolt.socket.native` FFI/poller groundwork (R; §6.1). J7 owns the larger datagram-contract and DHT integration effort, not discovery of whether C UDP is callable. Implement the datagram host seam via that narrow nonblocking POSIX socket adapter/FFI, preserving bound/send-failed/closed events, maximum datagram policy, IPv4/IPv6, and host-composed deposit medium. Existing `datagram.cljc` supplies semantics with the landed send-error behavior tested in §6.1 and retained by owner Q7. Do not silently add reliability or queues beneath it. P2P/DHT is explicitly outside the first local-lane cut. It becomes a full-parity gate, not a hidden skip. |\ncollab/jolt/1792427226000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r7.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:355:| R8 | Accepted | §7/J0c/J5 observe buffering and match first-failure/probe :end/:early/nil corpus; cst.clj:168–221 verified, C++ behavior untested. |\ncollab/jolt/1792427226000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r7.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:356:| R9 | Accepted | §6.1/J0b: N=1200 and larger configured N, target constants/limits recorded, EMSGSIZE distinguished from truncation. Default verified at datagram.cljc:55–60,317; platform values remain R pending check. |\ncollab/jolt/1793199000001-engineer-j5b-round2-resume.prompt.md:10:Resume J5b round 2 in /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-j5b: continue and complete collab/1793196000000-engineer-j5b-round2.prompt.md (in this worktree) with the Architect's binding rulings in collab/fable-j5b-rulings.md. Your log was empty: check git status and the tree to see which of A1, the reclassified legs, the doc/ledger edits D1-D9 you already made (18 files changed), do not redo finished work, finish the rest, run the macOS legs one lane at a time in the foreground, and end with the report the original brief asks for (changed files, per-C-item met/unmet/not run, the Linux commands for the orchestrator, the placeholder line in section 7.6 Platforms). Constraints unchanged (no stage/commit, no collab/ cites in docs or ledger, no bb test:jolt-j5 on the laptop). Begin with Completed-GMT / Completed-Local / Coding-Agent / Session-ID lines.\ncollab/jolt/1792424621000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r4.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:132:| `dao.stream.datagram.jvm` / UDP / P2P-DHT (J7) | Do not load the JVM socket namespace on jolt. J0 first probes the small raw-transport addition on the existing `jolt.socket.native` FFI/poller groundwork (R; §6.1). J7 owns the larger datagram-contract and DHT integration effort, not discovery of whether C UDP is callable. Implement the datagram host seam via that narrow nonblocking POSIX socket adapter/FFI, preserving bound/send-failed/closed events, maximum datagram policy, IPv4/IPv6, and host-composed deposit medium. Existing `datagram.cljc` supplies semantics except for the owner-requested backpressure mapping discrepancy identified in §6.1, which must be reconciled before production integration. Do not silently add reliability or queues beneath it. P2P/DHT is explicitly outside the first local-lane cut. It becomes a full-parity gate, not a hidden skip. |\ncollab/jolt/1793143000000-reviewer-j6a-policy-repin.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:6:- **P2 | `tools/jolt-autobahn/harness.py:130`** | The Pong check uses truthiness, so malformed evidence such as `rxFrameStats: {\"10\": null}` or `{\"10\": false}` passes. The missing-field fixture is covered, but malformed count values are not. | Validate the stats map’s keys and nonnegative integer counts (excluding booleans); add negative fixtures for null and false counts.\ncollab/jolt/1793143000000-reviewer-j6a-policy-repin.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:7:- **P2 | `tools/jolt-autobahn/triage.md:312`, `tools/jolt-autobahn/cases.json:2962`** | Compression N/A reasons still say “reject extension offers,” contradicting the amendment’s “ignore offers, negotiate none” policy and the updated README and §9.6. The stale wording repeats across the N/A rows. | Update the N/A reasons in both inventories to describe ignored offers and no negotiation; refresh the pin hash.\ncollab/jolt/1792421958748-architect-jolt-lane-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:128:| `dao.stream.datagram.jvm` / UDP / P2P-DHT (J7) | Do not load the JVM socket namespace on jolt. Implement the existing datagram host seam via a narrow nonblocking POSIX socket adapter/FFI, preserving bound/send-failed/closed events, maximum datagram policy, IPv4/IPv6, and host-composed deposit medium. Existing `datagram.cljc` contract supplies semantics; do not add reliability or queues beneath it. P2P/DHT is explicitly outside the first local-lane cut. It becomes a full-parity gate, not a hidden skip. |\ncollab/jolt/1792412960461-engineer-jolt-yin-repl-spike.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:87:5. The ~15 interop-heavy files that were not exercised (`file`, `store/fs`, `btree`, `linker/sign`, datagram): either `:jolt` branches or `jolt.ffi` for sockets. This is the unknown part: sign needs ed25519, and the networking stack (ws/UDP, P2P NAT traversal) is jolt FFI territory.\ncollab/jolt/1793145000000-reviewer-j6a-confirm.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:6:- **P2: statistics collection flag | Open |** The evaluator accepts an otherwise valid 7.1.6 report with `createStats: false` or a missing flag and an empty `rxFrameStats`. The [pinned upstream source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/crossbario/autobahn-testsuite/6ed6f439dc7ed0d7432fe2cf7481b110905ecc5c/autobahntestsuite/autobahntestsuite/fuzzing.py) records that flag and increments frame counts only when it is true. Although collection defaults to true in the pinned suite, such incomplete evidence would make the Pong check pass without demonstrating that statistics were collected. | **Remaining action:** require `createStats is True` when applying the opcode assertion and add missing/false flag fixtures.\ncollab/jolt/1793199000001-engineer-j5b-round2-resume.stdout.log:22:## A1: tried, measured, and the map kept (ruling §1)\ncollab/jolt/1793199000001-engineer-j5b-round2-resume.stdout.log:23:I built A1 (walk the parent chain at each rule entry, no map) and timed it against the map on the same at-bound shapes, three fresh runs each:\ncollab/jolt/1793199000001-engineer-j5b-round2-resume.stdout.log:25:| shape | map (ms) | A1 walk (ms) | change |\ncollab/jolt/1793199000001-engineer-j5b-round2-resume.stdout.log:36:Seven shapes are more than 10% slower, so as §1 prescribes the map stays. The comments and docs carry the A1 soundness wording (the chain length equals the live activations), state that `exitRule` is not virtual and that there are no labelled alternatives, and record why the map was kept.\ncollab/jolt/1793144000000-engineer-j6a-fixes.findings.md:7:Both reviewer P2s are fixed, and the unit tests and `harness.py check` pass. I staged and committed nothing.\ncollab/jolt/1792421958748-architect-jolt-lane-plan.gpt-6-astra.prompt.md:83:   datagram/ws networking: recommend scope (the P2P/DHT surface may be\ncollab/jolt/1793027866046-engineer-j4d-local-persistence.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:191:- **Mixed-runtime lock:** the limitation is disposed of as the documented known-gaps P2 row.\ncollab/jolt/1793174000000-engineer-j5b-continue.stdout.log:27:  - `src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/parser.cljc`: P2-5 (the stage opens before the worker; the worker is closed if the hand-over fails) and P2-6 (`rule-names` is a function).\ncollab/jolt/1792425503000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:132:| `dao.stream.datagram.jvm` / UDP / P2P-DHT (J7) | Do not load the JVM socket namespace on jolt. J0 first probes the small raw-transport addition on the existing `jolt.socket.native` FFI/poller groundwork (R; §6.1). J7 owns the larger datagram-contract and DHT integration effort, not discovery of whether C UDP is callable. Implement the datagram host seam via that narrow nonblocking POSIX socket adapter/FFI, preserving bound/send-failed/closed events, maximum datagram policy, IPv4/IPv6, and host-composed deposit medium. Existing `datagram.cljc` supplies semantics except for the owner-requested backpressure mapping discrepancy identified in §6.1, which must be reconciled before production integration. Do not silently add reliability or queues beneath it. P2P/DHT is explicitly outside the first local-lane cut. It becomes a full-parity gate, not a hidden skip. |\ncollab/jolt/1792426582000-architect-jolt-mob-glm.glm-5.3.findings.md:21:**Reasons.** (1) The adapter is the host's job: `dao.stream.ws` \"deliberately knows no WebSocket library\" (ws.cljc:4-8); every host ships its own (jvm.clj 471, node.cljs 339, dart.cljd 338 lines). Jolt would be the first to ship none: a permanent second process, crash domain and jolt+JVM coupling inside one peer, against the lane's standalone-binary point. (2) The sidecar still needs jolt.socket for local IPC, so that groundwork is built either way; only RFC 6455 is saved: handshake (SHA-1 via the vetted libcrypto wrapper, Q4 policy), masked framing, close codes, pressure→`:full` mapping the ws contract already defines. (3) P2P uniformity: a peer whose networking dies with a supervised sidecar is operationally a different node (datom.world.md:96-97); the label carries \"requires JVM\" forever. J6's cross-host fixtures retire front-loaded RFC 6455 risk — sidecar risk is permanent.\ncollab/jolt/1793147000000-reviewer-j6a-confirm2.gpt-6-luna.prompt.md:1:Resume session 01a17f2a-09b7-7d90-bba9-ae94d6d17eac for the J6a diff in /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-jolt-j6a. Your createStats P2: orchestrator agrees; harness.py:124 now requires createStats is True when forbid_rx_opcodes applies, with fixtures (false, false+empty stats, None, 1, 'true', missing) in both roles; pin hashes unchanged and match (cases 02dc657b..., exceptions d17d8fe0...). Orchestrator reran unittest (9 OK) and harness check (517/6/301). Re-read only relevant lines, challenge this, do not edit.\ncollab/jolt/1792427000000-architect-jolt-mob-synthesis.orchestrator.findings.md:22:- NATIVE WebSocket over jolt.socket, no JVM sidecar (opus, glm, argon). Reasons: the ws adapter is each host's job (ws.cljc:4-8; JVM host 471 lines); portable dao.stream.ws already owns bounds and outcomes so only the host seam + RFC 6455 handshake/framing is new; SHA-1 via the already-qualified libcrypto; a sidecar contradicts the P2P no-privileged-node invariant and the standalone-binary argument; with the parser in-process the sidecar would be the only reason a parity node needs a JDK. glm: a sidecar is admissible only as disclosed throwaway J6 scaffolding. Reverse-if: jolt.socket cannot keep correct park/backpressure under J6 stress.\ncollab/jolt/1792426582000-architect-jolt-mob-opus.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:23:- A sidecar makes a JVM the real network endpoint, with the jolt node reaching peers through a privileged co-process. That conflicts with the P2P / no-privileged-node invariant, and its helper protocol is close to an implementation-added contract (`datom.world.md:70`).\ncollab/jolt/1792426582000-architect-jolt-mob-argon.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:23:  1. **Standalone native binary & P2P symmetry**: The spike's core case for `jolt` is a standalone native binary sharing source (`collab/1792412960461-engineer-jolt-yin-repl-spike.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:90`). With Q3 running the ANTLR4 C++ parser in-process (`collab/1792426031000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r6.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:164`), a WebSocket sidecar would be the sole reason a parity node requires a JDK. In `datom.world`, client and server are symmetric interpreter roles (`docs/design/datom.world.md:97-98`); a sidecar forces a custom IPC protocol that must duplicate `dao.stream.ws` lifecycle and backpressure semantics (`collab/1792426031000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r6.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:136`).\ncollab/jolt/1793147000000-reviewer-j6a-confirm2.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:4:**createStats P2 | Resolved |** [harness.py](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-jolt-j6a/tools/jolt-autobahn/harness.py:124) requires `createStats is True` whenever a forbidden received opcode is checked. The [fixtures](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-jolt-j6a/tools/jolt-autobahn/test_harness.py:70) cover false, false with empty statistics, null, `1`, `\"true\"`, and a missing flag in both roles. Both recomputed file hashes match `pin.json`. | **Remaining action:** none.\ncollab/jolt/1792426031000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r6.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:138:| `dao.stream.datagram.jvm` / UDP / P2P-DHT (J7) | Do not load the JVM socket namespace on jolt. J0 first probes the small raw-transport addition on the existing `jolt.socket.native` FFI/poller groundwork (R; §6.1). J7 owns the larger datagram-contract and DHT integration effort, not discovery of whether C UDP is callable. Implement the datagram host seam via that narrow nonblocking POSIX socket adapter/FFI, preserving bound/send-failed/closed events, maximum datagram policy, IPv4/IPv6, and host-composed deposit medium. Existing `datagram.cljc` supplies semantics with the landed send-error behavior tested in §6.1; Q7 separately asks about a possible future contract amendment. Do not silently add reliability or queues beneath it. P2P/DHT is explicitly outside the first local-lane cut. It becomes a full-parity gate, not a hidden skip. |\ncollab/jolt/1792426031000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r6.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:342:| R8 | Accepted | §7/J0c/J5 observe buffering and match first-failure/probe :end/:early/nil corpus; cst.clj:168–221 verified, C++ behavior untested. |\ncollab/jolt/1792426031000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r6.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:343:| R9 | Accepted | §6.1/J0b: N=1200 and larger configured N, target constants/limits recorded, EMSGSIZE distinguished from truncation. Default verified at datagram.cljc:55–60,317; platform values remain R pending check. |\ncollab/jolt/1792557634000-reviewer-jolt-j1.glm-5.3.findings.md:23:| J1-R1 | P2 (record) | `src/jolt/dao/host/integer.jolt:121-145` | `(big-carrier? (promote 5))` is false on jolt, true on JVM/JS/Dart (compare.diff line 144). §2.4's P law \"equal arguments give equal results on every host\" breaks for this one input class. The one-carrier-per-value law still holds: jolt's canonical carriers match the JVM column exactly, and `conformance_test.cljc:78-110` never asserts `big-carrier?` of a promote result. Every repo consumer applies `big-carrier?` to values or canonical results (`yin/vm/values.cljc:200`, `data.cljc:421,548`, `engine.cljc:810`, `vm.cljc:929`, `integer.cljc:878`), so nothing observes it. | Record the jolt carrier model (promote/from-native/demote/to-native = identity over the by-value carrier; `big-carrier?` answers by value) as a jolt row in the profile's carrier-table docstring or the host-boundary design — a host-boundary-seat edit, not a code change. Do not add a boxed carrier (implementer's judgement is right). |\ncollab/jolt/1792557634000-reviewer-jolt-j1.glm-5.3.findings.md:24:| J1-R2 | P2 (open ruling, the STOP) | `src/jolt/dao/host/text.jolt:116-121`; `json.jolt:70-74` | `units->string` of an unpaired surrogate throws ex-info `{:jolt/unimplemented dao.host.text/units->string :unit u :index i}` (diag log DETAIL lines confirm). The law (shared `text.cljc:66-78` \"unpaired surrogates included\"; `code-points` \"an unpaired surrogate is its own\"; the `utf8-encode` refusal) is unimplementable on a scalar-only string host. Interim behaviour is right: loud, distinct from a profile refusal so no oracle row can pass on it, single cond branch as the seam. 4+1 compare lines, 8 oracle fails, 3 errors — all this one cause. | Keep until the Architect rules; options (a)-(d) in the r1 report are correctly framed, and (a)+(b) is the right recommendation. Sequencing condition: the ruling must land before any jolt text consumer and before yang.python lone-surrogate literals (the r1 report's J2/J5 note). |\ncollab/jolt/1792426582000-architect-jolt-mob-questions.brief.md:8:- /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/datom.world.md (invariants; \"implementations do not add contracts\"; dao.stream is the one boundary; P2P, no privileged node)\ncollab/jolt/1792426582000-architect-jolt-mob-questions.brief.md:18:For the later parity phase (J6/J8), may the jolt process tree include a JVM WebSocket sidecar, or must jolt carry its own WebSocket over jolt.socket (read, not run: non-blocking TCP, fibers park on the poller)? Weigh: the repo invariant \"dao.stream P2P, no server/client concept, no privileged node\"; the spike's argument for jolt as a standalone native binary; implementation cost of RFC 6455 handshake, framing, masking, close, backpressure on top of jolt.socket; SHA-1 via libcrypto; test burden; risk. Give a recommendation and the condition under which you would reverse it.\ncollab/jolt/1792422615171-architect-jolt-lane-plan-review.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:36:| F3 | medium | plan §6 WebSocket row and §10 (`plan:127, 209, 211-217`); spike §6 (`spike:90`); memory invariant \"dao.stream P2P, no server/client, no privileged node\" | J5 (parser) and J6 (WebSocket) both choose an out-of-process **JVM** adapter as the first production implementation, and J7 defers UDP. A J8 \"parity\" jolt node would then need a JVM process beside it to parse Python and to dial or serve WebSockets. This is legitimate implementation plumbing under dao.stream (the plan is careful: canonical data, identity correlation, no raw socket crosses), but it negates the spike's stated reason to prefer jolt over Rust (a standalone native binary with the same source) and weakens the P2P invariant in practice: a peer that cannot dial without a sidecar is a lesser peer. The plan only says a later direct Chez implementation \"must pass the same adapter suite\". | Add owner question 6: \"Does host-lane parity (J8) permit JVM sidecars in the jolt process tree for parsing and WebSocket, or must J8 require the direct Chez/libsocket WebSocket implementation and a non-JVM parse worker? If sidecars are permitted, the J8 label must say so.\" Also state in §2 that the local-REPL milestone label must disclose \"requires a configured parser worker runtime\". |\ncollab/jolt/1792423926000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r3.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:132:| `dao.stream.datagram.jvm` / UDP / P2P-DHT (J7) | Do not load the JVM socket namespace on jolt. J0 first probes the small raw-transport addition on the existing `jolt.socket.native` FFI/poller groundwork (R; §6.1). J7 owns the larger datagram-contract and DHT integration effort, not discovery of whether C UDP is callable. Implement the datagram host seam via that narrow nonblocking POSIX socket adapter/FFI, preserving bound/send-failed/closed events, maximum datagram policy, IPv4/IPv6, and host-composed deposit medium. Existing `datagram.cljc` supplies semantics except for the owner-requested backpressure mapping discrepancy identified in §6.1, which must be reconciled before production integration. Do not silently add reliability or queues beneath it. P2P/DHT is explicitly outside the first local-lane cut. It becomes a full-parity gate, not a hidden skip. |\ncollab/jolt/1792425688000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-review-r5.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:36:| R8 | low | plan §7 J0 probe (plan:174); `src/clj/yang/antlr/cst.clj:168-221` | `first-failure` differs by host. For NoViableAlt, the JVM uses the last buffered token because the Java runtime fills its token buffer lazily; JS and Dart \"fill to EOF and use the listener's offending token\" (cst.clj:173-178). The C++ runtime is a port of the Java one, so it probably fills lazily, but I have not verified that. The plan's probe lists \"incomplete multiline input\" but does not require matching `:end`/`:early` classification. | J0c records which rule C++ needs (JVM-style or JS/Dart-style) from observed behavior. It requires identical `first-failure` and `repl_probe/probe` results to the oracle on an incomplete-input corpus (open block, open bracket, open triple-quote, early error under an open bracket). |\ncollab/jolt/1792425688000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-review-r5.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:37:| R9 | low | plan §6.1 items 1-2 (plan:146-147); jolt `stdlib/jolt/socket/native.clj:64-121`; `src/cljc/dao/stream/datagram.cljc:55,317` | The consts table has neither `SOCK_DGRAM` (2 on both platforms) nor `EMSGSIZE` (40 on macOS, 90 on Linux). The plan's \"limit-sized packets\" never names the limit. The contract default `:max-bytes` is 1200. From memory, not checked (sysctl not run): macOS loopback `net.inet.udp.maxdgram` is commonly 9216, so an oversize send can fail at send with EMSGSIZE rather than truncate on receive. | Set N to the contract's `:max-bytes` (1200) plus one configured larger value under the platform maximum. Add `SOCK_DGRAM`/`EMSGSIZE` to the probe's platform constants. Record the relevant sysctl values. Expect EMSGSIZE as an error outcome for sends above the platform maximum, separately from the N+1 receive-sentinel case. |\ncollab/jolt/1792425688000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-review-r5.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:53:- The static DFA layout of ANTLR C++ generated code (R2), the C++ token-buffer fill behavior (R8), the macOS pthread stack default and `maxdgram` (R5, R9), and whether Cpp helpers exist at grammars-v4@`8af0d4c` (R6).\ncollab/jolt/1793146000000-engineer-j6a-fixes2.prompt.md:1:Resume J6a, round 3. Reviewer codex/luna (confirmation pass; raw log copied to collab/luna-confirm.jsonl, last agent_message) confirmed the first two fixes and found one more P2, which the orchestrator agrees with: the 7.1.6 evaluator accepts a report with createStats false/missing and an empty rxFrameStats, so the Pong check can pass vacuously (upstream fuzzing.py at 6ed6f439 increments frame counts only when createStats is true). Fix: when applying forbid_rx_opcodes, require the report's createStats to be exactly True (else fail \"malformed field: createStats\"); add fixtures for createStats missing, false, and non-bool in both roles; keep the passing case. Re-pin anything whose hash changes (exceptions.json/cases.json only if you edit them). Same constraints: only tools/jolt-autobahn files, no staging/commit, foreground only. Run python3 -m unittest discover -s tools/jolt-autobahn and python3 -I tools/jolt-autobahn/harness.py check. Begin the final response with Completed-GMT / Completed-Local / Coding-Agent / Session-ID lines, then changed files and exact outcomes.\ncollab/jolt/1793145000000-architect-j6a-signoff.claude-fable-5-1.prompt.md:10:Read-only. Review the uncommitted diff in /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-jolt-j6a (git -C /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-jolt-j6a diff) against your own verdict (/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-jolt-j6a/collab/architect-verdict.md, amendments 1-3 only). Independent review by codex/luna found two P2s (collab/luna-review.jsonl in the worktree; last agent_message), both since fixed by the engineer; luna's confirmation of the fixes is running concurrently, so your sign-off is conditional on it returning ready-to-commit. Orchestrator reran unittest (9 OK) and harness.py check (517/6/301). Check the diff implements amendments 1-3 faithfully, nothing beyond them, and nothing contradicts dao.stream.ws.md / §9.5-§9.6.\ncollab/jolt/1793145000000-architect-j6a-signoff.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:10:1. Fix the P2 below in the jolt row of dao.stream.ws.md.\ncollab/jolt/1793145000000-architect-j6a-signoff.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:16:- **P2 | docs/design/dao.stream.ws.md:530 | evidence:** the accepted set stops at 1011, so inbound 1012 to 1014 are answered 1002. The same document has served connections send 1013 for pending-overflow at line 321, and the JVM-client row at line 528 says served connections are the only sender of 1013. A jolt client attached to a JVM or Node server would therefore treat a legitimate overflow close from a sibling host as a protocol error. Nothing forces this: at the pinned release the 7.9.x rows probe 0, 999, 1004 to 1006, 1016, 1100, 2000 and 2999, never 1012 to 1014, and §9.5 line 1282 lists the invalid codes as below 1000, 1004 to 1006 and 1015 to 2999. The engineer transcribed my verdict exactly. The defect is in the verdict's set, and I amend it here as Architect. **Fix:** accepted set becomes 1000 to 1003, 1007 to 1014, and 3000 to 4999. Make the parenthetical exhaustive: 0 to 999, 1004 to 1006, 1015 to 2999, and 5000 and above. No evaluator, exception row or hash depends on it.\ncollab/jolt/1793145000000-architect-j6a-signoff.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:21:- Amendment 1. Six exception rows, 7.1.6 client and server with INFORMATIONAL, INFORMATIONAL, 1000 and no Pong. Counts 298/3/216, 301 per role, 1,204 total, in the triage header, README, design-doc note, pin hashes and tests. Negative fixtures cover Pong after Close, wrong and missing close code, OK, FAILED, timeout, and the malformed-count cases from luna's first P2. The verdict's open item is now closed: the per-case report dict at the pinned commit always carries `rxFrameStats`, keyed by opcode and stringified by JSON. The fuzzer drops the socket when its own close is answered, so a Pong sent before the testee's close reply is counted and a correct testee produces none.\ncollab/jolt/1793990000000-architect-j6g-diagnose.brief.md:3:# J6g diagnostic round (argon tier): why does peer B starve and A stall under workload W?\ncollab/jolt/1793990000000-architect-j6g-diagnose.brief.md:35:   (plan v3 §2 P2: codec decode enters the round) — if A's final chunk\ncollab/jolt/1793990000000-architect-j6g-diagnose.brief.md:41:4. The driver's sleep-fds!/poll deadline logic (R8/R9) never wakes for\ncollab/jolt/1793990000000-architect-j6g-diagnose.brief.md:55:  exact change, where, and why it preserves A1-A7) — the orchestrator\ncollab/jolt/1793990000000-architect-j6g-diagnose.brief.md:57:- If it is the CRITERION itself (workload W is unsatisfiable as\ncollab/jolt/1792454716000-architect-jolt-design-doc-review.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:16:| A1 | High | D:1073–1079,1493–1495; `src/cljc/dao/stream/transit.cljc:107–123` | Empty `:jolt` requires do **not** select function-level `:default` arms: jolt also enables `:clj`, so encode/decode still select Java/Transit calls. The proposed fallback defining only nil `profile` omits the public functions required by callers and tests. | Specify explicit `:jolt` refusal arms before `:clj` in encode/decode. Remove the one-form fallback or require a complete, narrow public surface with equivalent refusals. Test clean namespace loading and every public codec entry. |\ncollab/jolt/1793196000000-engineer-j5b-round2.prompt.md:10:Resume J5b in /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-j5b (uncommitted round-1 work stays). The Architect ruled on your three escalations: collab/fable-j5b-rulings.md in this worktree (BINDING; its section 1 accepts your recorded-depth deviation with the simplification A1; section 2 reclassifies R1c/R4a/R4b; section 3 rules time: no wall-clock refusal, J5c ledgered; section 4 confirms your C3 reading; section 5 sets the evidence plan; section 6 gives exact doc/comment edits D1-D9; section 7 is the round-2 acceptance list C1'-C12; section 8 withdraws the earlier exitRule/closure-override text). Implement round 2 exactly as section 7 states: A1 in jolt_parser.cpp (and its tests/calibration), the reclassified legs (r1c at 10,000, r4 at 20,000 under -Xss1g for the JVM oracle, power at 100,000 as the R4b replacement), the doc/ledger edits D1-D9 (§7.6 time paragraph and Platforms paragraph, known-gaps J5c row appended: union rule, never rewrite the file, row count monotonic, no collab/ cites anywhere in docs or ledger). Platforms: macOS legs C1'-C4,C6-C8,C10 you run locally ONE LANE AT A TIME (owner asked to reduce laptop load; do not run bb test:jolt-j5 on the laptop); the Linux legs (build, probe:jolt-j5, calibrate, budget leg, ASan/UBSan C5, cycles 20000, workers, parity, bb test:jolt-j5) are the orchestrator's on shiva: finish the code and list the exact commands in your report; the Platforms paragraph in section 7.6 must NOT say 'pending': leave a clearly marked placeholder line the orchestrator fills from the shiva logs and say so. If any leg cannot be met, report the exact leg and measurement and STOP (nothing reinterpreted locally). Constraints: no stage/commit; foreground only; cljstyle check on your files if your shell allows (else the orchestrator runs it); kondo. Begin with Completed-GMT / Completed-Local / Coding-Agent / Session-ID lines, then changed files from git status, exact counts per C item (met / unmet / not run and why), concerns.\ncollab/jolt/1792427469000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-review-r7.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:43:4. **Regression check:** R1 (plan:188-192, no C++ Jing encoder), R2 (:194-196), R3 (:154-158), R4 (:122-124), R5 (:126,198-200; see W5), R6 (:186,220,263), R7 (:271-273,283), R8 (:204), R9 (:146,153), R10 (:271; J0a adds the CMake pin) are all present and consistent. No sidecar text remains outside labelled history (plan:29,202,210,302 all say native). Milestone labels: local = through J5 with the native C++ parser library disclosed; parity = J8, native WebSocket and parser libraries, ws:// pending wss. Coherent. The open questions are only licensing and wss.\ncollab/jolt/1793079899150-architect-j4d-review.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:193:union rule. Row 63 (J4c closure) and the F5 mixed Node/OS-lock P2 row are\ncollab/jolt/1793079899150-architect-j4d-review.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:213:- P2 Key files are created by one `O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_CLOEXEC` open at 0600,\ncollab/jolt/1792423156000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:131:| `dao.stream.datagram.jvm` / UDP / P2P-DHT (J7) | Do not load the JVM socket namespace on jolt. Implement the existing datagram host seam via a narrow nonblocking POSIX socket adapter/FFI, preserving bound/send-failed/closed events, maximum datagram policy, IPv4/IPv6, and host-composed deposit medium. Existing `datagram.cljc` contract supplies semantics; do not add reliability or queues beneath it. P2P/DHT is explicitly outside the first local-lane cut. It becomes a full-parity gate, not a hidden skip. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
