p` is synchronous and the Node event loop is single\n8:  {:doc \"J6f Autobahn conformance: starts the testee and the Dockerized pinned suite, waits for the READY barrier, runs harness.py per role, collects results/, and shuts both sides down. Usage: bb autobahn:jolt <role> <agent>\"\n15:  ;; jolt host lane (experimental, docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md)\n17:  {:doc \"Materialize the jolt-toolchain.edn pins into build/tools/jolt (mise Chez/CMake checked, jolt cloned at the full SHA, never pulled) and write build/tools/jolt-env.sh\"\n22:  {:doc \"Copy/revert the jolt clone under gitignored build/bootstrap-neg (deleted on success, retained on failure) and declare a synthetic patch and prove bootstrap refuses it unapplied or corrupted, then accepts it applied (JOLT_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_DIR selects the source clone)\"\n27:  {:doc \"J0a baseline smoke under jolt -Srepro -M:jolt: tracked load of yang.antlr.export/packet and defcfn :blocking calls (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\n30:                         \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_smoke.clj\")))}\n33:  {:doc \"Run jolt -Srepro -M:jolt with the arguments given (a script path, -e ...), under build/tools/jolt-env.sh\"\n36:                         \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt \\\"$@\\\"\"\n45:  {:doc \"J1b: libcrypto provenance (qualified, missing, undeclared, version-floor, wrong-library-first, Linux LD_PRELOAD) and 256 MiB :blocking hash collect-safety, each in a child jolt process (needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\n50:  {:doc \"J5 acceptance: one Python session through the JVM and jolt REPL entry points with the standard catalog (output equal line for line), the multiline probe sequence, and the unavailable-library REPL legs (needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\n55:  {:doc \"J5b: the native Python parser's budget (input 4 MiB; in-parser guards: 8192 rule frames, 4096 SLL lookahead links, 256 full-LL links, on a 16 MiB parse thread): the review's repros, at/over per shape against the predicted table, 10x the old crash depths, the JVM's packets (incl. a 20,000-deep 1+ tree), the old crash depths in children on the jolt thread, injected C++ faults, the abort-is-a-failure property, lifecycle and unavailable-library legs. Args select legs: budget below crash inject abort unavailable (needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\n76:  {:doc \"J6d: the jolt TCP substrate and owner-thread pump (dao.stream.ws.tcp, dao.stream.ws.pump, driver sleep-fds!), one child jolt process per section: closure (no jolt.socket), address (literals/localhost, resolver trap), substrate (port 0, nonblocking accept/connect, EOF vs reset, gone-peer write survives), ordered (A3 short write, drain order, failure), fairness (A1 ii/iv), stdin (A1 i, held partial line), deadline (A2 seam), control (A3 event orders, A4 pong budget, D1 close slot), close (A5, D2, D3), listener (64 cap, lower-deadlines!, drained?); native memory and registry empty after close. Arguments select sections (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\n83:                                                \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_tcp_probe.clj \\\"$1\\\"\"\n90:  {:doc \"J6e: the jolt WebSocket host adapter (dao.stream.ws.jolt, the yin.repl.host shadow, the jolt -main wiring), one child jolt process per section: closure (C1), handshake (C2), bind (C3), address (C4), io (C5), close (C6), shutdown (C7, the real owner loop), isolation (C8), driver (C9, deadline folding, a --headless --port child), fairness (C10); native memory and registries empty after close. Arguments select sections (needs bb bootstrap:jolt and bb build:jolt-native)\"\n97:                                                \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_ws_probe.clj \\\"$1\\\"\"\n103:   workload-w:jolt\n104:   {:doc \"J6g: pre-registered Workload W, with an independent five-minute watchdog and ten-second sampler; one jolt worker serves two peers while stepping the REPL (needs bb bootstrap:jolt and bb build:jolt-native)\"\n116:  {:doc \"J1: the dao.host oracle (conformance, bytes, float, text tests) under jolt -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test through src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj; counts per namespace, nonzero exit on any failure, error or load failure (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\n124:  ;; build/j2-logs/; every step is its own jolt process.\n164:  {:doc \"J2: self-test the applicability manifest guard with a temporary test tree; no jolt or natives needed\"\n174:  {:doc \"J2: the cross-host integer-carrier test (Q1: carriers named by value). `encode` runs the JVM side (java -cp over the test:dev classpath, writes build/j2-logs/carrier-fixtures.edn); `verify` runs the jolt side (decode both rows, assert equal bytes and equal results)\"\n190:  {:doc \"Self-test the CBOR override review gate in temporary worktree copies; no jolt or natives needed\"\n195:  {:doc \"J2: differential parity of the jolt dao.stream.cbor host seam (src/jolt/dao/stream/cbor/boring.jolt) against the JVM's pinned Boring: `emit` encodes the shared corpus on the JVM (writes build/j2-logs/cbor-parity.edn), `check` re-encodes it on jolt byte-for-byte, round-trips each row and refuses a battery of non-canonical frames\"\n207:  {:doc \"Linearity guard for the jolt dao.host.text override: code-points, unit-count, an ascending code-unit walk and utf8-encode on BMP, astral and mixed strings of 64/256/1024 Ki code points; each 4x input under 8x the time, 1024 Ki under 5 s (src/dev/jolt_text_perf.clj; needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\n210:                         \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_text_perf.clj\")))}\n213:  {:doc \"J1: run src/dev/jolt_profile_compare.cljc on the JVM and on jolt (public vars, arities, refusal data, a differential case battery over dao.host.*) and diff the two; writes build/j1-logs/compare-{jvm,jolt}.edn and compare.diff; exit 1 when they differ\"\n216:                         \"mkdir -p build/j1-logs && clojure -M src/dev/jolt_profile_compare.cljc | grep '^\\\\[' > build/j1-logs/compare-jvm.edn && . build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_profile_compare.cljc | grep '^\\\\[' > build/j1-logs/compare-jolt.edn && diff build/j1-logs/compare-jvm.edn build/j1-logs/compare-jolt.edn > build/j1-logs/compare.diff; s=$?; cat build/j1-logs/compare.diff; exit $s\")))}\n219:  {:doc \"J1 DIAGNOSTIC, not the oracle verdict: dao.host.float-test and dao.host.text-test, unchanged, under jolt with the :jolt-diag stand-in for the corpus loader dao.jing.cbor-fixtures (isolates these checks from the real corpus loader); see src/dev/jolt_diag/dao/jing/cbor_fixtures.cljc\"\n225:  {:doc \"J1: the jolt clojure.data.json shim (src/jolt/clojure/data/json.jolt) against src/dev/jolt_json_shim_check.cljc, under jolt; the same file passes against the real data.json on the JVM (clojure -M:dev, see its header)\"\n237:  {:doc \"Run the bootstrapped jolt with build/tools/jolt-env.sh, passing every argument through (e.g. bb jolt:run -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_j0c_workers.clj)\"\n/opt/homebrew/bin/clojure\n/opt/homebrew/bin/jolt\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"The current Peer A sender makes one bounded send attempt per round and yields on `:would-block`. That rules out the suspected inner write spin in this harness version. I’m tracing the work done inside each pump visit and REPL step; rotation cannot help if either takes a long time to return.\n"}}
