{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'A1|A2|A3|A4|A5|A6|A7|P2|Workload|workload|R8|R9' src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/pump.jolt; cat src/jolt/dao/stream/waitset/driver.jolt; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/ws/rfc6455.cljc | sed -n '310,485p'; cat src/jolt/dao/host/bytes.jolt\"","aggregated_output":"3:   J6 plan rulings A1-A5). One instance per `create` call: its registry of\n7:   Ownership (A1). Every entry runs on the thread that drives the instance;\n15:   Bounded turn (A1). One `pump!` visits each ready descriptor at most once,\n21:   One ordered write path (A3). Each connection owns one FIFO of whole wire\n41:   Control budget (A4). At most `max-pongs` pending pongs per connection plus\n49:   Close record (A5). `{:local nil|:queued|:sent, :peer nil|:received,\n104:  \"Pending pongs per connection before its input pauses (A4).\"\n109:  \"From the first close event to forced teardown (A5).\"\n114:  \"Default per-listener cap on accepted, not yet upgraded sockets (A4).\"\n119:  \"Default deadline for an upgrade, from accept or connect (A4).\"\n390:  \"A transfer failure: a :ws connection terminates per A5, a :raw one owes\n401:;; Writes (A3)\n480:;; Close (A5) and control output (A4)\n641:;; Reads and visits (A1)\n860:;; Listener lifecycle (A6 seam)\n884:   A5 deadline: shut, 1006.\"\n892:  \"The instance as the driver's `:pump` value (A2): `:interest`,\n(ns dao.stream.waitset.driver\n  \"Jolt wait-set wake policy: a nonblocking self-pipe carrying contentless\n   tokens. No interpreter state or dispatch lives here. Plain-thread waits\n   use the poller's monotonic deadline; stdin and socket waits multiplex the\n   same pipe with fd 0 and a pump's interest descriptors through jolt's\n   native poll binding, on the one owner thread. No reader thread.\n\n   Stdin is read raw from fd 0 into a driver-owned line buffer (plan v2 A1),\n   one read(2) per round and only after poll reported fd 0 ready, so the\n   read never waits. Complete lines are deposited; a partial line stays\n   buffered and never blocks the owner; a zero-length read is end of input.\n   Chez's buffered System/in is never read, so no byte is split between two\n   readers.\"\n  (:require [dao.host.text :as text]\n            [jolt.ffi :as ffi]\n            [jolt.io-poller :as poller]\n            [jolt.socket.native :as native]))\n\n\n(ffi/load-library)\n(ffi/defcfn c-pipe \"pipe\" [:pointer] :int)\n\n\n(def ^:private stdin-chunk 4096)\n\n\n(defn make-wake\n  []\n  (let [fds (ffi/alloc 8)]\n    (try\n      (when (neg? (c-pipe fds))\n        (throw (ex-info \"wake pipe creation failed\" {:errno (ffi/errno)})))\n      (let [r (ffi/read fds :int 0) w (ffi/read fds :int 4)]\n        (poller/nonblock! r)\n        (poller/nonblock! w)\n        ;; :stdin is the partial line held between rounds (bytes after the\n        ;; last newline), owned by this wake's one owner thread\n        {:read r :write w :stdin (atom (byte-array 0))})\n      (finally (ffi/free fds)))))\n\n\n(defn close!\n  [wake]\n  (poller/forget! (:read wake))\n  (poller/c-close (:read wake))\n  (poller/c-close (:write wake))\n  nil)\n\n\n(defn nudge!\n  [wake]\n  (let [b (ffi/alloc 1)]\n    (try\n      (ffi/write b :uint8 1)\n      (loop []\n        (let [n (poller/c-write (:write wake) b 1) e (ffi/errno)]\n          (cond\n            (= n 1) nil\n            (poller/eintr? e) (recur)\n            (poller/eagain? e) nil ; a full pipe already owes a wake\n            :else (throw (ex-info \"wake pipe write failed\" {:errno e})))))\n      (finally (ffi/free b)))))\n\n\n(defn- drain!\n  [wake]\n  (let [b (ffi/alloc 256)]\n    (try\n      (loop [woken? false]\n        (let [n (poller/c-read (:read wake) b 256) e (ffi/errno)]\n          (cond\n            (pos? n) (recur true)\n            (poller/eintr? e) (recur woken?)\n            (poller/eagain? e) woken?\n            :else (throw (ex-info \"wake pipe read failed\" {:errno e :read n})))))\n      (finally (ffi/free b)))))\n\n\n(defn sleep!\n  [wake sleep-ms]\n  (poller/wait-ready (:read wake) :read (poller/deadline-ms sleep-ms))\n  (drain! wake))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Stdin lines\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- concat-bytes\n  [a b]\n  (let [na (alength a) nb (alength b) out (byte-array (+ na nb))]\n    (dotimes [i na] (aset out i (aget a i)))\n    (dotimes [i nb] (aset out (+ na i) (aget b i)))\n    out))\n\n\n(defn- slice\n  [bs start end]\n  (let [out (byte-array (- end start))]\n    (dotimes [i (- end start)] (aset out i (aget bs (+ start i))))\n    out))\n\n\n(defn- decode-line\n  \"The text of line bytes `bs` (newline excluded), one trailing CR dropped\n   as the JVM's readLine does. Ill-formed UTF-8 falls back to jolt's\n   lossy decode rather than losing the line.\"\n  [bs]\n  (let [n (alength bs)\n        n (if (and (pos? n) (= 13 (aget bs (dec n)))) (dec n) n)]\n    (try\n      (text/utf8-decode bs 0 n)\n      (catch Throwable _\n        (let [p (ffi/alloc (max 1 n))]\n          (try (ffi/write-array p bs 0 n)\n               (ffi/read-bytes p n)\n               (finally (ffi/free p))))))))\n\n\n(defn- deposit-lines!\n  \"Append `chunk` to the held partial line and deposit every complete line\n   through `line!`, keeping the remainder.\"\n  [wake chunk line!]\n  (let [bs (concat-bytes @(:stdin wake) chunk)\n        n (alength bs)]\n    (loop [start 0 i 0]\n      (cond\n        (= i n) (reset! (:stdin wake) (slice bs start n))\n        (= 10 (aget bs i)) (do (line! (decode-line (slice bs start i)))\n                               (recur (inc i) (inc i)))\n        :else (recur start (inc i))))))\n\n\n(defn- end-of-input!\n  \"Deposit a held unterminated last line, as read-line answers it, then\n   nil.\"\n  [wake line!]\n  (let [held @(:stdin wake)]\n    (reset! (:stdin wake) (byte-array 0))\n    (when (pos? (alength held)) (line! (decode-line held)))\n    (line! nil)))\n\n\n(defn- read-stdin!\n  \"One read(2) of fd 0, which poll reported ready. Answers true when it\n   deposited or reached end of input.\"\n  [wake line!]\n  (let [buf (ffi/alloc stdin-chunk)]\n    (try\n      (let [n (poller/c-read 0 buf stdin-chunk) e (ffi/errno)]\n        (cond\n          (pos? n) (do (deposit-lines! wake (ffi/read-array buf n) line!) true)\n          (and (neg? n) (or (poller/eintr? e) (poller/eagain? e))) false\n          ;; zero, or a descriptor that cannot be read (closed fd 0): end\n          :else (do (end-of-input! wake line!) true)))\n      (finally (ffi/free buf)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; One owner round\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn sleep-fds!\n  \"One owner round's wait (plan v2 A1): poll the wake pipe, fd 0 (when\n   `line!` is given) and `pump`'s interest descriptors (when `pump` is\n   given) until one is ready or the earlier of `sleep-ms` and the pump's\n   `:deadline` (`jolt.io-poller/clock-ms`; nil, or a pump without one, is\n   the cadence alone) passes; then drain the wake pipe, run one\n   `(:pump! pump)` turn over the observed `[[fd revents] ...]` (every\n   round; `[]` after a timeout), then deposit stdin lines through `line!`\n   (nil at end of input). A deadline already due still polls once, with a\n   zero timeout, so readiness seen then reaches the same `pump!` turn as\n   the expiry. Never evaluates. Answers truthy when anything was woken,\n   moved or deposited.\"\n  [wake sleep-ms pump line!]\n  (let [interest (if pump (vec ((:interest pump))) [])\n        base (if line! 2 1)\n        n (+ base (count interest))\n        fds (native/alloc-pollfds n)\n        cadence (poller/deadline-ms sleep-ms)\n        due (when-let [f (:deadline pump)] (f))\n        deadline (if due (min due cadence) cadence)]\n    (try\n      (native/init-pollfd! fds 0 (:read wake) native/pollin)\n      (when line! (native/init-pollfd! fds 1 0 native/pollin))\n      (dotimes [i (count interest)]\n        (let [[fd events] (nth interest i)]\n          (native/init-pollfd! fds (+ base i) fd events)))\n      (loop []\n        (let [remaining (max 0 (long (Math/ceil (- deadline (poller/clock-ms)))))\n              [rc e] (native/c-poll fds n remaining)]\n          (cond\n            (and (neg? rc) (native/eintr? e)) (recur)\n            (neg? rc) (throw (ex-info \"owner poll failed\" {:errno e}))\n            :else nil)))\n      (let [ready (vec (keep (fn [i]\n                               (let [rev (native/pollfd-revents fds (+ base i))]\n                                 (when (pos? rev) [(first (nth interest i)) rev])))\n                             (range (count interest))))\n            woken? (drain! wake)\n            progressed? (when pump (:progressed? ((:pump! pump) ready)))\n            stdin? (when (and line! (pos? (native/pollfd-revents fds 1)))\n                     (read-stdin! wake line!))]\n        (or woken? progressed? stdin?))\n      (finally (ffi/free fds)))))\n\n\n(defn sleep-input!\n  \"Wait for a nudge, stdin, or the cadence deadline. `line!` only deposits\n   lines (nil at EOF). Never evaluate from this seam.\"\n  [wake sleep-ms line!]\n  (sleep-fds! wake sleep-ms nil line!))\n   310\t\n   311\t\n   312\t(defn- finish-frame\n   313\t  [state]\n   314\t  (let [{:keys [fin? opcode chunks len]} (:frame state)\n   315\t        base (assoc state :phase :header :frame nil)]\n   316\t    (if (>= opcode 8)\n   317\t      (let [payload (concat-chunks chunks len)]\n   318\t        (case opcode\n   319\t          9 [base [{:type :ping :payload payload}]]\n   320\t          10 [base [{:type :pong :payload payload}]]\n   321\t          [(assoc base :phase :done) [(parse-close payload)]]))\n   322\t      (if-not fin?\n   323\t        [base []]\n   324\t        (let [msg (:msg state)]\n   325\t          (if (and (= :text (:opcode msg)) (not (utf8-complete? (:utf8 msg))))\n   326\t            [(assoc base :phase :done)\n   327\t             [{:type :fail :code 1007 :reason \"text message ends inside a character\"}]]\n   328\t            [(assoc base :msg nil)\n   329\t             [{:type :message :opcode (:opcode msg)\n   330\t               :payload (concat-chunks (:chunks msg) (:size msg))}]]))))))\n   331\t\n   332\t\n   333\t(defn- take-payload\n   334\t  \"Consume `take` bytes of `chunk` from `i` into the current frame.\"\n   335\t  [state chunk i take]\n   336\t  (let [{:keys [key got opcode]} (:frame state)\n   337\t        piece (let [s (bytes/slice chunk i (+ i take))]\n   338\t                (if key (unmask s key got) s))\n   339\t        state (-> state\n   340\t                  (update-in [:frame :got] + take)\n   341\t                  (update-in [:frame :chunks] conj piece))]\n   342\t    (if (>= opcode 8)\n   343\t      [state nil]\n   344\t      (let [msg (:msg state)\n   345\t            utf8 (if (= :text (:opcode msg))\n   346\t                   (utf8-feed (:utf8 msg) piece)\n   347\t                   (:utf8 msg))]\n   348\t        (if (nil? utf8)\n   349\t          [state [1007 \"invalid UTF-8 in a text message\"]]\n   350\t          [(-> state\n   351\t               (update-in [:msg :chunks] conj piece)\n   352\t               (update-in [:msg :size] + take)\n   353\t               (assoc-in [:msg :utf8] utf8)\n   354\t               (update-in [:frame :chunks] (constantly [])))\n   355\t           nil])))))\n   356\t\n   357\t\n   358\t(defn parse-frame\n   359\t  \"Resume parsing `chunk` at `offset` until one event is produced or the\n   360\t   chunk is exhausted: `[event-or-nil parser' offset']`.  `offset'` is the\n   361\t   first byte not consumed, so a caller that stops after an event keeps the\n   362\t   rest of its chunk by offset and resumes later with the same chunk and\n   363\t   `offset'`; nothing is copied or re-read.  With a nil event `offset'` is the\n   364\t   chunk length and any partial frame is held in `parser'`.  An event is a\n   365\t   completed control frame, a completed message (non-final data frames\n   366\t   produce none), or a failure; a done parser answers `[nil parser offset]`.\n   367\t   The chunk is never mutated.\"\n   368\t  [state chunk offset]\n   369\t  (let [n (bytes/length chunk)]\n   370\t    (loop [st state i offset]\n   371\t      (cond\n   372\t        (= :done (:phase st)) [nil st i]\n   373\t        (>= i n) [nil st n]\n   374\t\n   375\t        (= :header (:phase st))\n   376\t        (let [hdr (conj (:hdr st) (bytes/get chunk i))\n   377\t              c (count hdr)\n   378\t              st (assoc st :hdr hdr)\n   379\t              early (when (= c 2) (check-first-two st (nth hdr 0) (nth hdr 1)))]\n   380\t          (cond\n   381\t            early (let [[s es] (fail st (first early) (second early))]\n   382\t                    [(first es) s (inc i)])\n   383\t            (and (>= c 2) (= c (header-length (nth hdr 1))))\n   384\t            (let [[st' es] (begin-frame st hdr)]\n   385\t              (cond\n   386\t                (seq es) [(first es) st' (inc i)]\n   387\t                (and (= :payload (:phase st')) (zero? (:len (:frame st'))))\n   388\t                (let [[s es2] (finish-frame st')]\n   389\t                  (if (seq es2)\n   390\t                    [(first es2) s (inc i)]\n   391\t                    (recur s (inc i))))\n   392\t                (= :done (:phase st'))\n   393\t                [nil st' (inc i)]\n   394\t                :else (recur st' (inc i))))\n   395\t            :else (recur st (inc i))))\n   396\t\n   397\t        :else\n   398\t        (let [{:keys [len got]} (:frame st)\n   399\t              take (min (- len got) (- n i))\n   400\t              [st' failure] (take-payload st chunk i take)]\n   401\t          (cond\n   402\t            failure (let [[s es] (fail st' (first failure) (second failure))]\n   403\t                      [(first es) s (+ i take)])\n   404\t            (= (+ got take) len)\n   405\t            (let [[s es] (finish-frame st')]\n   406\t              (if (seq es)\n   407\t                [(first es) s (+ i take)]\n   408\t                (recur s (+ i take))))\n   409\t            :else (recur st' (+ i take))))))))\n   410\t\n   411\t\n   412\t(defn feed\n   413\t  \"Feed one received `chunk`; `[parser' events]`: `parse-frame` to\n   414\t   exhaustion.\"\n   415\t  [state chunk]\n   416\t  (loop [st state offset 0 events []]\n   417\t    (let [[event st' offset'] (parse-frame st chunk offset)]\n   418\t      (if event\n   419\t        (recur st' offset' (conj events event))\n   420\t        [st' events]))))\n(ns dao.host.bytes\n  \"The jolt override of src/cljc/dao/host/bytes.cljc (the :jolt alias puts\n   src/jolt first, docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §4.2): the\n   same public entries, arities, laws and refusal data\n   (docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md §4.2, table A; §2.4).\n\n   The host byte array on jolt is jolt's own byte array (`byte-array`,\n   class `byte/1`, signed elements like the JVM's `byte[]`), so shared code\n   that reads one with `aget`/`alength`, and the test fixtures, see the\n   same value. A byte is read and written as a native integer 0 to 255.\n   Every entry is written over jolt's core array functions only, with the\n   prevalidation and memmove the laws require spelled out, rather than over\n   the `System/arraycopy` and `java.util.Arrays` shims the shared :clj arms\n   would reach.\"\n  (:refer-clojure :exclude [bytes? get set!]))\n\n\n(defn- refuse\n  [entry cls detail]\n  (throw (ex-info (str \"dao.host refused: \" entry \" \" (name cls) \" (\" detail \")\")\n                  {:dao.host/refusal cls :dao.host/entry entry :detail detail})))\n\n\n(defn bytes?\n  \"P. True when `x` is a host byte array.\"\n  [x]\n  (clojure.core/bytes? x))\n\n\n(defn- native-int?\n  [x]\n  (int? x))\n\n\n(defn- check-bytes!\n  [entry bs]\n  (when-not (bytes? bs)\n    (refuse entry :unsupported-value \"not a host byte array\")))\n\n\n(defn- check-index!\n  \"Refuse unless native integer `i` lies in [lo, hi].\"\n  [entry i lo hi]\n  (when-not (and (native-int? i) (<= lo i) (<= i hi))\n    (refuse entry :out-of-range (str i \" not in [\" lo \", \" hi \"]\"))))\n\n\n(defn- check-byte!\n  [entry v]\n  (when-not (and (native-int? v) (<= 0 v) (<= v 255))\n    (refuse entry :out-of-range (str v \" is not a byte 0-255\"))))\n\n\n(defn length\n  \"P. The number of bytes in `bs`.\"\n  [bs]\n  (check-bytes! 'length bs)\n  (alength bs))\n\n\n(defn alloc\n  \"P, fresh. A new host byte array of `n` zero bytes, `n` a native\n   integer from 0.\"\n  [n]\n  (when-not (and (native-int? n) (<= 0 n))\n    (refuse 'alloc :out-of-range (str n \" is not a length\")))\n  (byte-array n))\n\n\n(defn- byte-at\n  \"The byte at an index already checked.\"\n  [bs i]\n  (bit-and (aget bs i) 0xff))\n\n\n(defn- put!\n  \"Write byte `v` at an index already checked.\"\n  [bs i v]\n  (aset bs i (unchecked-byte v)))\n\n\n(defn get\n  \"P. The byte at index `i` of `bs`, 0 to 255.\"\n  [bs i]\n  (check-index! 'get i 0 (dec (length bs)))\n  (byte-at bs i))\n\n\n(defn slice\n  \"P, fresh. A new host byte array holding `bs[start, end)`, for\n   0 <= start <= end <= length.\"\n  [bs start end]\n  (let [n (length bs)]\n    (check-index! 'slice start 0 n)\n    (check-index! 'slice end start n))\n  (let [out (byte-array (- end start))]\n    (dotimes [i (- end start)]\n      (aset out i (aget bs (+ start i))))\n    out))\n\n\n(defn equal?\n  \"P. True when byte arrays `a` and `b` hold the same bytes.\"\n  [a b]\n  (let [n (length a)]\n    (and (= n (length b))\n         (loop [i 0]\n           (or (= i n)\n               (and (= (byte-at a i) (byte-at b i))\n                    (recur (inc i))))))))\n\n\n(defn from-vector\n  \"P, fresh. A new host byte array of `xs`, a vector of native integers\n   0 to 255; any other element is refused `:out-of-range` before\n   anything is built.\"\n  [xs]\n  (when-not (vector? xs)\n    (refuse 'from-vector :unsupported-value \"not a vector\"))\n  (run! #(check-byte! 'from-vector %) xs)\n  (let [out (byte-array (count xs))]\n    (dotimes [i (count xs)]\n      (put! out i (nth xs i)))\n    out))\n\n\n(defn to-vector\n  \"P. The bytes of `bs` as a vector of native integers 0 to 255.\"\n  [bs]\n  (let [n (length bs)]\n    (loop [i 0\n           out (transient [])]\n      (if (< i n)\n        (recur (inc i) (conj! out (byte-at bs i)))\n        (persistent! out)))))\n\n\n(defn set!\n  \"M. Write byte `v`, 0 to 255, at index `i` of target `bs`; nil. A bad\n   index or byte is refused before the write.\"\n  [bs i v]\n  (check-index! 'set! i 0 (dec (length bs)))\n  (check-byte! 'set! v)\n  (put! bs i v)\n  nil)\n\n\n(defn copy!\n  \"M. Copy `len` bytes from `src[src-pos ...]` into target\n   `dest[dest-pos ...]`; nil. Both ranges are checked before any write,\n   and overlapping ranges in one array copy as memmove: backward when the\n   destination starts after the source, forward otherwise.\"\n  [src src-pos dest dest-pos len]\n  (let [sn (length src)\n        dn (length dest)]\n    (check-index! 'copy! len 0 (min sn dn))\n    (check-index! 'copy! src-pos 0 (- sn len))\n    (check-index! 'copy! dest-pos 0 (- dn len)))\n  (if (and (identical? src dest) (> dest-pos src-pos))\n    (loop [i (dec len)]\n      (when (<= 0 i)\n        (aset dest (+ dest-pos i) (aget src (+ src-pos i)))\n        (recur (dec i))))\n    (dotimes [i len]\n      (aset dest (+ dest-pos i) (aget src (+ src-pos i)))))\n  nil)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc | sed -n '132,181p;424,476p;579,620p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc | sed -n '1055,1110p;1270,1325p;1410,1445p'; cat BRIEF-j6g-fix.md; ls -la /opt/homebrew/bin/jolt; rg --files -uuu /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs | rg '/(bb|cljstyle)\"'$'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc | sed -n '132,181p;424,476p;579,620p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc | sed -n '1055,1110p;1270,1325p;1410,1445p'; cat BRIEF-j6g-fix.md; ls -la /opt/homebrew/bin/jolt; rg --files -uuu /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs | rg '/(bb|cljstyle)\"'$'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"   132\t(defn- drain-input\n   133\t  \"Read up to `input-budget` input elements, total over every `next` outcome.\n   134\t   A gap means typed lines were evicted: the loss is published, the recovery\n   135\t   cursor is taken, and none of the missing input is evaluated.\"\n   136\t  [state]\n   137\t  (loop [remaining input-budget\n   138\t         state state\n   139\t         lines []]\n   140\t    (if (or (zero? remaining) (nil? (:input-cursor state)))\n   141\t      [state lines]\n   142\t      (let [result (stream/next (:input state) (:input-cursor state))\n   143\t            outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)]\n   144\t        (case outcome\n   145\t          :dao.stream/ok\n   146\t          (recur (dec remaining)\n   147\t                 (assoc state :input-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor result))\n   148\t                 (conj lines (get (:dao.stream/value result) line-key)))\n   149\t\n   150\t          :dao.stream/gap\n   151\t          (recur (dec remaining)\n   152\t                 (-> state\n   153\t                     (assoc :input-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor result))\n   154\t                     (publish :yin.repl.driver/notice\n   155\t                              \";; input lost: typed lines were evicted before this step\"))\n   156\t                 lines)\n   157\t\n   158\t          :dao.stream/blocked\n   159\t          [(assoc state :input-ledger outcome) lines]\n   160\t\n   161\t          [(-> state\n   162\t               (assoc :input-ledger outcome)\n   163\t               (publish :yin.repl.driver/notice\n   164\t                        (str \";; input \" (name outcome))))\n   165\t           lines])))))\n   166\t\n   167\t\n   168\t;; =============================================================================\n   169\t;; Local and remote input\n   170\t;; =============================================================================\n   171\t\n   172\t(defn- evaluate-locally\n   173\t  [state line]\n   174\t  (let [[repl text] (repl/eval-input (:repl state) line)]\n   175\t    (-> state\n   176\t        (assoc :repl repl)\n   177\t        (assoc :running? (boolean (:running? repl)))\n   178\t        (publish :yin.repl.driver/result text))))\n   179\t\n   180\t\n   181\t(defn- rpc-client\n   424\t(defn- handle-line\n   425\t  [state line]\n   426\t  (let [command (adapter/local-command line)]\n   427\t    (cond\n   428\t      ;; A shell that has quit evaluates nothing more.  Hosts append an\n   429\t      ;; end-of-input `(quit)` that a typed `(quit)` has already answered.\n   430\t      (not (:running? state)) state\n   431\t\n   432\t      (not (string? line))\n   433\t      (publish state :yin.repl.driver/diagnostic\n   434\t               (str \";; ignored non-string input: \"\n   435\t                    (pr-str (data/summarize line diagnostic-bounds))))\n   436\t\n   437\t      (str/blank? line) state\n   438\t\n   439\t      ;; Local control commands bypass the remote queue, so a stuck or slow\n   440\t      ;; remote request cannot trap the operator.\n   441\t      (= 'connect command) (connect-command state line)\n   442\t\n   443\t      (= 'disconnect command) (disconnect state)\n   444\t\n   445\t      (= 'repl-state command)\n   446\t      (cond-> (evaluate-locally state line)\n   447\t        (:connection state)\n   448\t        (publish :yin.repl.driver/result\n   449\t                 (repl/format-value (connect/summary (:connection state)))))\n   450\t\n   451\t      (and (remote-routed? state) (not command))\n   452\t      (cond\n   453\t        ;; A dropped or ended remote evaluates nothing.  The line was never\n   454\t        ;; sent, so it waits for an explicit reattachment decision.\n   455\t        (remote-terminal state)\n   456\t        (-> state\n   457\t            (update :queued conj line)\n   458\t            (publish :yin.repl.driver/notice\n   459\t                     \";; not connected: queued until (connect …) reattaches\"))\n   460\t\n   461\t        ;; `:unsent` is the RPC client's own retained envelope, and the\n   462\t        ;; authority on whether the request path is free: submitting here would\n   463\t        ;; resend it and discard this line.  `:retrying` is only the driver's\n   464\t        ;; record of which line that envelope carries.\n   465\t        (or (:outstanding state) (:retrying state) (remote-unsent? state))\n   466\t        (queue-line state line)\n   467\t\n   468\t        :else (submit-remote state line queue-line))\n   469\t\n   470\t      :else (evaluate-locally state line))))\n   471\t\n   472\t\n   473\t;; =============================================================================\n   474\t;; Remote completions\n   475\t;; =============================================================================\n   476\t\n   579\t(defn repl-step\n   580\t  \"Advance the REPL once.  Called by exactly one ticker per host; never loops on\n   581\t   `:dao.stream/blocked`.  `now` is the host's clock reading, recorded but not\n   582\t   waited on: this layer has no deadline of its own.\"\n   583\t  [state now]\n   584\t  (let [state (assoc state :last-tick now)\n   585\t        state (retry-unsent state)\n   586\t        ;; Completions and lifecycle are observed before this tick's lines are\n   587\t        ;; handled, so a `(connect …)` typed in the same tick as the drop that\n   588\t        ;; makes it legal sees the terminal fact rather than being told the\n   589\t        ;; shell is already connected.\n   590\t        state (poll-remote state now)\n   591\t        state (observe-connection state)\n   592\t        [state lines] (drain-input state)\n   593\t        state (reduce handle-line state lines)]\n   594\t    (release-queue state)))\n  1055\t   input medium, and a refused one stops the shell.  The custody control\n  1056\t   plane is stepped next, before the refusal and admission branches, so\n  1057\t   renewals, pending releases and request retries continue during\n  1058\t   hydration and past a refusal.  A `--port` process\n  1059\t   serves one shared shell, as v1's atom made it: the driver evaluates this\n  1060\t   tick's local\n  1061\t   lines first, so a definition typed at the local prompt is already in the\n  1062\t   shell the endpoint evaluates remote requests against in the same tick, and\n  1063\t   the endpoint's shell (remote definitions included) is threaded back\n  1064\t   before the next tick.  The custody program step follows the driver's own\n  1065\t   step and precedes the endpoint's; once the shell has stopped it is\n  1066\t   replaced by the stop latch, so no custody program call runs after\n  1067\t   `:running?` turns false.  A require parked on a closure load the node\n  1068\t   ended this tick is re-checked once, before any typed line, with no line\n  1069\t   of its own (yin.repl/recheck-on-tick, yin.vm.linker.dht.md 8.2),\n  1070\t   and linker progress resumes a parked run (7.5): its text prints after the\n  1071\t   node's lines.  Returns `[state server lines]`;\n  1072\t   the caller only prints.\"\n  1073\t  [state server now]\n  1074\t  (let [[repl dht-lines events] (repl.dht/step (:repl state) now)\n  1075\t        state (custody-control-step (assoc state :repl repl))]\n  1076\t    (cond\n  1077\t      (repl.dht/refusal repl)\n  1078\t      [(custody-stop (assoc state :running? false)) server dht-lines]\n  1079\t\n  1080\t      (not (repl.dht/admitting? repl))\n  1081\t      [state server dht-lines]\n  1082\t\n  1083\t      :else\n  1084\t      (let [[repl rechecked] (shell/recheck-on-tick (:repl state) events)\n  1085\t            dht-lines (cond-> dht-lines\n  1086\t                        (seq rechecked) (conj rechecked))\n  1087\t            state (assoc state :repl repl)\n  1088\t            stepped (driver/repl-step state now)\n  1089\t            stepped (if (:running? stepped)\n  1090\t                      (custody-program-step stepped)\n  1091\t                      (custody-stop stepped))\n  1092\t            [entries state'] (driver/take-outbox stepped)\n  1093\t            server' (when server\n  1094\t                      (serve/step (assoc-in server [:repl] (:repl state'))\n  1095\t                                  now))\n  1096\t            [server-entries server''] (if server'\n  1097\t                                        (serve/take-outbox server')\n  1098\t                                        [[] nil])\n  1099\t            state'' (if server'' (assoc state' :repl (:repl server'')) state')]\n  1100\t        [state'' server'' (into dht-lines\n  1101\t                                (map entry-text)\n  1102\t                                (into (vec entries) server-entries))]))))\n  1103\t\n  1104\t\n  1105\t(defn moved?\n  1106\t  \"The tick owner's cadence bit, computed from this tick's own results: true\n  1107\t   when there are lines to print, when the endpoint reports movement (a\n  1108\t   woken probe, a published notice), or when either composition still owes a\n  1109\t   write -- the shell's own or a custody control-plane one.  A pending write\n  1110\t   keeps cadence at the base interval; it must never wait out a backoff\n  1270\t        journal, so what the budget leaves outstanding is a restart's to\n  1271\t        resend.  Answers the drained state.\"\n  1272\t  [state server now sleep!]\n  1273\t  (if (shutdown-enter? state server)\n  1274\t    (loop [state (update state :repl repl.dht/stop!)\n  1275\t           server (some-> server serve/stop!)\n  1276\t           remaining stop-ticks]\n  1277\t      (let [[state' server' lines _stopped?]\n  1278\t            (shutdown-tick state server (now))]\n  1279\t        (doseq [line lines]\n  1280\t          (println line))\n  1281\t        (flush)\n  1282\t        (cond\n  1283\t          (shutdown-drained? state' server') state'\n  1284\t          (zero? remaining) (do (println stop-timeout-text) state')\n  1285\t          :else (let [round-end (+ (now) tick-millis)]\n  1286\t                  ;; a sleep readiness ends early pumps, then sleeps the\n  1287\t                  ;; rest: an early wake cannot spend a round (R17)\n  1288\t                  (loop []\n  1289\t                    (sleep! (max 0 (- round-end (now))))\n  1290\t                    (when (< (now) round-end) (recur)))\n  1291\t                  (recur state' server' (dec remaining))))))\n  1292\t    state))\n  1293\t\n  1294\t\n  1295\t(defn run-owner!\n  1296\t  \"Serial shell owner shared by the JVM and jolt. Host policy supplies\n  1297\t   clock, interruptible sleep and status-aware exit. No producer evaluates.\"\n  1298\t  [state server headless? now sleep! exit!]\n  1299\t  (loop [state state\n  1300\t         server server\n  1301\t         cadence (cadence/init default-cadence)]\n  1302\t    (let [[state' server' lines] (step-all state server\n  1303\t                                           (now))]\n  1304\t      (doseq [line lines]\n  1305\t        (println line))\n  1306\t      (flush)\n  1307\t      (if (:running? state')\n  1308\t        (do (when (and (not headless?) (prompt-owed? state state' lines))\n  1309\t              (do (print prompt) (flush)))\n  1310\t            (let [{:keys [cadence-state sleep-ms]}\n  1311\t                  (cadence/cadence-step cadence\n  1312\t                                        (moved? state' server' lines))]\n  1313\t              (sleep! sleep-ms)\n  1314\t              (recur state' server' cadence-state)))\n  1315\t        (let [state' (drain-owner! state' server' now sleep!)]\n  1316\t          (println)\n  1317\t          (close-index-store! state')\n  1318\t          (flush)\n  1319\t          (exit! (exit-status state')))))))\n  1320\t\n  1321\t\n  1322\t#?(:cljd\n  1323\t   nil\n  1324\t   :jolt nil\n  1325\t   :clj\n  1410\t             (.halt (Runtime/getRuntime) 0)))))))\n  1411\t\n  1412\t\n  1413\t#?(:jolt\n  1414\t   (defn -main\n  1415\t     \"One plain-thread owner. Stdin deposits only; EOF deposits (quit).\n  1416\t      One host WebSocket instance serves the shell, the head board and\n  1417\t      --port; every owner round polls its sockets (headless included) and\n  1418\t      the instance is closed before exit, however the drain ended.\n  1419\t      Saved flags persist in the node directory, as on the JVM (J4d):\n  1420\t      --reset forgets them and --no-state neither reads nor writes them.\"\n  1421\t     [& args]\n  1422\t     (let [adapter (host/websocket)\n  1423\t           started (startup args {:persist? true :adapter adapter})]\n  1424\t       (when (contains? started :exit) (exit-with! started))\n  1425\t       (if-some [refusal (:refusal started)]\n  1426\t         (refuse! refusal)\n  1427\t         (let [{:keys [opts state server]} started\n  1428\t               headless? (boolean (:headless? opts))\n  1429\t               eof? (atom false)\n  1430\t               w (wake/make-wake)\n  1431\t               line! (fn [line]\n  1432\t                       (if (nil? line)\n  1433\t                         (do (reset! eof? true)\n  1434\t                             (driver/submit-line! (:input state) \"(quit)\"))\n  1435\t                         (driver/submit-line! (:input state) line)))\n  1436\t               sleep! (fn [ms]\n  1437\t                        (wake/sleep-fds! w ms (:pump adapter)\n  1438\t                                         (when-not (or headless? @eof?) line!)))]\n  1439\t           (doseq [line (banner opts)] (println line))\n  1440\t           (when-not headless? (print prompt))\n  1441\t           (flush)\n  1442\t           ;; the exit status leaves through System/exit, which skips the\n  1443\t           ;; finally, so the exit path closes the instance itself too\n  1444\t           (try\n  1445\t             (run-owner! state server headless? #(System/currentTimeMillis)\n# J6g fix round: the workload W run hangs — attribute, guard, and re-measure\n\n(Re-pasted from the orchestrator's dispatch; the agy rounds died twice on\nthis unit, so this fix round is dispatched to codex per the terminal-state\nrule's escalation.)\n\n## What happened (the orchestrator's verification run, jupiter, j6ggate18)\n\nThe workload W harness compiled and ran: server listening, peer B\nconnected and upgraded, peer A connected and upgraded, frame length\n4,194,318 bytes, \"Entering owner round loop...\" — then 100% CPU spin for\n69 minutes, no output flush, no transfer completion. Killed at rc=143.\n\nThe pre-registered criterion (BRIEF-j6g.md, unchanged): A's 4 MiB message\ndelivered once within a ~60 s window while B samples p99 ≤ 250 ms with\n≥ 600 samples. Nothing measurable was produced.\n\n## Your tasks\n\n1. **Attribute the spin.** Two hypotheses — distinguish them with reads\n   (you cannot run anything):\n   (a) a harness defect: `write-all!`'s retry loop (`poll-one fd pollout\n   2000` then `send-chunk!`) spins if poll returns writable while send\n   answers :would-block, or if the loop never advances off 0; and there\n   is no max-runtime guard, so any stall hangs forever.\n   (b) a real composition finding: the REPL's owner round serves peer B\n   but never drains peer A's 4 MiB transfer (the exact starvation\n   workload W exists to expose).\n   Read src/dev/jolt_workload_w.clj's write-all!/run-workload-w loop and\n   the driver's owner round in src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc (the\n   sleep-fds! + step path). State which you conclude, with file:line.\n2. **Fix the harness defects** regardless of (b):\n   - a max-runtime guard: the whole workload terminates with a FAILURE\n     report (p99 absent, samples counted, elapsed) after a hard cap\n     (5 minutes), never hanging;\n   - the write-all! loop gets a no-progress guard: N consecutive\n     :would-block polls without a byte advancing = transfer stalled →\n     report and abort the transfer leg (this is data: the criterion\n     failing, honestly measured);\n   - the sampler flushes its running p99/sample-count to stdout every\n     10 s so a stuck run leaves evidence.\n3. **If (b) is your conclusion** (the adapter starves A): do NOT patch\n   the adapter — report it as the finding with the reads that support it.\n   The Architect rules on adapter changes.\n4. cljstyle clean; no collab/ path in comments.\n\n## Reporting\n\nWrite BRIEF-j6g-fix-findings.md in this workspace with: the attribution,\nthe guards added, and what the next verification run should show under\neach hypothesis.\nlrwxr-xr-x@ 1 sto  admin  29 Sep  6 13:50 /opt/homebrew/bin/jolt -> ../Cellar/jolt/0.8.3/bin/jolt\n/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/babashka/1.12.218/bb\n/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/babashka/1.13.225/bb\n/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/babashka/1.13.223/bb\n/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/cljstyle/0.17.642/cljstyle\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
