{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '1100,1240p;1920,2050p;2120,2180p'; nl -ba src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/pump.jolt | sed -n '1,100p'; rg -n 'plan v3|A7|Workload W|workload W|R8.*R9' docs collab/jolt -g '*.md' | tail -70; ls /Users/sto/workspace\"","aggregated_output":"  1100\t  (let [append (::result-append vm')\n  1101\t        render (:render (::frontend state'))\n  1102\t        [state'' output-text results]\n  1103\t        (drain-output (commit-frontend\n  1104\t                        (assoc state' :vm (dissoc vm' ::result-append))))\n  1105\t        round (round-id state')\n  1106\t        current (filterv #(= round (:round %)) results)]\n  1107\t    (if (seq current)\n  1108\t      (let [value (:value (peek current))]\n  1109\t        [(record-last-value state state'' value)\n  1110\t         (str output-text\n  1111\t              (if render\n  1112\t                (render value)\n  1113\t                (format-value value (host-fn-namer (:vm state'')))))])\n  1114\t      [state''\n  1115\t       (str output-text \"Error: \" result-loss-text\n  1116\t            (when (and append (not= :dao.stream/ok append))\n  1117\t              (str \" (append: \" (name append) \")\")))])))\n  1118\t\n  1119\t\n  1120\t(defn- drain-observer\n  1121\t  \"Advance one observer past every batch still on its medium, keeping any\n  1122\t   gap it recovers across.  A nil observer — a session without that medium —\n  1123\t   stays nil.\"\n  1124\t  [observer]\n  1125\t  (when observer\n  1126\t    (loop [observer observer]\n  1127\t      (let [{:keys [status] observer' :observer}\n  1128\t            (observer/observe-next observer)]\n  1129\t        (if (#{:ok :gap} status) (recur observer') observer')))))\n  1130\t\n  1131\t\n  1132\t(defn- ingress-gaps\n  1133\t  \"Gaps the evaluation path's observers counted.  The code indexer's are\n  1134\t   its own: an index loss is reported without refusing evaluation.\"\n  1135\t  [state]\n  1136\t  (+ (:ingress-gaps (:observer state) 0)\n  1137\t     (:ingress-gaps (:row-observer state) 0)))\n  1138\t\n  1139\t\n  1140\t(defn- consume-failed-round\n  1141\t  \"Answer a round that threw with a recoverable shell state.\n  1142\t\n  1143\t   The failed input is consumed exactly once: each of the session's\n  1144\t   observers resumes from the session the throw carried — the failing\n  1145\t   stage's, matched by the medium it holds — or from where the round began\n  1146\t   when it carried none, and reads past every batch still on its medium.\n  1147\t   The shell is the only appender and appends one batch per round, so what\n  1148\t   remains is the failed batch alone.  The VM is the one the round began\n  1149\t   with, so a half-run continuation cannot be resumed — and its error\n  1150\t   replayed — by the next input.  Output the round already emitted is\n  1151\t   drained here, once.\"\n  1152\t  [state error]\n  1153\t  (let [carried (get-in (ex-data error) [:session :observer])\n  1154\t        resume (fn [observer]\n  1155\t                 (if (and observer\n  1156\t                          carried\n  1157\t                          (= (:stream carried) (:stream observer)))\n  1158\t                   carried\n  1159\t                   observer))\n  1160\t        drained (assoc state\n  1161\t                       :observer (drain-observer (resume (:observer state)))\n  1162\t                       :row-observer (drain-observer\n  1163\t                                       (resume (:row-observer state)))\n  1164\t                       :indexer (index/skip (:indexer state))\n  1165\t                       :ast-indexer (ast-index/skip (:ast-indexer state)))\n  1166\t        [state' output-text]\n  1167\t        (drain-output\n  1168\t          (cond-> drained\n  1169\t            (> (ingress-gaps drained) (ingress-gaps state))\n  1170\t            (assoc :ingress-loss? true)))]\n  1171\t    [state' (str output-text (format-error error))]))\n  1172\t\n  1173\t\n  1174\t(defn- run-index-stage\n  1175\t  \"Drive the code indexer's observer over `program-out`: it commits each\n  1176\t   forwarded packet as one transaction and publishes the covered indexes.\n  1177\t   It runs before the evaluator, so a program is indexed whether its VM\n  1178\t   returns, parks, or raises; the two observers meet only at the medium.\"\n  1179\t  [state]\n  1180\t  (update state :indexer index/step (:round state)))\n  1181\t\n  1182\t\n  1183\t(defn- run-ast-index-stage\n  1184\t  \"Drive the AST indexer's observer over `program-out`: it adds each\n  1185\t   forwarded packet's rows and occurrences to the session's `$ast` and\n  1186\t   `$occ` relations.  It runs before the evaluator for the same reason the\n  1187\t   code indexer does, and neither indexer reads the other.\"\n  1188\t  [state]\n  1189\t  (update state :ast-indexer ast-index/step))\n  1190\t\n  1191\t\n  1192\t(defn- with-index-notice\n  1193\t  \"Append what the round's index steps lost, if anything, to its result\n  1194\t   text, one line per notice in the order given; the evaluation's own\n  1195\t   answer is unchanged.\"\n  1196\t  [[state text] notices]\n  1197\t  (if-let [notice (some->> (remove nil? notices) seq (str/join \"\\n\"))]\n  1198\t    [state (if (str/blank? text) notice (str text \"\\n\" notice))]\n  1199\t    [state text]))\n  1200\t\n  1201\t\n  1202\t(defn- run-expander-stage\n  1203\t  \"Drive the expander over `program-in` and drain its summary.  It expands\n  1204\t   each observed batch and appends the tree packet to `program-out`; a\n  1205\t   failed expansion forwards nothing, yet its cursor advances (yin.vm.macro.md\n  1206\t   decision 12).  Returns the state with the expander's progress and the\n  1207\t   drained `{:errors :forwarded}` summary.\"\n  1208\t  [state]\n  1209\t  (let [{:keys [observer consumer]}\n  1210\t        (macro/step {:observer (:observer state), :consumer (:expander state)})\n  1211\t        [expander summary] (macro/drain-errors consumer)]\n  1212\t    [(assoc state :observer observer :expander expander) summary]))\n  1213\t\n  1214\t\n  1215\t(defn- run-evaluator-stage\n  1216\t  \"Drive the evaluator's observer over `program-out`: it loads each\n  1217\t   expanded tree packet into the VM, runs it, and answers its value on the\n  1218\t   output medium.  The two stages meet only at `program-out`; neither calls\n  1219\t   the other.\"\n  1220\t  [{:keys [load-program output-stream] :as state}]\n  1221\t  (let [{:keys [observer] vm :consumer}\n  1222\t        (observer/run-on-stream {:observer (:row-observer state),\n  1223\t                                 :consumer (:vm state)}\n  1224\t                                engine/ready-for-ingress?\n  1225\t                                load-program\n  1226\t                                (make-runner output-stream (round-id state)))]\n  1227\t    (assoc state :row-observer observer :vm vm)))\n  1228\t\n  1229\t\n  1230\t(defn- format-expansion-errors\n  1231\t  [errors]\n  1232\t  (str/join \"\\n\" (map #(str \"Error: Macro expansion failed: \" (format-value %))\n  1233\t                      errors)))\n  1234\t\n  1235\t\n  1236\t(defn- link-waiting?\n  1237\t  \"True while `vm` parks on a link wait: the two link states `require`\n  1238\t   parks in, or the install it waits on (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.2).\n  1239\t   These are the reasons the shell's interpreter can move, so they are\n  1240\t   the ones a round drives before reporting the VM wedged.\"\n  1920\t                          \"\\nTrusted: \"\n  1921\t                          (pr-str (vec (sort (:trusted (:admission state))))))]\n  1922\t      reset [(rebuild-session\n  1923\t               (configure-admission state (:initial-admission state))\n  1924\t               (:vm-type state))\n  1925\t             (str (get vm-labels (:vm-type state)) \" reset\")]\n  1926\t      abandon (abandon-pending state)\n  1927\t      help [state help-text]\n  1928\t      repl-state [state (format-value (repl-state state))]\n  1929\t      quit [(assoc state :running? false) \"Bye\"]\n  1930\t      telemetry [state telemetry-text]\n  1931\t      host [state host-text]\n  1932\t      [state (str \"Error: Unknown Yin REPL command \" (pr-str command))])))\n  1933\t\n  1934\t\n  1935\t(defn- eval-compiled\n  1936\t  \"Evaluate a program `compile-input` or `compile-source` lowered.  What\n  1937\t   its lowering left (`::frontend`: the session and the `:render` hook) is\n  1938\t   staged on the round and committed only where the round's VM state\n  1939\t   survives: when the program halts, now or when its parked require\n  1940\t   completes (`finalize-eval`).  A round that fails, rolls back, or is\n  1941\t   abandoned keeps the shell's previous `:frontend-session`.\"\n  1942\t  [state ast]\n  1943\t  (let [staged (::frontend (meta ast))\n  1944\t        [state' text] (eval-program (cond-> state\n  1945\t                                      staged (assoc ::frontend staged))\n  1946\t                                    ast)]\n  1947\t    [(dissoc state' ::frontend) text]))\n  1948\t\n  1949\t\n  1950\t(defn- eval-parsed*\n  1951\t  \"The parse dispatch of one line, against a shell with no require to\n  1952\t   re-check.\"\n  1953\t  [state trimmed parsed]\n  1954\t  (try\n  1955\t    (let [forms (:forms parsed)\n  1956\t          form (when (= 1 (count forms)) (first forms))]\n  1957\t      (cond\n  1958\t        (and form (command-form? form)) (handle-command state form)\n  1959\t        (and form (datom-stream? form)) (eval-program state (vec form))\n  1960\t        (and form (ast-map? form)) (eval-program state form)\n  1961\t        forms (eval-compiled state (compile-input state trimmed forms))\n  1962\t        (forms-input? state) [state (format-error (:error parsed))]\n  1963\t        :else (eval-compiled state (compile-source state trimmed))))\n  1964\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) error\n  1965\t      (let [[state' output-text] (drain-output state)]\n  1966\t        [state' (str output-text (format-error error))]))))\n  1967\t\n  1968\t\n  1969\t(defn- fold-queued\n  1970\t  \"Evaluate the lines retained while a require was pending, in the order\n  1971\t   they were typed, each exactly once, and join their texts.  A line that\n  1972\t   parks the shell on a require of its own stops the fold: the lines\n  1973\t   after it stay retained, in order, on the new `:pending-run`.\"\n  1974\t  [[state text] queued]\n  1975\t  (loop [state state\n  1976\t         text text\n  1977\t         [in & more :as queued] (seq queued)]\n  1978\t    (cond\n  1979\t      (empty? queued) [state text]\n  1980\t      (:pending-run state) [(update-in state [:pending-run :pending-lines]\n  1981\t                                       (fnil into []) queued)\n  1982\t                            text]\n  1983\t      :else (let [[state' text'] (eval-parsed* state\n  1984\t                                               (:trimmed in)\n  1985\t                                               (:parsed in))]\n  1986\t              (recur state' (str text \"\\n\" text') more)))))\n  1987\t\n  1988\t\n  1989\t(defn- recheck-pending*\n  1990\t  \"One bounded re-check of the shell's `:pending-run`: serve the\n  1991\t   interpreter, run the parked VM, and either answer its value -- the\n  1992\t   round the require began in finally completes, and the lines retained\n  1993\t   while it was pending, then `input`, evaluate against it -- consult\n  1994\t   the link policy when the re-check leaves the run pending, `:checks`\n  1995\t   counting this pending run's re-checks that made no progress and\n  1996\t   resetting on one that did, or, when the re-check raised the link's\n  1997\t   refusal, return the shell to the round's base with the error as text\n  1998\t   and evaluate `input` there.  `input` is nil for the host's\n  1999\t   `recheck-pending`, which evaluates no line of its own.\"\n  2000\t  [state input initial-progress]\n  2001\t  (let [parked (:pending-run state)]\n  2002\t    (try\n  2003\t      (let [[state' vm' pending progress?] (drive-links state (:vm parked)\n  2004\t                                                        initial-progress)]\n  2005\t        (if (vm/halted? vm')\n  2006\t          (let [vm'' (engine/restore-initial-env (:env (:base parked)) vm')\n  2007\t                [st text] (finalize-eval state\n  2008\t                                         (cond-> (assoc state' :vm vm'')\n  2009\t                                           (:frontend parked)\n  2010\t                                           (assoc ::frontend\n  2011\t                                                  (:frontend parked)))\n  2012\t                                         (tokenize state' vm''))]\n  2013\t            (fold-queued [(assoc st :vm vm'' :pending-run nil) text]\n  2014\t                         (cond-> (vec (:pending-lines parked))\n  2015\t                           input (conj input))))\n  2016\t          (let [checks (if progress? 0 (inc (or (:checks parked) 0)))\n  2017\t                parked' (cond-> (assoc parked\n  2018\t                                       :vm vm'\n  2019\t                                       :links pending\n  2020\t                                       :checks checks)\n  2021\t                          input (update :pending-lines\n  2022\t                                        (fnil conj []) input))\n  2023\t                [st text] (drain-output (assoc state'\n  2024\t                                               :vm vm'\n  2025\t                                               :pending-run parked'))]\n  2026\t            (consult-link-policy st text (pending-text pending)))))\n  2027\t      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) error\n  2028\t        (let [[st text] (drain-output state)\n  2029\t              d (ex-data error)]\n  2030\t          (fold-queued\n  2031\t            [(carry-served (assoc st\n  2032\t                                  :vm (query/discard-answers\n  2033\t                                        (carry-link-identity\n  2034\t                                          (:base parked)\n  2035\t                                          {:id-counter (::link-counter d)\n  2036\t                                           :origins (::link-origins d)})\n  2037\t                                        (:query-pair st))\n  2038\t                                  :pending-run nil)\n  2039\t                           d)\n  2040\t             (str text\n  2041\t                  (format-error error)\n  2042\t                  (dropped-lines-text (count (:pending-lines parked))))]\n  2043\t            (cond-> [] input (conj input))))))))\n  2044\t\n  2045\t\n  2046\t(defn recheck-pending\n  2047\t  \"One re-check of the shell's `:pending-run` without an input line --\n  2048\t   the step an unattended host drives at its own cadence\n  2049\t   (yin.repl.link-policy.md section 4): serve the interpreter, run the\n  2050\t   parked VM, and consult the link policy when the run is still\n  2120\t\n  2121\t(defn- input-probe\n  2122\t  \"The completeness probe of the session's frontend, or nil when it has\n  2123\t   none or none is installed (the compile then reports it).\"\n  2124\t  [state]\n  2125\t  (:probe (usable-binding (select-frontend (:frontends state) (:lang state)))))\n  2126\t\n  2127\t\n  2128\t(defn eval-input\n  2129\t  \"Evaluate one input line locally, returning `[state text]`.\n  2130\t\n  2131\t   Input that is not yet a whole submission is retained as `:pending-input`\n  2132\t   and produces no text: for a frontend with a `:probe` the probe decides\n  2133\t   and the line is kept verbatim (whitespace can be inside a string);\n  2134\t   otherwise the brackets must balance.  Nothing here is asynchronous: the\n  2135\t   driver, not this namespace, decides when the next step happens.\"\n  2136\t  [state line]\n  2137\t  (let [probe (input-probe state)\n  2138\t        pending (or (:pending-input state) \"\")\n  2139\t        line (if probe line (str/trim line))\n  2140\t        combined (if (str/blank? pending)\n  2141\t                   line\n  2142\t                   (str pending \"\\n\" line))]\n  2143\t    (cond\n  2144\t      (and probe (str/blank? combined))\n  2145\t      [(assoc state :pending-input nil) \"\"]\n  2146\t\n  2147\t      (if probe\n  2148\t        (= :incomplete (probe combined))\n  2149\t        (pos? (bracket-balance combined)))\n  2150\t      [(assoc state :pending-input combined) \"\"]\n  2151\t\n  2152\t      :else\n  2153\t      (let [state' (assoc state :pending-input nil)\n  2154\t            parsed (try {:forms (read-forms combined)}\n  2155\t                        (catch #?(:cljd Object\n  2156\t                                  :clj Exception\n  2157\t                                  :cljs js/Error) error\n  2158\t                          {:error error}))]\n  2159\t        (eval-parsed state' combined parsed)))))\n  2160\t\n  2161\t\n  2162\t(defn repl-state\n  2163\t  \"A serializable summary of shell state.\n  2164\t\n  2165\t   The stream summaries read the ledger rather than asking a handle whether it\n  2166\t   is closed: dao.stream has no `closed?`, and an idle medium has no last\n  2167\t   operation.\n  2168\t   The program media are the composition's own, observed beside the VM, so\n  2169\t   the shell reports what it knows of them — the declared capacity, the gaps\n  2170\t   the session's observers counted, and whether a loss has already refused\n  2171\t   further evaluation.  Each `:pending` entry carries the link policy's\n  2172\t   name (`:manual` or `:fn`) and the pending run's `:checks`, so a host\n  2173\t   can display why a run is still waiting (yin.repl.link-policy.md\n  2174\t   section 3.5).  `:macros` maps each macro the expander's store holds\n  2175\t   to its lambda's root address (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1).  `:index` is the\n  2176\t   code indexer's `yin.repl.index/status`: whether every committed program\n  2177\t   is published, whether a gap lost the indexer, and its last failure.\n  2178\t   `:ast-index` is the AST indexer's `yin.repl.ast-index/status`: the sizes\n  2179\t   of its `$ast` and `$occ` relations, whether a gap lost it, and why it\n  2180\t   failed.\"\n     1\t(ns dao.stream.ws.pump\n     2\t  \"Jolt-only owner-thread pump under the native WebSocket host adapter (J6d;\n     3\t   J6 plan rulings A1-A5). One instance per `create` call: its registry of\n     4\t   descriptors, write queues, close records and deadlines live in that\n     5\t   instance and nowhere else, so two instances never share state.\n     6\t\n     7\t   Ownership (A1). Every entry runs on the thread that drives the instance;\n     8\t   nothing here waits, parks or polls a socket. A driver polls the `interest`\n     9\t   descriptors until the earlier of its cadence and `next-deadline`\n    10\t   (`jolt.io-poller/clock-ms`, nil when nothing is due), then hands the\n    11\t   `[[fd revents] ...]` it observed to `pump!`, `[]` on a timeout: every\n    12\t   call runs the due expiries. A composition that never pumps an instance\n    13\t   makes no progress, by design.\n    14\t\n    15\t   Bounded turn (A1). One `pump!` visits each ready descriptor at most once,\n    16\t   starting after the one visited last in the previous turn (round robin in\n    17\t   registration order). A connection visit attempts at most one write of\n    18\t   the head of its queue and reads at most one chunk (one reused 64 KiB\n    19\t   native buffer); a listener visit accepts at most `accept-batch`.\n    20\t\n    21\t   One ordered write path (A3). Each connection owns one FIFO of whole wire\n    22\t   segments; the head carries an offset and is never rewritten. `send!`\n    23\t   writes at once only into an empty FIFO and queues the unsent tail;\n    24\t   otherwise it appends. Protocol output (pongs, close frames) joins the\n    25\t   same FIFO at generation time; nothing has priority. `send!` answers nil\n    26\t   or `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}`, never false.\n    27\t   `queued-bytes` counts every byte handed over and not yet accepted by the\n    28\t   kernel, control frames included; 0 after the terminal.\n    29\t\n    30\t   Two connection modes. A :raw connection (an HTTP upgrade in progress, or\n    31\t   a plain byte stream) delivers `:on-data` chunks, `:on-eof` once and\n    32\t   `:on-error` once. `upgraded!` turns it into a :ws connection, which parses\n    33\t   its input one frame at a time through the injected `:protocol`\n    34\t   (`{:parser :parse-frame :encode-frame :close-payload :mask-key}`; the\n    35\t   parse contract is `(parse-frame state chunk offset)` =>\n    36\t   `[event-or-nil state' offset']` with `:message`, `:ping`, `:pong`,\n    37\t   `:close` and `:fail` events, a close-frame failure carrying `:close?\n    38\t   true`), answers each ping with one pong, delivers `:on-message`, and\n    39\t   reports exactly one `:on-closed` terminal.\n    40\t\n    41\t   Control budget (A4). At most `max-pongs` pending pongs per connection plus\n    42\t   one reserved close slot. When the pongs fill the budget the connection\n    43\t   stops parsing after that frame, leaves read interest and keeps the\n    44\t   unparsed rest of its chunk; when a drain frees a pong slot the rest is\n    45\t   parsed before any new read, and read interest returns once it is\n    46\t   consumed. The close slot never counts against the budget and is never\n    47\t   refused.\n    48\t\n    49\t   Close record (A5). `{:local nil|:queued|:sent, :peer nil|:received,\n    50\t   :peer-status nil|:absent|:invalid|code, :code, :reason, :initiator,\n    51\t   :deadline}`. The first of a local `close!` and the peer's close frame\n    52\t   starts the 5 s `close-deadline`; the first local request wins. The\n    53\t   terminal code: a completed handshake reports the local code when this\n    54\t   side initiated, else the peer's status (an empty close reports 1005, an\n    55\t   invalid one 1002); a peer close followed by end of stream before the\n    56\t   response left reports the peer's status; end of stream, reset or a\n    57\t   transfer failure without a peer close reports 1006; deadline expiry in\n    58\t   any state reports 1006. A parser `:fail` without `:close?` fails the\n    59\t   connection (RFC 6455 section 7.1.7) and opens no handshake: the record\n    60\t   gets `:failed? true`, the close frame takes the reserved slot, input is\n    61\t   read only to see end of stream and discarded, and once the frame is\n    62\t   written the terminal is the local code with cause `:fail`; the peer's\n    63\t   reply is never parsed. A `:fail` after a local `close!` keeps that\n    64\t   request's frame and code and ends the same way. 1005 and 1006 are never\n    65\t   put on the wire. A ping that arrives once a local close is queued gets no\n    66\t   pong: the pong would queue behind our close frame, RFC 6455 section 5.5.1\n    67\t   forbids only data frames after a close, and no Autobahn case exercises\n    68\t   it.\n    69\t\n    70\t   Listeners. Accepted sockets register with `:listener` and `:upgrading?`;\n    71\t   at `max-pending-upgrades` upgrading sockets (or `:max-connections` owned\n    72\t   ones) the listener leaves the interest set until a slot frees. An\n    73\t   upgrade not completed within its timeout is released and reported to\n    74\t   `:on-upgrade-expired`. `close-listener!` closes the listener descriptor;\n    75\t   `drained?` answers true once no connection it owns is left, and its\n    76\t   `:on-drained` is called once then. `lower-deadlines!` brings the close\n    77\t   deadline of every connection a listener owns to at most a given time.\n    78\t\n    79\t   Callbacks. Data callbacks (`:on-data`, `:on-message`) run inside the\n    80\t   visit. Terminals and other lifecycle reports run at the start or end of\n    81\t   a turn, never inside an entry the composition called; `next-deadline`\n    82\t   answers now while one is owed.\n    83\t\n    84\t   Native memory: the read and write buffers exist while the registry is\n    85\t   non-empty and are freed when its last descriptor leaves.\"\n    86\t  (:require\n    87\t    [dao.stream.ws.tcp :as tcp]\n    88\t    [jolt.ffi :as ffi]\n    89\t    [jolt.io-poller :as poller]\n    90\t    [jolt.socket.native :as native]))\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\t(def chunk-bytes\n    94\t  \"The read chunk and the largest single write attempt.\"\n    95\t  (* 64 1024))\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\t(def accept-batch\n    99\t  \"The most connections one listener visit accepts.\"\n   100\t  16)\ncollab/jolt/1793990000000-architect-j6g-diagnose.brief.md:3:# J6g diagnostic round (argon tier): why does peer B starve and A stall under workload W?\ncollab/jolt/1793990000000-architect-j6g-diagnose.brief.md:35:   (plan v3 §2 P2: codec decode enters the round) — if A's final chunk\ncollab/jolt/1793990000000-architect-j6g-diagnose.brief.md:41:4. The driver's sleep-fds!/poll deadline logic (R8/R9) never wakes for\ncollab/jolt/1793990000000-architect-j6g-diagnose.brief.md:55:  exact change, where, and why it preserves A1-A7) — the orchestrator\ncollab/jolt/1793990000000-architect-j6g-diagnose.brief.md:57:- If it is the CRITERION itself (workload W is unsatisfiable as\ncollab/jolt/1792425688000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-review-r5.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:53:- The static DFA layout of ANTLR C++ generated code (R2), the C++ token-buffer fill behavior (R8), the macOS pthread stack default and `maxdgram` (R5, R9), and whether Cpp helpers exist at grammars-v4@`8af0d4c` (R6).\ncollab/jolt/1792427469000-architect-jolt-lane-plan-review-r7.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:43:4. **Regression check:** R1 (plan:188-192, 