{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'A7|A6|Workload W|workload W|P2|R8|R9' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-orch/orchestrator-logs/1793358019-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-jolt-seat-retake.md | head -70; rg -n 'defn.*step|defn.*value|:steps|step-count|steps' src/cljc/yin/vm/{semantic,engine}.cljc | head -60; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc | sed -n '1,130p'; rg -n 'defn|refresh|publish|step' src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc | tail -40; rg -n 'codec.*decode|decode' src/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc | head -30; git diff -- src/dev/jolt_workload_w.clj src/dev/jolt_workload_w_run.clj\"","aggregated_output":"48:  regression (prime suspect: the R8/R9 sleep-fds! deadline folding), no\n61:  (bb.edn is the only shared file). One P2 rides with J6f's own round:\n169:- The agy round's workload W harness compiled and ran on jupiter\n189:  — the exact thing workload W exists to expose) — the fix round must\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:239:(defn vm-value\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1561:(defn- link-read-step\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1834:(defn- ffi-read-step\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2461:;; later run the same `trace` k steps per round. Ids are never reused:\n     1\t(ns yin.repl.index\n     2\t  \"The shell's code indexer: a `dao.space.index` observer on `program-out`\n     3\t   (docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md).\n     4\t\n     5\t   It is a peer of the evaluator's observer on the same medium, attached\n     6\t   independently and advanced by the evaluation round, never by the\n     7\t   evaluator: neither knows the other.  Each expanded tree packet `[root\n     8\t   rows]` it observes is projected to local `[e a v t m]` AST facts\n     9\t   (yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md §6.5) and committed as ONE atomic transaction\n    10\t   record through a `dao.space.transactor`, which allocates `t`; this\n    11\t   namespace supplies no clock.  Every row of a committed packet is\n    12\t   materialized into the `dao.jing` store in the same round, so its\n    13\t   `:yin/address` facts name content the store holds (yin.vm.linker.dht.md\n    14\t   5.1, rows every round).  After a round that committed, the covered\n    15\t   indexes are published through `transactor/publish!` into that round's\n    16\t   own fresh intake, the intake is drained into the `dao.jing` store, the\n    17\t   manifest is read back, and the intake is dropped: between rounds the\n    18\t   indexer retains its local transaction log and nothing of any\n    19\t   publication.\n    20\t\n    21\t   Cost, accepted as the price of the owner's every-round cadence\n    22\t   (2026-09-28): each publication rebuilds the covered indexes over the\n    23\t   whole retained history, and opening the round's transactor rescans\n    24\t   that history to derive `t`, so a round's index time grows linearly with\n    25\t   the session's committed code and a session's total grows\n    26\t   quadratically.  Memory does not: at most one publication is held, and\n    27\t   only during its round.  An incremental publish in `dao.space.index`\n    28\t   would remove the time growth; nothing here would need to change but\n    29\t   the call.\n    30\t\n    31\t   Every `e` is a transactor-local entity id; the only durable name in the\n    32\t   projection is the `:yin/address` fact each node occurrence carries back\n    33\t   to its row address.  `m` is a local metadata entity, one per program,\n    34\t   carrying `:db/op`, the shell's stable session token, the program's root\n    35\t   address, and the round.  Only code is indexed: no printed output, last\n    36\t   value, or evaluation result enters.\n    37\t\n    38\t   Loss is reported, never hidden, and never stops the evaluator (owner\n    39\t   ruling, 2026-09-28): a gap is counted on the observer (`:ingress-gaps`)\n    40\t   and marks the indexer `:lost?`, after which it consumes packets without\n    41\t   indexing any until reset rebuilds it; a packet that could not be\n    42\t   committed, or a publication that did not become readable, is recorded\n    43\t   under `:failure`, never counted as indexed.  `notice` renders what a\n    44\t   round lost for the shell's round result, and `status` is the\n    45\t   evaluator-independent view `repl-state` reports.  Everything here is a\n    46\t   session-composition value; reset and VM selection rebuild it with the\n    47\t   session.  Over a durable store a new process's indexer is seeded from\n    48\t   the recovered snapshot (`rehydrate`), and a rebuilt session's continues\n    49\t   the old one's index (`carry-over`), so `t` and entity allocation never\n    50\t   restart there.\"\n    51\t  (:require [dao.datom :as datom]\n    52\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    53\t            [dao.space.index :as index]\n    54\t            [dao.space.transactor :as transactor]\n    55\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    56\t            [dao.stream.memory-log :as memory-log]\n    57\t            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n    58\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    59\t            [yin.vm.macro :as macro]))\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t;; =============================================================================\n    63\t;; The §6.5 projection\n    64\t;; =============================================================================\n    65\t\n    66\t(defn- assign-local-ids\n    67\t  \"Give every node occurrence of `node`, the map AST rebuilt from row `id`,\n    68\t   a fresh local entity id as its `:eid`, pairing it with its row through\n    69\t   the §2.3 slot table.  Distinct occurrences of one shared row get distinct\n    70\t   ids, so `vm/ast->datoms` emits every occurrence exactly as it does for a\n    71\t   tree without `:eid`s.  `acc` is `[next-e addresses]`; answers\n    72\t   `[node' acc']`, `addresses` mapping each id to its row address.\"\n    73\t  [rows node id [next-e addresses]]\n    74\t  (let [row (get rows id)\n    75\t        sl