{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"agent_message","text":"I found a concrete source of growing owner-round cost: every submitted loop republishes the code index over the entire retained history. `yin.repl.index` documents this as quadratic total work across a session. That happens before either pump runs, so fair descriptor rotation does not imply timely service.\n\nThe supplied totals do not identify the exact hot subcall. I’m adding opt-in phase tracing to distinguish REPL work from parsing on the next remote run, and fixing the harness checks for actual loop completion and replies that overlap A’s transfer.\n"}}
