{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,95p' src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/jolt.jolt; sed -n '1,80p' src/dev/jolt_ws_probe.clj; rg -n 'A7|A6|plan v3|v3.1' orchestrator-logs | head -45; git status --short -- src/jolt src/cljc src/dev/jolt_workload_w.clj src/dev/jolt_workload_w_run.clj\"","aggregated_output":"(ns dao.stream.ws.jolt\n  \"The jolt host edge for the DaoStream v2 WebSocket transport (J6e; J6\n   plan rulings A1-A6 and the J6e design rulings R1-R7): a dialer and a\n   listener over the owner-thread pump (`dao.stream.ws.pump`) and the\n   nonblocking TCP substrate (`dao.stream.ws.tcp`), the HTTP upgrade from\n   the pure `dao.stream.ws.upgrade` core, and frames from the pure\n   `dao.stream.ws.rfc6455` core with jolt's SHA-1 and masking entropy\n   (`dao.stream.ws.crypto`).\n\n   One instance per `create` call. Its pump registry, connection records\n   and listener records live in that instance and nowhere else; two\n   instances never share state. Nothing here waits, parks or polls: the\n   instance makes progress only while a driver polls `(host-pump instance)`\n   and hands it readiness (A1, A2).\n\n   Seams. `connect!` and a listener's `accept!` get the raw-socket seam\n   `{:send! :close! :queued-bytes}` (the server's also `:ws/subprotocol`).\n   `send!` frames a string as text and host bytes as binary and answers nil\n   or `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}`, never false: the\n   transport decides `full` from `:queued-bytes`, which counts every wire\n   byte not yet accepted by the kernel. `close!` answers nil. Callbacks into\n   the composition use the `dao.stream.ws/adapter` key shape (`:opened!`\n   `:message!` `:binary!` `:closed!` `:too-large!`, plus `:ws/codec` and\n   `:ws/max-frame-bytes` on the dialer's map).\n\n   Terminals (R6). Each upgraded connection reports exactly one\n   `(:closed! code reason)`, from the pump's owed terminal, never inside\n   `send!` or `close!`; a parser failure over the message bound (1009)\n   calls `:too-large!` first. Before its upgrade completes a dialed\n   connection has no frames: every failure there (refused connect, a\n   refused or invalid 101, an unsolicited extension, an oversized head, the\n   upgrade deadline, end of stream) is one `:closed! 1006\n   \\\"dao.stream/connect-failed\\\"`, and a transport `close!` then discards\n   the socket and reports its own code. A pre-upgrade server socket has no\n   composition handle: a refused upgrade answers its HTTP status and\n   deposits one `:upgrade-failed`.\n\n   Policies (A4). Head 8 KiB (incremental), 64 pending upgrades per\n   listener with accept paused at the cap, a 10 s upgrade deadline and a\n   5 s close deadline (both overridable per instance and per listener),\n   the pump's 64 KiB read chunk and 16-pong control budget. The pong budget\n   can stall a peer that pings faster than its socket drains, by design and\n   bounded. A ping that arrives once a local close is queued gets no pong:\n   the pong would queue behind our close frame, RFC 6455 section 5.5.1\n   forbids only data frames after a close, and no Autobahn case exercises\n   it. This side sends no unsolicited pings and ignores pongs.\n\n   Addresses are IPv4 or IPv6 literals or `localhost` (A8): any other host\n   name, and a descriptor naming the `wss` scheme, makes `connect!` answer\n   nil, which the attacher reports as a transport error. Nothing resolves.\n\n   Shutdown (A6). `unbind!` closes the listener at once, discards the\n   sockets it owns that are still upgrading, closes 1001 any upgraded one\n   nobody has closed yet, and lowers every owned connection's close\n   deadline to within `unbind-grace-ms`; the listener's `:stopped` is\n   deposited once its last owned connection has ended. `close-host!` is\n   forced cleanup after the owner loop has ended: every descriptor closed,\n   every buffer released, no deposit and no callback.\n\n   Clocks (R7). Pump deadlines are monotonic (`jolt.io-poller/clock-ms`);\n   the `now` handed to `accept!` is wall-clock milliseconds, the domain the\n   endpoint's acceptance expiry compares against.\"\n  (:require\n    [dao.host.text :as text]\n    [dao.stream.codec :as codec]\n    [dao.stream.ws.crypto :as crypto]\n    [dao.stream.ws.pump :as pump]\n    [dao.stream.ws.rfc6455 :as rfc6455]\n    [dao.stream.ws.tcp :as tcp]\n    [dao.stream.ws.upgrade :as upgrade]\n    [jolt.io-poller :as poller]))\n\n\n(def unbind-grace-ms\n  \"How long connections a stopped listener owns may drain (A6): strictly\n   below the remote channel's 2000 ms stop grace, so `:stopped` precedes\n   its unconfirmed verdict.\"\n  1500)\n\n\n(def ^:private ok {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})\n(def ^:private transport-error {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error})\n\n\n(def ^:private connect-failed \"dao.stream/connect-failed\")\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Instance\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn create\n  \"A fresh instance with an empty registry. `opts`: `:upgrade-timeout-ms`\n   and `:close-deadline-ms` override the pump defaults for every connection\n   this instance makes (a listener's own options take precedence).\"\n;; bb probe:jolt-ws: the J6e gates for the jolt WebSocket host adapter\n;; (dao.stream.ws.jolt over the J6d pump and substrate, with the J6b frame and\n;; upgrade cores and J6c's SHA-1), one section per child jolt process so an\n;; abort cannot erase another section's report:\n;;\n;;   closure    C1: the adapter, pump, substrate, cores and crypto are loaded\n;;              with jolt.socket.native, jolt.io-poller and jolt.ffi; neither\n;;              jolt.socket (the java.net shim) nor dao.stream.transit is;\n;;   handshake  C2: jolt dials jolt (CBOR negotiated, the seam names it); the\n;;              RFC 6455 sample key's accept value through libcrypto SHA-1;\n;;              server refusals (Transit-only offer, no subprotocol, not an\n;;              upgrade, a 9 KiB head, a stalled head at the overridden\n;;              deadline), each with its one :upgrade-failed; client failures\n;;              (426, bad accept key, unsolicited extension, oversized 101,\n;;              refused connect), each exactly one :closed! 1006\n;;              connect-failed; wss:// dials nothing;\n;;   bind       C3: port 0 deposits :bind-succeeded with the kernel's port\n;;              inside bind!; serve! reaches :serving naming it; a port in use\n;;              is a transport error (::bind-failed); 0.0.0.0 by literal;\n;;   address    C4: literals, [::1] and localhost dial; a host name is a\n;;              transport error at attach! with the REPL's reachability text;\n;;              the resolver trap is never sprung;\n;;   io         C5: the transport over the real adapter: exact :queued-bytes\n;;              behind a scripted short write, outbound high water (full, then\n;;              ok after drain), outbound overflow (1008, closed), a message\n;;              over the frame bound (frame-too-large, 1009, never delivered),\n;;              EOF and reset (one :ws/closed 1006), send after failure, a\n;;              150 KB message both ways;\n;;   close      C6: close-ended! 4000 (:ws/ended both sides), 1000\n;;              (:ws/closed), the empty close (1005, empty response), 5000\n;;              (1002 both ways), a non-reading peer (1006 at the overridden\n;;              deadline);\n;;   shutdown   C7: (quit) through the real owner loop (main/run-owner!) with\n;;              two acknowledged jolt REPL peers on a second instance, a\n;;              non-reading peer holding pending bytes and a continuously\n;;              readable peer: :stopped before the unconfirmed verdict, 4000 at\n;;              both peers, the non-reading peer shut within the unbind grace,\n;;              the registry empty before close-host!, drained/forced per\n;;              connection, :unbind-closed 0, fewer rounds than stop-ticks\n;;              and no timeout text; the same gate with a peer readable at\n;;              every poll (R17), which receives 4000 from the composition;\n;;              the 1001 slot exists only when no upgraded connection remains;\n;;              then a\n;;              one-tick budget: forced, and close-host! leaves nothing;\n;;   isolation  C8: two instances, each a listener and a dial, interleaved;\n;;              no cross-talk; close-host! on one leaves the other serving;\n;;   driver     C9: driver/sleep-fds! folds the deadline: an empty registry\n;;              waits the cadence, a 50 ms deadline under a 1000 ms cadence\n;;              wakes at about 50 ms, a past deadline still polls and hands a\n;;              ready fd and the expiry to one pump!; a --headless --port\n;;              child process answers a connected peer (R11);\n;;   fairness   C10: a readable connection plus runnable REPL work: the step\n;;              and the delivered-frame counts both advance every round.\n;;\n;; The adapter sections run under the native-memory ledger of the J6d probe\n;; (jolt.ffi alloc, string->ptr and free wrapped) and end with every instance's\n;; registry and buffers empty. The REPL-composing sections (shutdown, driver's\n;; child-process leg, fairness) check their instances' registries instead.\n;; The scripted transfer seam is dao.stream.ws.tcp's single-transfer vars.\n;;\n;; Run: bb probe:jolt-ws (all sections), or under jolt directly:\n;;   jolt -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_ws_probe.clj <section>\n;; Prints PASS/FAIL per gate and RECORD per observation; exits nonzero on any\n;; FAIL.\n(ns jolt-ws-probe\n  (:require [jolt.ffi :as ffi]\n            [jolt.io-poller :as poller]\n            [jolt.socket.native :as native]))\n\n\n(require '[clojure.string :as str]\n         '[dao.host.text :as text]\n         '[dao.stream :as stream]\n         '[dao.stream.cbor :as cbor]\n         '[dao.stream.codec :as codec]\n         '[dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n         '[dao.stream.waitset.driver :as wake]\n         '[dao.stream.ws :as ws]\n         '[dao.stream.ws.crypto :as crypto]\n         '[dao.stream.ws.jolt :as wsj]\norchestrator-logs/1793176338-jolt-yang-php-yang-typescript-orchestration.md:110:Done this seat: J4 closed (23fa701f, archived); J6a landed (a99edbca, 7a4b958c); J6 plan v3 + v3.1 ADOPTED (fable, sol ADOPT); J5 reopened (sol 4 P1s; fable ruling: in-parser guards, iterative walkers, 16 MiB thread) -> J5b; P4 S5 fix rounds 1-5; 17.3 ruling (oracle harness bug, not design row 22); 186 old prompts/findings archived (ffea556a), design docs cite collab/ paths; routing: claude implements/architects, codex gpt-6.1-sol reviews only.\norchestrator-logs/1793358019-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-jolt-seat-retake.md:57:  testee seam and every pump interface plan v3 promises exist on the J6e\n M src/dev/jolt_workload_w.clj\n M src/dev/jolt_workload_w_run.clj\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
