{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\(defn.*(publish|material|build|open|transact)|\"'^'\"\\\\(def.*(publish|material|build)' src/cljc/dao/space/{transactor,index}.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/transactor.cljc | sed -n '40,130p'; rg -n 'publish-index|defn.*publish|sort|build-index|index-snapshot' src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc | tail -35; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc | sed -n '236,260p'; rg -n 'fairness|repl-step' src/dev/jolt_ws_probe.clj | tail -15\"","aggregated_output":"src/cljc/dao/space/transactor.cljc:231:(defn transact!\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/transactor.cljc:271:(defn publish!\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:368:(defn published-index\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:564:(defn publish-index!\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:1142:(defn publish!\n    40\t   Operational outcomes are data; argument defects keep throwing. The\n    41\t   watermark advances if and only if the local append answered\n    42\t   :dao.stream/ok, so retrying the identical call re-attempts the identical\n    43\t   t. publish! builds the covered indexes over the local stream and\n    44\t   enqueues them into the intake pool (dao.space.index/publish-index!).\n    45\t   Publication is explicit and acknowledges enqueuing only, never observer\n    46\t   materialization.\n    47\t\n    48\t   Closing is per value: it rejects further appends/transacts with\n    49\t   {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed} but neither closes nor erases\n    50\t   the local stream or the intake pool.\"\n    51\t  (:require [dao.datom :as datom]\n    52\t            [dao.space.index :as index]\n    53\t            [dao.stream :as stream]))\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\t(defn- entity->datoms\n    57\t  \"One datom per k/v pair, all sharing transaction time `t`. `:db/id` is\n    58\t   required: a durable log cannot mint per-batch tempids without colliding\n    59\t   across appends. Attribute order within one entity's own datoms is\n    60\t   whatever the host's map iteration yields — unspecified across platforms.\"\n    61\t  [m t]\n    62\t  (when-not (contains? m :db/id)\n    63\t    (throw (ex-info \"entity map requires :db/id\" {:entity m})))\n    64\t  (let [e (:db/id m)]\n    65\t    (mapv (fn [[a v]]\n    66\t            (let [d [e a v t datom/default-op]]\n    67\t              (when-not (datom/local-datom? d)\n    68\t                (throw (ex-info \"invalid persistent local datom\"\n    69\t                                {:datom d, :entity m})))\n    70\t              d))\n    71\t          (remove (fn [[a _v]] (= a :db/id)) m))))\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t(defn- pad-datom\n    75\t  \"Pad [e a v] / [e a v t m] to the canonical 5-tuple. The transactor owns\n    76\t   transaction time: a non-nil explicit t is rejected, a nil t is stamped\n    77\t   with the allocated `t`. A nil m takes the default assertion op; an\n    78\t   explicit m (0, a retraction) is preserved.\"\n    79\t  [d t]\n    80\t  (let [[e a v dt dm] d]\n    81\t    (when-not (nil? dt)\n    82\t      (throw\n    83\t        (ex-info\n    84\t          \"the transactor owns transaction time: explicit datom t is rejected\"\n    85\t          {:datom d})))\n    86\t    (let [padded [e a v t (if (nil? dm) datom/default-op dm)]]\n    87\t      (when-not (datom/local-datom? padded)\n    88\t        (throw (ex-info \"invalid persistent local datom\"\n    89\t                        {:datom padded, :input d})))\n    90\t      padded)))\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\t(defn- val->datoms\n    94\t  [val t]\n    95\t  (cond\n    96\t    (map? val) (entity->datoms val t)\n    97\t    (and (vector? val) (<= 3 (count val) 5)) [(pad-datom val t)]\n    98\t    :else\n    99\t    (throw\n   100\t      (ex-info\n   101\t        \"a value must be an entity map or datom vector [e a v] / [e a v nil m]\"\n   102\t        {:val val}))))\n   103\t\n   104\t\n   105\t#_{:clj-kondo/ignore [:unused-binding]}\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\t(defn- with-write-lock\n   109\t  \"Serialize timestamp allocation and append on hosts with shared-memory\n   110\t   threads. ClojureScript and ClojureDart calls are synchronous within one\n   111\t   isolate, so the direct call has the same single-writer semantics.\"\n   112\t  [lock f]\n   113\t  #?(:clj (locking lock (f))\n   114\t     :default (f)))\n   115\t\n   116\t\n   117\t(defn- derive-next-t\n   118\t  \"Derive the next transaction time from a flattened retained history: 0 for\n   119\t   an empty history, else 1 + the maximum datom t. A datom t that is not a\n   120\t   non-negative integer is a malformed history and throws — this scan is the\n   121\t   causality boundary of the value.\"\n   122\t  [datoms]\n   123\t  (if (empty? datoms)\n   124\t    0\n   125\t    (let [ts (mapv index/datom-t datoms)]\n   126\t      (when-not (every? #(and (integer? %) (<= 0 %)) ts)\n   127\t        (throw\n   128\t          (ex-info\n   129\t            \"malformed retained history: datom t must be a non-negative integer\"\n   130\t            {:history datoms})))\n10:     - `publish-index!` snapshots the agent's local stream, builds the four\n21:     - the sort orders (`eavt-cmp`/`aevt-cmp`/`avet-cmp`/`vaet-cmp` over\n60:   carriers are not host numbers, and must sort among numbers by value.\"\n114:;; Datom slots and sort orders\n202:  \"VAET sort: v, a, e, t, m. Reverse-reference lookup — 'which datoms\n223:(defn- sorted-index-by\n225:  (bt/sorted-set-by cmp))\n233:  [sorted-set cmp sentinel]\n234:  (bt/slice sorted-set sentinel nil cmp))\n238:  \"Build {:eavt ... :aevt ... :avet ... :vaet ...} sorted indexes from a\n241:  {:eavt (into (sorted-index-by eavt-cmp) datoms),\n242:   :aevt (into (sorted-index-by aevt-cmp) datoms),\n243:   :avet (into (sorted-index-by avet-cmp) datoms),\n244:   :vaet (into (sorted-index-by vaet-cmp) datoms)})\n250:;; publish-index! stores the four covered indexes as immutable,\n368:(defn published-index\n407:;; publish-index! — build, record, append\n523:             \"publish-index! :branching-factor must be an integer of at least 2\"\n533:        \"publish-index! intake-pool must be a collection of writable dao.stream values\"\n536:    (throw (ex-info \"publish-index! intake-pool must be non-empty\"\n540:             \"publish-index! :select-stream must be a function of the pool\"\n546:          \"publish-index! :select-stream returned a value outside the intake pool\"\n558:      (throw (ex-info (str \"publish-index! stream append failed: \"\n564:(defn publish-index!\n593:     (publish-index! local-stream intake-pool)\n594:     (publish-index! local-stream intake-pool\n600:  ([local-stream intake-pool] (publish-index! local-stream intake-pool nil))\n1142:(defn publish!\n   236\t(defn- open-publication\n   237\t  \"The round's transactor and the `dao.jing` pool observer over its intake.\n   238\t   `transactor/create!` derives the next `t` from `:local`'s retained\n   239\t   history, so transaction time continues across rounds.  The intake is\n   240\t   complete-retention: `publish-index!` appends every node blob before the\n   241\t   manifest and the round drains only after it returns, so an evicting\n   242\t   intake would lose the head of any publication larger than its capacity\n   243\t   and that publication could never complete.\"\n   244\t  [ix]\n   245\t  (if (:publication ix)\n   246\t    ix\n   247\t    (let [intake (memory-log)]\n   248\t      (assoc ix\n   249\t             :publication\n   250\t             {:transactor (transactor/create! {:local-stream (:local ix)\n   251\t                                               :intake-pool [intake]\n   252\t                                               :name \"yin.repl.index\"})\n   253\t              :pool (jing/observer-state\n   254\t                      [{:stream intake\n   255\t                        :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n   256\t                                  (stream/cursor intake\n   257\t                                                 :dao.stream/oldest))}])}))))\n   258\t\n   259\t\n   260\t(defn- write-rows\n52:;;   fairness   C10: a readable connection plus runnable REPL work: the step\n58:;; child-process leg, fairness) check their instances' registries instead.\n1225:;; fairness (C10)\n1228:(defn- section-fairness\n1492:   \"fairness\" section-fairness})\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
