{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"agent_message","text":"The harness edits are in place and pass `cljstyle`. Trace mode now reports the active phase and round to the independent watchdog, including nested code-index and AST-index calls. It cannot report a qualifying PASS.\n\nI’m writing the findings with a clear distinction: synchronous owner work can stop both peers despite fair pump rotation, and repeated full-history index publication is a concrete growing cost. The exact hot subcall in attempts 18 and 21 still needs runtime evidence, which the new trace is designed to capture.\n"}}
